@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix vann: <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow> ;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "logic" ;
    vann:preferredNamespaceUri "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/" ;
    rdfs:comment "Foundation vocabulary for GMEOW Logic. The logic: namespace <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> is the canonical reasoning surface; its terms are declared standalone (no gUFO stereotypes, no rdfs:subClassOf into gmeow: reasoned classes) so the gUFO projection can be generated from them rather than the reverse. The rules, solver, profile machinery, and conformance corpus are minted as the native engine lands; this module mints the term surface."@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "GMEOW Logic"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The GMEOW Logic module — home of the `logic:` reasoning vocabulary. It declares the canonical UFO⁺ foundation (the foundational sorts and relations authored in `logic:`, of which gUFO is a generated down-projection), the semantic profiles every rule set must declare, the world/modal terms, the four distinct quantitative axes (probability, confidence, weight, evidence), and the preservation-polarity vocabulary of the loss ledger. The `logic:` namespace is the canonical foundation; OWL, Datalog, SHACL, Prolog, N3, and the gUFO/BFO/DOLCE upper ontologies are its generated lossy projections (Principle 17). `logic:` terms are STANDALONE: they carry no gUFO parentage, because gUFO is a projection of `logic:`, not its ground. The normative semantics are in `design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md`; the preservation contract is in `design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md`."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxConfigBox ,
        gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:AbstractIndividual
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Abstract Individual"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An individual that exists outside spacetime and bears no qualities — a number, a set, a value structure — neither enduring nor perduring nor inhering. The counterpart of gufo:AbstractIndividual; the abstract sibling of the concrete (endurant/perdurant) individuals. Quality values live here (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:AbstractIndividualType
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Abstract Individual Type"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A logic:Type whose instances are logic:AbstractIndividuals — the type whose extension (via logic:instanceOf) is drawn from individuals outside spacetime (numbers, sets, logic:QualityValues). The counterpart of gufo:AbstractIndividualType. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:ConcreteIndividualType, whose instances are located in spacetime."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:ActionSchema
    a owl:Class ,
        owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:NodeKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Action Schema"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A named precondition / effect / invariant template that a transaction program may invoke: the reusable unit of state change. Distinct from the concrete transaction program that instantiates it, so a reusable schema is never conflated with a single state-changing run. Punned (OWL 2 DL metamodelling): it is simultaneously the IR node kind AND the class whose instances are specific reusable action schemas — an action occurrence is a gmeow:Event that instantiates one such schema through logic:instantiatesSchema. The structure means–end reasoning reads is declared on a schema by the eight action-theory facets: logic:precondition, logic:effect, logic:invariant, logic:capability, logic:nondeterministicOutcome, logic:observation, logic:compensation, and logic:actionResource."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Admissible Valuation Policy"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The facet value class of the admissible-valuation (gap/glut) policy: which of the four Belnap values a valuation is ALLOWED to assign. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. Forbidding the gap, the glut, or both carves the classic sub-logics out of the same logic:BelnapBilattice algebra — it is a FORMAL ERROR to reduce the FDE↔LP difference to the designated-value set, because the two differ precisely in this admissible-valuation set, not in their designated values."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:AdmitAllFour
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Admit All Four"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The admissible-valuation policy that permits all four Belnap values — true, false, both (glut), and neither (gap). It carves out First-Degree Entailment (FDE): a valuation may leave an atom under-determined (gap) or over-determined (glut). Reducing the FDE↔LP difference to the designated-value set is a formal error — FDE differs from LP by admitting the gap, not by its designated values."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:AgencyAssessment
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Agency Assessment"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The canonical relational construct of holonic agency: a four-valued assessment of whether a holon exhibits Koestler's two co-equal Janus tendencies — self-assertive (autonomy, as a whole) and integrative (subordination, as a part) — always made relative to a declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile. Holon integrity is assessed, never asserted — the assessment is reified with the role properties logic:agencyHolon and logic:agencyProfile, and the engine derives its logic:agencyVerdict (logic:HolonIntegral, logic:AutonomyDeficient, logic:IntegrationDeficient, or logic:AgencyUnknown). The two pathologies are the collapse of one tendency: a 'part' with no autonomy (logic:AutonomyDeficient) and a 'whole' that refuses to integrate (logic:IntegrationDeficient); integrity is both present, and neither face is privileged over the other (Principle 9). The convenient unary reading 'this holon is integral' is the lossy projection of this assessment, exactly as logic:Holon projects logic:HolonicPosition and logic:EmergenceAssessment carries emergence (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:AgencyUnknown
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:AgencyVerdict ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Agency Unknown"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The agency-verdict value when neither Janus tendency is evidenced: under the declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile, the assessed holon bears neither an logic:selfAssertiveBasis value nor an logic:integrativeBasis value, so neither the self-assertive nor the integrative marker can fire and the integrity question has no positive footing. This subsumes the 'cannot pose the question' case: it fires both when the holon bears no basis value and when the profile declares no basis at all (no marker can derive). The first-class fourth value, kept distinct from the two pathologies so that a holon evidencing neither tendency is never silently read as a deficiency of one — failure-to-evidence is not integrity, and a basis-free profile is unknown, not deficient. Mirrors logic:EmergenceUnknown and logic:ConstraintUnknown (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:AgencyVerdict
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Agency Verdict"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed class of holonic-agency outcomes: the four-valued result an logic:AgencyAssessment receives via logic:agencyVerdict. Its four named individuals are logic:HolonIntegral (both Janus tendencies present), logic:AutonomyDeficient (a 'part' with no autonomy), logic:IntegrationDeficient (a 'whole' refusing to integrate), and logic:AgencyUnknown (neither tendency evidenced, so the integrity question has no positive footing). The set is closed, so a misspelt verdict names no declared value and is rejected rather than silently accepted, mirroring logic:EmergenceVerdict and logic:ConstraintVerdict (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Aggregate
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:EmergenceVerdict ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Aggregate"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The emergence-verdict value for a part-reducible whole property: under the declared logic:ReductionTheory of an logic:EmergenceAssessment, the whole's property is reconstructible from its proper parts — the theory carries the property in its logic:reductionBasis and a proper part also bears it (logic:bearsProperty) — so the property is a mere aggregate, a sum or closure over parts, not an emergent one. The positive, derivation-grounded verdict, reached by an actual part-reconstruction rather than by negation; contrast logic:Emergent (not part-reducible under the theory) and logic:EmergenceUnknown (the reducibility question cannot be posed) (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:AntiRigidType
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Anti-Rigid Type"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A logic:Type that applies contingently to EVERY one of its instances — for each instance there is a world of existence in which it lacks the type (the anti-rigidity witness; logic:rigidlyAppliesTo holds for none of its instances). The counterpart of gufo:AntiRigidType; the meta-type whose instances are the anti-rigid sorts: logic:Phase and logic:Role (each a logic:AntiRigidType and a logic:Sortal), logic:RoleMixin and logic:PhaseMixin (each a logic:AntiRigidType and a logic:NonSortal). Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. The discipline that anti-rigid instantiation owes a witness is logic:dischargeObligation. Contrast logic:RigidType."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:ArgumentationSemantics
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Argumentation Semantics"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The facet value class of the argumentation facet: how conflicts among defeasible arguments are resolved. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. Its individuals range from no argumentation through the grounded and preferred Dung semantics to a policy-specific resolution."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:Argument , gmeow:Attack , gmeow:Support .

logic:Aspect
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Aspect"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A moment (trope): an endurant that exists only by inhering in a bearer on which it existentially depends — a colour, a belief, a marriage's commitment. The counterpart of gufo:Aspect, covering its intrinsic/extrinsic split (gufo:IntrinsicAspect inheres in a single bearer, gufo:ExtrinsicAspect depends on several): logic: carries that distinction on the inherence/dependence relation rather than as separate classes. The dependent counterpart of logic:Substantial. Qualities and modes are aspects (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:AutonomyDeficient
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:AgencyVerdict ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Autonomy Deficient"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The agency-verdict value for the first Koestlerian pathology — a 'part' with no autonomy: under the declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile, the holon bears an logic:integrativeBasis value (it subordinates as a part) but bears no logic:selfAssertiveBasis value, so its self-assertive (autonomy-as-a-whole) face has collapsed. Reached by negation-as-failure over the self-assertive marker while the integrative marker holds, so the verdict is profile-relative, never a bare default. The co-equal counterpart of logic:IntegrationDeficient (the opposite collapse); contrast logic:HolonIntegral (both faces) and logic:AgencyUnknown (neither evidenced) (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:BelnapBilattice
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:TruthAlgebra ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Belnap Bilattice"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The four-valued Belnap truth algebra with the values true, false, both (over-determined / glut) and neither (under-determined / gap). The richest truth algebra a ReasoningContract may select; the classic sub-logics (FDE, LP, K3, classical) are carved out of this same algebra by the admissible-valuation policy and the designated-value set, which vary independently of the algebra."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:BudgetBoundedResource
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ResourcePolicy ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Budget-Bounded Resource"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The resource execution policy that runs under a declared resource budget or bound: on exhaustion the engine returns a budget-exhausted, incomplete result — sound but incomplete — and never a false answer. The bounded counterpart of logic:CertifiedFragmentResource; a contract may carry both, since resource is an execution policy holding several independent properties together rather than a single complete-vs-bounded toggle."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Builtin
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Builtin"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A native computational primitive usable in rule bodies under logic:ProceduralPrologProfile: the registry entry for a derivational builtin such as string concatenation, date arithmetic, or basic math (criticism 8, LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md §OWL 2 criticisms). Builtins are the lightweight derivations a foundation genuinely needs (Principle 12, in-logic); heavy domain computation — geo/datum transforms, relation-algebra composition, vector operations — stays external by reference. The registry is declared here; builtin execution is seamed to the compiler/engine."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:CanonicalProjection
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ProjectionTarget ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Canonical Projection"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The projection-target value requesting the answer be rendered in the canonical logic: surface — the orthogonal, lossless form GMEOW reasons over, before any down-projection. The default output request; it never alters which entailments hold."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Category
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Category"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A rigid non-sortal that classifies instances of several different Kinds by shared essential properties without itself supplying a principle of identity: it dispersively spans Kinds rather than carrying its own identity criterion. Rigid but identity-dispersive; the rigid counterpart of the anti-rigid RoleMixin and PhaseMixin."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:CertifiedFragmentResource
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ResourcePolicy ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Certified-Fragment Resource"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The resource execution policy that requires the rule set to lie within a certified-complete, terminating fragment: it guarantees hard termination and a complexity bound, and the result reports complete-for-fragment. The certified counterpart of logic:BudgetBoundedResource; because resource is an execution policy holding independent properties together, a contract may require both a certified fragment and a budget at once."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ClassicalModelSemantics
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ModelSemantics ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Classical Model Semantics"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The model-semantics facet value selecting classical first-order entailment: truth in every model. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; contrast the least-model, well-founded, and stable-model values that select a distinguished model or model set for rule programs."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ClassicalTwoValued
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:TruthAlgebra ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Classical Two-Valued"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The two-valued truth algebra with only true and false. The degenerate truth algebra a ReasoningContract selects when neither gluts nor gaps are needed; equivalent to selecting the Belnap algebra with logic:ForbidGapAndGlut, offered as a direct value for the common classical case."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Closed
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:OccurrentBoundary ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Closed"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The occurrent-boundary value for a completed unitary event: a perdurant whole over a closed temporal interval, finished and no longer able to change — the arrival, the run completed, the executed record. The event half of the YAMATO/Galton action(open)/event(closed) distinction; a Closed occurrent that bears a time-varying logic:Fluent is the logic:OccurrentChangeAsymmetry violation, since a completed whole cannot vary. Contrast logic:Open."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ClosedWorldClosure
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ClosureValue ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Closed-World Closure"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed-world value of the closure map: for the predicate or context key it is bound to, the materialized extension is complete and absence may be read as falsity. Realized within a logic:WorldBoundary by the built-in SHACL (the CWA lane); it is the per-key value of the closure map, never a global flag — open-world is the default for unlisted keys."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ClosureEntry
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Closure Entry"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A reified entry of the Closure facet map: it binds a predicate or context key (logic:closureKey) to an open- or closed-world value (logic:closureValue). The Closure facet is a map, not a global flag; WorldBoundary-scoped closed-world is the per-key value, open-world the default for unlisted keys."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:ClosureValue
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Closure Value"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The facet value class of a single closure setting — open-world or closed-world. It is the per-key value of the closure map (carried as the map default via logic:defaultClosure or as the value of a logic:ClosureEntry), not the closure facet itself, which is a map keyed by predicate or context."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Collection
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Collection"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A plurality individuated by its members, where the members are themselves the relevant units of the whole — a deck of cards, a committee, a playlist. The counterpart of gufo:Collection; members relate to it via logic:memberOf rather than logic:properPartOf. Contrast logic:Quantity, which is individuated by constitution rather than by member count."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:CommonLogicProjection
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ProjectionTarget ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Common Logic Projection"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The projection-target value requesting the answer be rendered to the ISO Common Logic surface. One of several output targets a single contract may name at once; like every projection target it is a rendering request and never alters which entailments hold."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ComparativeRelationshipType
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Comparative Relationship Type"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A logic:RelationshipType whose instances are comparative relations grounded directly in the qualities of their relata, with NO mediating relator (heavier-than, older-than, the same colour as). The counterpart of gufo:ComparativeRelationshipType; the relation holds in virtue of the relata's logic:Quality values standing in an ordering within a logic:QualitySpace, not in virtue of any logic:Relator. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:MaterialRelationshipType, which is relator-founded."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:CompatibilityRule
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Compatibility Rule"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A single local rule of the reasoning-contract feature model (constraint graph): it states that two facet values require each other, exclude each other, or together demand a particular resource value or decidability class. The supported-contract set is computed from these rules — a contract is supported iff it violates none. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust) and projected here as documentation; the projection is lossy (Principle 17)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:CompleteOverApproximation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PreservationKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Complete Over-Approximation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The projection may overgenerate but does not miss canonical answers: complete but possibly unsound. Every canonical answer appears, alongside possible spurious ones; the dual of logic:SoundUnderApproximation."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ConcreteIndividual
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Concrete Individual"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A logic:Individual located in spacetime — an endurant or a perdurant, something that bears qualities and stands in causal relations. The counterpart of gufo:ConcreteIndividual; the concrete sibling that complements logic:AbstractIndividual within logic:Individual. Every logic:Endurant and every logic:Perdurant is a logic:ConcreteIndividual (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge); it is the instance-level counterpart of logic:ConcreteIndividualType."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:ConcreteIndividualType
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Concrete Individual Type"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A logic:Type whose instances are logic:ConcreteIndividuals — the type whose extension (via logic:instanceOf) is drawn from individuals located in spacetime (endurants and perdurants). The counterpart of gufo:ConcreteIndividualType; the umbrella over logic:EndurantType together with the type-of-perdurants. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:AbstractIndividualType."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Constraint
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:NodeKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An integrity condition whose violation is a finding, not a derivation: the node kind for a condition that detects bad data rather than producing new facts. Kept distinct from logic:DerivationRule so a check is never mistaken for a productive rule."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ConstraintBinding
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ConstraintVerdict ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Constraint Binding"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The constraint-verdict value for a downward constraint that holds upon its target: under the declared logic:GovernanceRegime of a logic:DownwardConstraint, the named target is a proper part of the governing whole and the regime activates the constrained state (logic:activationBasis), and no declared override is borne by the target — so the whole's constraint binds the part. The verdict is strictly regime-relative: it is reached by negation-as-failure over the override derivation while the assessment still binds a declared regime, never as a bare 'unconstrained' default, and a different or stronger logic:GovernanceRegime may activate or quiet the same state under another constraint without contradiction. This is downward constraint, not material causation — the whole limits the part's permissible role/state, it does not produce the part. Contrast logic:ConstraintOverridden and logic:ConstraintUnknown (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ConstraintOverridden
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ConstraintVerdict ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Constraint Overridden"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The constraint-verdict value for a downward constraint defeated by a declared exception: the logic:DownwardConstraint names an override (logic:constraintOverride) and the constrained target bears that override token (logic:bearsProperty), so the whole's constraint does not bind the part. The positive, derivation-grounded verdict, reached by an actual override-match rather than by negation; it settles before logic:ConstraintBinding so that an overridden constraint is never read as binding. Constraint, not causation: the override quiets a governing limit, it does not unmake a part. Contrast logic:ConstraintBinding (active and not overridden) and logic:ConstraintUnknown (no regime activates the state) (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ConstraintUnknown
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ConstraintVerdict ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Constraint Unknown"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The constraint-verdict value when the binding question cannot be posed: the logic:DownwardConstraint names a target that is a proper part of the governing whole, but no declared logic:GovernanceRegime activates the constrained state (no logic:constraintRegime, or the regime's logic:activationBasis does not carry the state), and no override is borne — so neither a binding (logic:ConstraintBinding) nor an override-defeat (logic:ConstraintOverridden) can be derived. The first-class third value, kept distinct from the other two so that an un-activated constraint is never silently read as binding — failure-to-activate is not constraint, and a regime-free constraint is unknown, not binding (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ConstraintVerdict
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Constraint Verdict"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed class of downward-constraint outcomes: the tri-valued result a logic:DownwardConstraint receives via logic:constraintVerdict. Its three named individuals are logic:ConstraintBinding (the whole's constraint holds upon the part under the declared regime), logic:ConstraintOverridden (a declared exception defeats it), and logic:ConstraintUnknown (no regime activates the constrained state). The set is closed, so a misspelt verdict names no declared value and is rejected rather than silently accepted, mirroring logic:EmergenceVerdict and logic:MereologyConstraint (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:ContextAxis
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Context Axis"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The facet value class of one index axis of the multi-dimensional context facet. Context is multi-dimensional: a single result may be indexed simultaneously by world, standpoint, time, and path. Each logic:ContextAxis individual names one such axis; they coexist on one result rather than being alternative values of one slot."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Correspondence
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:NodeKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Correspondence"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A law-bearing, possibly-lossy, possibly-bidirectional alignment between a source pattern and a target pattern: the ninth node kind. It carries its morphism class on an ordered law-spine, its claimed laws with discharge status, the separated quantitative axes, FOL/SOL caveats, and standpoint indexing; its get and put legs are transaction programs while its caveat-and-relation envelope is meta-level and stays meta. It is the single kind cross-ontology alignment compiles into, and from which the SSSOM, EDOAL, FnO, SPARQL, and up-lift surfaces are generated lowerings. Fully specified in design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:DatalogFragment
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormulaFragment ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Datalog Fragment"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The formula-fragment facet value selecting the function-free, range-restricted Datalog class of formulae. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; the decidable, terminating fragment more restrictive than logic:HornFragment (no function symbols) and the projection target for which least-model semantics is PTIME-data."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:DatalogProjection
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ProjectionTarget ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Datalog Projection"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The projection-target value requesting the answer be rendered to a Datalog surface. One of several output targets a single contract may name at once; like every projection target it is a rendering request and never alters which entailments hold."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:DefaultNegation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:NegationOperator ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Default Negation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The negation-as-failure operator: a body literal that holds when its atom is not derivable. One member of the negation-operator set facet (which may also include logic:ExplicitNegation); a program using it requires at least the stratified-negation reading of the model-semantics facet rather than positive-Horn least-model semantics."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:DependencyModel
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Dependency Model"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:subClassOf logic:ProbabilityModel ;
    skos:definition "A probability model carrying an EXPLICIT joint distribution over a correlated set of logic:probability facts: where logic:FullIndependence factorizes as a product, a dependency model substitutes a declared joint table (logic:correlates names the correlated facts; logic:jointOutcome enumerates the joint outcomes with their logic:jointProbability). Facts outside the correlated set remain independent and factorize as usual. The declared joint outcomes must be exhaustive and sum to one."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:DerivationRule
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:NodeKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Derivation Rule"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A head entailed from a body: the productive subset of the IR, where satisfying the antecedents derives the consequent. Distinct from logic:Constraint, whose violation is reported as a finding rather than producing new assertions."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:DesignateTrueAndBoth
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:DesignatedValueSet ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Designate True And Both"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The designated-value set that counts both true and both (the glut) as designated — i.e. as holding for the purpose of consequence. The designated set shared by FDE and LP in their standard presentations; what distinguishes FDE from LP is the admissible-valuation policy, not this designated set, so it is a formal error to attribute the FDE↔LP difference to the designated values."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:DesignateTrueOnly
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:DesignatedValueSet ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Designate True Only"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The designated-value set that counts only true as designated. The designated set of K3 and classical logic; combined with the admissible-valuation policy and truth algebra it fixes which logic a contract selects, the three components varying independently."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:DesignatedValueSet
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Designated Value Set"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The facet value class of the designated-value set: which truth values count as designated (as holding) for the purpose of consequence. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. It is one of the three independent components — truth algebra, admissible-valuation policy, designated values — that together separate FDE, LP, K3 and classical logic; collapsing any two of them erases exactly the choices that distinguish those logics."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Discipline
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Discipline"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A named OntoUML structural discipline a class can violate: the closed vocabulary of anti-patterns the foundation lowering checks (stereotype cardinality, identity overlap, free role, mixed rigidity, relator completeness). Its named individuals are the labels a logic:violation fact points at; the set is closed so a misspelt label names no declared discipline and is rejected rather than silently accepted."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Disposition
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Disposition"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A bearer-held tendency, power, or liability to manifest events of a characteristic type when triggered — a fragility, a solubility, a hazard's potential to harm — which remains fully real even while it never manifests. gUFO has no Disposition class and models such tendencies as a gufo:IntrinsicMode; logic: subsumes that by carrying the disposition as first-class, so an unmanifested tendency needs no counterfactual reification. A logic:Mode whose manifestations are logic:Events of the characteristic type (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge); the bearer relation is asserted with a domain property (Principle 5), never gufo:inheresIn."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:DownwardConstraint
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Downward Constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The canonical relational construct of holonic governance: the downward (governing) face of a holon, a typed directed constraint a whole imposes on a named proper part — the whole limits which roles or states the part may take. This is downward CONSTRAINT, never material causation: the governing whole bounds the part's permissible state, it does not produce or compose the part. Reified with the role properties logic:constraintWhole, logic:constraintTarget, logic:constraintState, logic:constraintRegime, and logic:constraintOverride, and the engine derives its logic:constraintVerdict (logic:ConstraintBinding, logic:ConstraintOverridden, or logic:ConstraintUnknown). The constraint is structured and NON-TRANSITIVE by default (ME9): it applies to the explicitly named target and says nothing automatic about the target's own proper parts — there is no rule cascading the constraint down logic:properPartOf, exactly as no rule propagates logic:bearsProperty down it (mirroring logic:EmergenceAssessment / logic:HolonicPosition; design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:EmergenceAssessment
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Emergence Assessment"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The canonical relational construct of emergence: a tri-valued assessment of whether a whole's property is reducible to its proper parts, always made relative to a declared logic:ReductionTheory. Emergence is assessed, never asserted — the assessment is reified with the role properties logic:assessmentWhole, logic:assessmentProperty, and logic:assessmentReductionTheory, and the engine derives its logic:assessmentVerdict (logic:Aggregate, logic:Emergent, or logic:EmergenceUnknown). Failure to derive a property from the parts under one theory is not proof of irreducibility: because the assessment records the theory it is relative to, a later, stronger theory can overturn an logic:Emergent verdict without contradiction. The convenient unary reading 'P is emergent' is the lossy projection of this assessment, exactly as logic:Holon projects logic:HolonicPosition (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:EmergenceUnknown
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:EmergenceVerdict ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Emergence Unknown"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The emergence-verdict value when the reducibility question cannot be posed: the whole bears the property under assessment, but the logic:EmergenceAssessment declares no logic:ReductionTheory (no logic:assessmentReductionTheory), so neither a part-reconstruction (logic:Aggregate) nor a theory-relative non-reduction (logic:Emergent) can be derived. ME9's first-class third value, kept distinct from logic:Aggregate and logic:Emergent so that a genuinely unclassifiable assessment is never silently read as emergence — failure-to-derive is not irreducibility, and a theory-free assessment is unknown, not emergent (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:EmergenceVerdict
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Emergence Verdict"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed class of emergence-assessment outcomes: the tri-valued result an logic:EmergenceAssessment receives via logic:assessmentVerdict. Its three named individuals are logic:Aggregate (part-reducible under the declared theory), logic:Emergent (borne by the whole but not part-reducible under that theory), and logic:EmergenceUnknown (the reducibility question cannot be posed). The set is closed, so a misspelt verdict names no declared value and is rejected rather than silently accepted, mirroring logic:MereologyConstraint (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Emergent
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:EmergenceVerdict ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Emergent"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The emergence-verdict value for a genuinely emergent whole property: under the declared logic:ReductionTheory of an logic:EmergenceAssessment, the whole bears the property but it is not reconstructible from the parts — the theory does not carry it in its logic:reductionBasis, or no proper part bears it — so the property does not propagate down logic:properPartOf and is not entailed by the parts' properties. The verdict is strictly theory-relative: it is reached by negation-as-failure over the aggregate derivation, never as a bare 'unflagged' default, and failure to derive under this theory is not proof of irreducibility — a stronger logic:ReductionTheory may reduce the same property under a different assessment without contradiction. Contrast logic:Aggregate and logic:EmergenceUnknown (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Endurant
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Endurant"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A continuant: an individual that persists through time and is wholly present at each moment of its existence, enduring through change rather than unfolding through it. The counterpart of gufo:Endurant and the bearer side of the endurant/perdurant divide; contrast logic:Perdurant, which has temporal parts. Substantials and aspects are both endurants."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:EndurantType
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Endurant Type"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A logic:Type whose instances are logic:Endurants — the type whose extension (via logic:instanceOf) is drawn from continuants. The counterpart of gufo:EndurantType; the type-of-endurants branch under which the sortal and non-sortal foundation meta-types (logic:Kind, logic:Phase, logic:Role, logic:Category, …) ultimately fall. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:Event and logic:Situation, which carry gUFO's EventType/SituationType roles per the down-projection."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:EntrenchmentRevision
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:RevisionPolicy ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Entrenchment Revision"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The revision-policy value under which conflicting information is absorbed by an AGM-style belief revision driven by a declared epistemic-entrenchment ordering: the least entrenched beliefs are surrendered to restore consistency. Contrast logic:MonotonicRevision (nothing retracted) and logic:TruthMaintenanceRevision (justification-tracked retraction)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:EqualityPolicy
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Equality Policy"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The facet value class of the equality facet: when two terms are taken to denote one entity. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. Its individuals range from RDF equality through explicit (asserted) equality to an optional unique-name assumption."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Event
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Event"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A perdurant occurrence that happens in time and is composed of temporal parts: an action, a process, a happening that unfolds and is complete once it has occurred. Tokens it as an occurrence rather than an endurant; in the type-level world strata (risk, teleology, norms) the no-occurrence gate keeps reasoning over Event *types* without entailing any Event instance. Unitary: a proper temporal part of an event is not itself that event, and a completed (logic:Closed) event cannot vary — it bears no time-varying logic:Fluent (the change-asymmetry, logic:OccurrentChangeAsymmetry). An event is constituted by the process it is made of (logic:occurrentConstituent)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:EvolutionMode
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Evolution Mode"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The facet value class of the evolution facet: whether and how state changes over the course of reasoning. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. Its individuals range from the static (one-state) default through state-transition to the Transaction-Logic transaction-path semantics; evolution is independent of the model-semantics facet, which is why state-change reasoning is a facet value, never a parallel profile. Commitment — whether a program's effects are committed or discarded — is a separate orthogonal facet (logic:ExecutionMode), not a value of this one: a program may be hypothetically executed (logic:HypotheticalExecution) under any evolution mode."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:ExecutionMode
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Execution Mode"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The facet value class of the execution-commitment facet: whether a Transaction-Logic program's effects are committed or discarded. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract and ORTHOGONAL to the evolution facet — a program may be executed hypothetically under any logic:EvolutionMode, because commitment (commit vs. discard) and state-change shape are independent dimensions. Its individuals are logic:CommittedExecution (the default) and logic:HypotheticalExecution (the sandbox operator). The sandbox operator is DISTINCT from modal possibility (◇): ◇ is the standard translation over the appropriate typed accessibility relation — logic:epistemicallyPossible or logic:doxasticallyAccessible (an alethic or doxastic claim about what is possible), not over the bare logic:accessibleFrom superproperty — whereas hypothetical execution asserts a program can execute from here without committing; conflating them would let an execution sandbox masquerade as a statement about what is possible."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:CommittedExecution
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ExecutionMode ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Committed Execution"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The execution-mode value under which a transaction program's elementary updates are committed — the effects advance the path and persist. The default execution mode; contrast logic:HypotheticalExecution, which discards effects."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:HypotheticalExecution
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ExecutionMode ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Hypothetical Execution"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The execution-mode value realizing the sandbox/hypothetical operator: a transaction program is executed to test whether it WOULD succeed, with its effects discarded rather than committed. It asserts that a program can execute from here without committing, and is NOT modal possibility (◇) — ◇ is the standard translation over the appropriate typed accessibility relation, logic:epistemicallyPossible or logic:doxasticallyAccessible (an alethic or doxastic claim), not over the bare logic:accessibleFrom superproperty; the two share construction machinery but are separate typed operators with separate meanings. The sandbox operator of the Transaction-Logic design, kept apart from the alethic/doxastic possibility of the context algebra."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ExactPreservation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PreservationKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Exact Preservation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The projection yields the same answers as the canonical model for the declared query class: neither misses canonical answers nor adds spurious ones. The strongest preservation polarity, claimable only for a certified subfragment."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ExistentialRulesFragment
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormulaFragment ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Existential Rules Fragment"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The formula-fragment facet value selecting the existential-rules (tuple-generating-dependency / Datalog±) class, admitting existential quantifiers in rule heads. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; more expressive than logic:DatalogFragment (value invention) and the fragment over which acyclicity or guardedness conditions buy back decidability."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ExplicitEqualityPolicy
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:EqualityPolicy ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Explicit Equality Policy"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The equality-policy value under which two terms are one only when their identity is explicitly asserted (e.g. via owl:sameAs-style equality facts): no implicit unification beyond what is declared. Contrast logic:RdfEqualityPolicy (RDF node identity) and logic:UniqueNameEqualityPolicy (distinct names denote distinct entities)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ExplicitNegation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:NegationOperator ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Explicit Negation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The strong (explicit) negation operator: an atom is asserted false, distinct from being merely not derivable. One member of the negation-operator set facet — a program may legitimately use explicit negation and logic:DefaultNegation together — which records the permitted operator set, not a single chosen operator."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:FOLFragment
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormulaFragment ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "FOL Fragment"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The formula-fragment facet value selecting unrestricted first-order formulae. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; the most expressive (and only semi-decidable) fragment, against which the Horn, Datalog, and existential-rules values are the decidability-bought restrictions."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:FixedCollection
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Fixed Collection"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A logic:Collection with fixed membership: its members (via logic:memberOf) do not change over its existence, so gaining or losing a member yields a different collection — a specific deck of 52 cards, the founding signatories of a treaty. The counterpart of gufo:FixedCollection. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Because membership is invariant across worlds the membership relation reads rigidly; contrast logic:VariableCollection."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Fluent
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Fluent"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A value or relation indexed to time (and world): a time-varying property whose truth changes across moments — an object's location, an account's balance, a temperature reading. The native temporal-fluent construct of the four-dimensional treatment (criticism 3), pairing with Principle-11 frame-relativity so each temporal value lives in an explicit reference system rather than as a bare literal."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:ForbidGap
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Forbid Gap"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The admissible-valuation policy that forbids the neither gap while admitting the both glut — every atom is at least true or false, but may be both. It carves out the Logic of Paradox (LP). FDE and LP share the designated set true,both; LP differs from FDE by forbidding the gap, not by its designated values — reducing the FDE↔LP difference to designated values is a formal error."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ForbidGapAndGlut
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Forbid Gap And Glut"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The admissible-valuation policy that forbids both the neither gap and the both glut, leaving exactly true and false. It carves classical logic out of the Belnap algebra; combined with logic:DesignateTrueOnly it recovers ordinary two-valued entailment."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ForbidGlut
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Forbid Glut"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The admissible-valuation policy that forbids the both glut while admitting the neither gap — every atom is at most true or false, but may be neither. It carves out Strong Kleene logic (K3), the dual restriction to logic:ForbidGap; the difference between K3 and the gap-admitting logics lies in this admissible-valuation set, not in the designated values."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:FormulaFragment
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Formula Fragment"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The facet value class of the formula-fragment facet: the syntactic class of formulae a rule set is admitted from. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. Its individuals range from unrestricted first-order through Horn and Datalog to existential rules, fixing both expressivity and the decidability ceiling."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:FreeRole
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:Discipline ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Free Role"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The OntoUML FreeRole anti-pattern: an anti-rigid sortal (Role or Phase) must specialize a rigid sortal from which to inherit a principle of identity. An anti-rigid sortal with no rigid (Kind/SubKind) ancestor violates it. One half of the lowering of reasoning_lint.anti_rigidity_discipline."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:FullIndependence
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ProbabilityModel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Full Independence"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The well-known probability model under which every logic:probability fact is an independent Bernoulli variable — the ProbLog default, made explicit rather than assumed. The probability of a total choice is the product over the chosen facts of their probabilities times the product over the unchosen of their complements; a query's marginal is the sum of total-choice probabilities over the choices whose least Herbrand model derives it."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:FunctionalComplex
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Functional Complex"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A whole whose parts play distinct functional roles — a car (engine, wheels, chassis), an organism (organs), an organization (departments): a complex object, not a mere collection of like members. The counterpart of gufo:FunctionalComplex; its parts relate to it via logic:properPartOf (mereological parthood) rather than logic:memberOf, and each part contributes a different function. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:Collection (uniform members) and logic:Quantity (homogeneous stuff)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:FuzzyMeasure
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:UncertaintyMeasure ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Fuzzy Measure"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The uncertainty measure carrying fuzzy (degree-of-truth) membership values. One member of the uncertainty-measure set facet, which may carry several measures at once; distinct from logic:ProbabilisticMeasure (a calibrated probability) and logic:WeightedRankingMeasure (a solver preference order)."@x-gmeow-english .

# === Teleology layer: goal expressions, evaluation, plans, decomposition ======
# The reasoning structure over GMEOW's own teleological vocabulary (gmeow:Goal,
# gmeow:Desire/Intention/Commitment, gmeow:satisfiedBy). Classes and named
# individuals are grouped as one cohesive cluster (mirroring the ReasoningResult
# status cluster); the teleology object/datatype properties are grouped together
# in the property block below. Normative in design/LOGIC-TELEOLOGY.md.

logic:AndDecomposition
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "And-Decomposition"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The decomposition of a gmeow:Goal under which all of its necessary sub-goals must hold together for the parent to be satisfied — a conjunctive node of the and-or goal graph means–end search runs over. It groups the logic:necessaryFor sub-goals of the parent: every grouped sub-goal must be satisfied. The co-equal counterpart of logic:OrDecomposition (any one sufficient sub-goal settles the parent); the two compose into the and-or goal graph. Decomposition carries satisfaction dependency and is typed apart from the generic mereology spine — a sub-goal may be both a gmeow:properPartOf and logic:necessaryFor its parent, yet part-hood alone does not express the satisfaction dependency planning needs."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:FeasibilityStatus
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Feasibility Status"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed value class of the feasibility axis of a logic:GoalEvaluation: whether the goal is reachable from the situation it is judged against. Its individuals are logic:Feasible (a path to the goal exists), logic:Blocked (no path exists in the current situation but the obstruction may lift), logic:Infeasible (no path exists in any reachable situation), and logic:FeasibilityUnknown (the feasibility question has not been settled). The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. This axis varies independently of satisfaction, lifecycle, and goal-evaluation status — a goal may be partial in satisfaction, blocked in feasibility, and active in lifecycle at once."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Feasible
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FeasibilityStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Feasible"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:FeasibilityStatus value for a goal a path can reach from the situation it is judged against — the goal is achievable. Contrast logic:Blocked (no current path, but the obstruction may lift) and logic:Infeasible (no path in any reachable situation)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Blocked
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FeasibilityStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Blocked"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:FeasibilityStatus value for a goal with no path from the current situation, where the obstruction may yet lift — temporarily unreachable rather than permanently so. Contrast logic:Infeasible (unreachable in every reachable situation) and logic:Feasible (a path exists)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Infeasible
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FeasibilityStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Infeasible"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:FeasibilityStatus value for a goal no path can reach from any reachable situation — permanently unachievable, not merely currently obstructed. The strongest infeasibility reading; contrast logic:Blocked (the obstruction may lift)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:FeasibilityUnknown
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FeasibilityStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Feasibility Unknown"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:FeasibilityStatus value when the reachability question has not been settled — the engine has neither found a path nor proved none exists. The first-class fourth value, kept distinct from logic:Blocked so an unexamined goal is never silently read as obstructed."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:GoalEvaluation
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Goal Evaluation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The reified, vantage-indexed record of whether a goal is met: one logic:GoalEvaluation per (goal, situation or world it is judged against, evaluator holding the judgment, time of judgment, criterion applied), identified by that tuple of subjects and attributed through gmeow:accordingTo. Its outcome is factored into independent axes rather than one collapsed label — logic:satisfactionStatus, logic:feasibilityStatus, logic:lifecycleStatus, logic:goalEvaluationStatus, and the logic:satisfactionDegree quantity — each varying independently. The binary gmeow:satisfiedBy edge is the conclusive projection of this record: an edge is generated from each evaluation whose satisfaction status is logic:Satisfied and whose goal-evaluation status is logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted, and a directly authored gmeow:satisfiedBy edge deterministically expands into a default such evaluation under the asserting vantage, so the flat and reified records never disagree. Two evaluators who disagree are two coexisting evaluations, each retained rather than reconciled (Principle 9)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:GoalEvaluationStatus
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Goal Evaluation Status"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed value class of the goal-evaluation-completeness axis of a logic:GoalEvaluation: whether the evaluation has reached a conclusive judgment. Its individuals are logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted (a conclusive judgment), logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined (not yet conclusive — a maintenance or avoidance goal whose window has not closed holds so far but is not yet conclusively satisfied), and logic:GoalEvaluationUnsupported (the evaluator has no defined procedure for the judgment). The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. DISTINCT from logic:EvaluationStatus, the engine-computation axis of a logic:ReasoningResult (what the engine was able to do): the two are orthogonal and must never be conflated — one factors a goal judgment's conclusiveness, the other a reasoning run's computational completion."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:GoalEvaluationStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Goal Evaluation Completed"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:GoalEvaluationStatus value for a goal evaluation that has reached a conclusive judgment. Together with satisfaction status logic:Satisfied it is the condition under which a gmeow:satisfiedBy edge is generated. A maintenance or avoidance goal reaches this only when its window closes (satisfied) or its target fails (violated)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:GoalEvaluationStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Goal Evaluation Undetermined"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:GoalEvaluationStatus value for a goal evaluation not yet conclusive — most characteristically a maintenance or avoidance goal whose bounding window has not closed: holding so far is not conclusive satisfaction. Distinct from logic:GoalEvaluationUnsupported (no procedure exists): here the procedure exists but the judgment is open."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:GoalEvaluationUnsupported
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:GoalEvaluationStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Goal Evaluation Unsupported"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:GoalEvaluationStatus value for a goal evaluation the evaluator has no defined procedure for — the judgment cannot be made under the applicable criterion. Distinct from logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined (the procedure exists but the judgment is open)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:GoalExpression
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Goal Expression"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The typed IR term carrying the compositional structure of a goal's target so the engine can evaluate it compositionally, attached to a gmeow:Goal through logic:hasGoalCondition. Its node kind is one of nine variants: atomic (satisfied when a named situation type obtains), conjunctive and disjunctive (satisfied when all, or any, sub-expressions are), achievement (satisfied once the target first obtains along a path), maintenance (satisfied only while the target holds at every state of an interval, violated at the first failure), avoidance (the dual of maintenance — satisfied while a proscribed situation never obtains), optimization (directed at a measure, satisfied to the degree the measure is extremized rather than by a crisp boundary), conditional (a target applying only when a guard situation holds), and deadline-window (an achievement or maintenance target indexed to a bounding interval after which the window closes). Identity is STRUCTURAL: two expressions with the same node kind, operands, and bound situation type are the same term, so a goal condition is data the engine reads and writes rather than prose. The flat gmeow:hasGoal and conclusive gmeow:satisfiedBy edges are the surface views this richer form generates; projections that cannot hold the structure record the loss in the preservation ledger."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:GoalExpressionKind
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Goal Expression Kind"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed value class of the node kind of a logic:GoalExpression — which of the nine compositional variants the expression is, read by the engine to evaluate it. Its individuals are logic:AtomicGoal (a named situation type obtains), logic:ConjunctiveGoal and logic:DisjunctiveGoal (all, or any, operand sub-expressions hold), logic:AchievementGoal (the target first obtains along a path), logic:MaintenanceGoal (the target holds at every state of an interval, violated at the first failure), logic:AvoidanceGoal (the dual — a proscribed situation never obtains), logic:OptimizationGoal (directed at a measure, satisfied to a degree rather than crisply), logic:ConditionalGoal (a target applying only when a guard situation holds), and logic:DeadlineWindowGoal (an achievement or maintenance target indexed to a bounding interval after which the window closes). The set is closed; a misspelt kind names no declared variant and is rejected."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:AtomicGoal
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:GoalExpressionKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Atomic Goal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a leaf goal satisfied exactly when its logic:boundSituationType obtains at the relevant state. The base of the compositional algebra; contrast the conjunctive/disjunctive combinators and the temporal kinds."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ConjunctiveGoal
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:GoalExpressionKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Conjunctive Goal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a goal satisfied only when ALL of its logic:operand sub-expressions are satisfied. The conjunctive combinator of the goal algebra; co-equal counterpart of logic:DisjunctiveGoal."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:DisjunctiveGoal
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:GoalExpressionKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Disjunctive Goal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a goal satisfied when ANY of its logic:operand sub-expressions is satisfied. The disjunctive combinator of the goal algebra; co-equal counterpart of logic:ConjunctiveGoal."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:AchievementGoal
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:GoalExpressionKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Achievement Goal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a goal satisfied once its logic:boundSituationType FIRST obtains at any state along the logic:Path — a one-shot attainment. Contrast logic:MaintenanceGoal (must hold at every state)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:MaintenanceGoal
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:GoalExpressionKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Maintenance Goal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a goal satisfied only while its logic:boundSituationType holds at EVERY state of the interval, violated at the FIRST state it fails; while the bounding window is still open the evaluation is logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined, not conclusively satisfied. The dual of logic:AvoidanceGoal."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:AvoidanceGoal
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:GoalExpressionKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Avoidance Goal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a goal satisfied only while its proscribed logic:boundSituationType NEVER obtains across the interval, violated at the first state it obtains — the dual of logic:MaintenanceGoal. While the window is still open the evaluation is logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:OptimizationGoal
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:GoalExpressionKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Optimization Goal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a goal directed at a logic:objectiveValue read in a logic:objectiveDirection, satisfied to the DEGREE the measure is extremized (carried as logic:satisfactionDegree) rather than by a crisp boundary. Its outcome is recorded as a degree, never folded into a crisp truth value."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ConditionalGoal
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:GoalExpressionKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Conditional Goal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a goal whose target applies only when its logic:guardSituation holds; when the guard is false the goal prescribes nothing and its evaluation reflects does-not-apply rather than satisfied or violated. The single operand carries the guarded target sub-expression."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:DeadlineWindowGoal
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:GoalExpressionKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Deadline-Window Goal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for an achievement or maintenance target indexed to a bounding logic:deadlineWindow interval; the evaluation stays logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined while the window is open and becomes conclusive once it closes. The single operand carries the windowed target sub-expression."@x-gmeow-english .


logic:LifecycleStatus
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Lifecycle Status"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed value class of the lifecycle axis of a logic:GoalEvaluation: where the goal stands in its adoption history. Its individuals are logic:LifecycleActive (currently held), logic:LifecycleRetired (no longer pursued, its tenure closed), and logic:LifecycleSuperseded (replaced by another goal). The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. This axis varies independently of satisfaction and feasibility — goal revision is supersession, never erasure, so a retired or superseded goal remains an auditable closed tenure."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:LifecycleActive
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:LifecycleStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Lifecycle Active"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:LifecycleStatus value for a goal currently held and pursued — its adoption tenure open. Contrast logic:LifecycleRetired (tenure closed) and logic:LifecycleSuperseded (replaced)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:LifecycleRetired
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:LifecycleStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Lifecycle Retired"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:LifecycleStatus value for a goal no longer pursued, its adoption tenure closed by supersession rather than erased — the abandoned goal remains auditable. Contrast logic:LifecycleSuperseded, where a specific replacement goal takes its place."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:LifecycleSuperseded
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:LifecycleStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Lifecycle Superseded"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:LifecycleStatus value for a goal replaced by another — a closed tenure standing under a successor goal. Distinct from logic:LifecycleRetired (closed with no successor named)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:OrDecomposition
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Or-Decomposition"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The decomposition of a gmeow:Goal under which any one sufficient sub-goal settles the parent on its own — a disjunctive node of the and-or goal graph means–end search runs over. It groups the logic:sufficientFor sub-goals of the parent: satisfying any one settles it. The co-equal counterpart of logic:AndDecomposition (all necessary sub-goals must hold together); the two compose into the and-or goal graph. Like all decomposition it carries satisfaction dependency and is typed apart from the generic mereology spine, which carries only structural part-hood."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Plan
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Plan"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A transaction program (a logic:TransactionProgram-kind node) whose primitive operations invoke action schemas and whose success criterion is a goal expression. As a program it carries the structure a decomposed goal alone cannot — ordering and serial composition, guards, branching, concurrency, loops, and fallback — all in the operators of the transaction layer. A POLICY is a plan whose branches are conditioned on what an earlier action's observation reveals rather than fixed in advance; this is a reading of a plan, NOT a separate class. Plan adoption and revision are recorded as an intention is: a plan is held over an interval and revised by suppression, never mutated. Because an action schema may carry a nondeterministic outcome set, plan success is quantified over those outcomes through logic:planSuccessMode rather than left to the bare executional-success reading. On the foundational spine a logic:Plan is a gmeow:SocialObject (a description, not a physical thing), grounded in prose per the logic-core convention rather than by a subclass edge; a process surface that specializes logic:Plan therefore also asserts its own gmeow:SocialObject or gmeow:InformationObject sort directly, since the prose grounding licenses no DL inference of it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:PlanSuccessMode
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Plan Success Mode"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed value class of the success quantification a logic:Plan declares over the nondeterministic outcomes of its action schemas. Its individuals are logic:WeakPlanSuccess (some outcome path reaches the goal), logic:StrongPlanSuccess (every outcome path reaches it), and logic:StrongCyclicPlanSuccess (every fair execution is guaranteed to reach it in finitely many steps, allowing retried loops through recoverable failures). The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. The quantification exists because the bare executional-success reading of the transaction layer would count the mere existence of one favourable path as success."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:WeakPlanSuccess
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PlanSuccessMode ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Weak Plan Success"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:PlanSuccessMode value under which a plan succeeds when SOME outcome path reaches the goal — the existential reading. The weakest of the three; contrast logic:StrongPlanSuccess (every path) and logic:StrongCyclicPlanSuccess (every fair execution, allowing loops)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:StrongPlanSuccess
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PlanSuccessMode ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Strong Plan Success"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:PlanSuccessMode value under which a plan succeeds when EVERY outcome path reaches the goal — the universal reading, guaranteeing the goal regardless of how nondeterminism resolves. Contrast logic:WeakPlanSuccess (some path) and logic:StrongCyclicPlanSuccess (every fair execution, allowing retried loops)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:StrongCyclicPlanSuccess
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PlanSuccessMode ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Strong-Cyclic Plan Success"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:PlanSuccessMode value under which a plan succeeds when every FAIR execution is guaranteed to reach the goal in finitely many steps, allowing retried loops through recoverable failures — the reading that tolerates cyclic recovery a strong plan forbids while still guaranteeing eventual success a weak plan does not. Between logic:WeakPlanSuccess and logic:StrongPlanSuccess in strength."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:SatisfactionStatus
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Satisfaction Status"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed value class of the satisfaction axis of a logic:GoalEvaluation: to what extent the goal is met against the situation it is judged against. Its individuals are logic:Satisfied (fully met), logic:PartiallySatisfied (met in part — held apart from a low logic:confidence in a satisfied evaluation, which is a different question), logic:Violated (a maintenance or avoidance target has failed), and logic:Unsatisfied (not met, with no positive partial progress recorded). The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. Together with logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted, logic:Satisfied is the condition under which a gmeow:satisfiedBy edge is generated."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Satisfied
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:SatisfactionStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Satisfied"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:SatisfactionStatus value for a goal fully met against the situation it is judged against. Together with goal-evaluation status logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted it is the condition that generates a gmeow:satisfiedBy edge. Distinct from a high logic:confidence in a satisfied evaluation — how met is not how sure."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:PartiallySatisfied
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:SatisfactionStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Partially Satisfied"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:SatisfactionStatus value for a goal met in part, its extent carried as a logic:satisfactionDegree quantity. Held apart from a low logic:confidence in a logic:Satisfied evaluation: partial satisfaction is how much of the goal is achieved, never how sure the evaluator is. Contrast logic:Unsatisfied (no positive progress) and logic:Violated (a target has failed)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Violated
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:SatisfactionStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Violated"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:SatisfactionStatus value for a goal whose target has failed — a maintenance goal that failed at some state of its interval, or an avoidance goal whose proscribed situation obtained. Stronger than logic:Unsatisfied: a violation is an active breach, not mere non-achievement."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Unsatisfied
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:SatisfactionStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Unsatisfied"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:SatisfactionStatus value for a goal not met, with no positive partial progress recorded. Distinct from logic:Violated (an active breach of a maintenance or avoidance target) and from logic:PartiallySatisfied (some progress made)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:GovernanceRegime
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Governance Regime"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A declared scope within which a logic:DownwardConstraint is active, relative to which its logic:constraintVerdict is read. It carries, via logic:activationBasis, the constrained states it activates as binding — a constraint binds only when its constrained state is in the regime's basis. Governance is always regime-relative: the same whole may bind a part's state under one GovernanceRegime and leave it logic:ConstraintUnknown under another, and a binding can be quieted by a different regime without contradiction precisely because the constraint records which regime it is relative to. The holonic-governance analogue of a logic:ReductionTheory (which scopes the emergence calculus) and a logic:MereologyProfile (which scopes weak supplementation) — it scopes the downward-constraint calculus rather than asserting governance foundation-wide (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:GroundedArgumentation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ArgumentationSemantics ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Grounded Argumentation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The grounded Dung argumentation semantics: the unique, sceptical, least fixed point of the characteristic function — an argument is accepted only when every attack on it is defeated by an accepted argument. The argumentation-facet value that resolves conflict deterministically; contrast logic:PreferredArgumentation, which admits multiple maximal admissible sets."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:ArgumentEvaluation .

logic:Holarchy
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Holarchy"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The bounded logic:properPartOf strict partial order viewed as a nested whole/part structure — a holarchy in Koestler's sense. Because logic:properPartOf is transitive, asymmetric, and irreflexive, a holarchy is a directed acyclic graph (a DAG, not a strict ladder): an entity may be a proper part of several wholes along several paths. It is the structure over which a logic:HolonicPosition is read and logic:holonicLevel is measured (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Holon
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Holon"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The lossy unary projection of logic:HolonicPosition: an entity that, within some holarchy, is simultaneously a whole and a part — both a proper part of some larger whole and itself having a proper part. Holon-ness is never a bare property of the entity; it is a position occupied in a particular holarchy, context, interval, and path, so logic:Holon is the convenient, lossy projection of that relational logic:HolonicPosition, exactly as the standpoint-modality view projects finer axes (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section). Root wholes and atomic leaves are not holons."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:HolonIntegral
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:AgencyVerdict ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Holon Integral"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The agency-verdict value for a holon that exhibits both Janus tendencies: under the declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile of an logic:AgencyAssessment, the holon bears (logic:bearsProperty) both a logic:selfAssertiveBasis value (it asserts itself as a whole) and a logic:integrativeBasis value (it subordinates itself as a part) — Koestler's balanced holon. The positive, derivation-grounded verdict, reached by an actual two-face conjunction rather than by negation; the two faces are co-equal, neither privileged (Principle 9). Contrast logic:AutonomyDeficient and logic:IntegrationDeficient (one face collapsed) and logic:AgencyUnknown (neither evidenced) (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:HolonicAgencyProfile
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Holonic Agency Profile"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A declared profile of holonic agency that a holarchy may adopt, relative to which an logic:AgencyAssessment is made. It carries, via logic:selfAssertiveBasis and logic:integrativeBasis, the property-values that respectively evidence a holon's self-assertive (autonomy-as-a-whole) and integrative (subordination-as-a-part) tendencies — Koestler's two co-equal Janus faces, neither primary (Principle 9). Holonic agency is always relative to such a profile: it is a named profile a holarchy adopts, NOT a universal well-formedness rule every holon must satisfy — a bolt, a file-segment, or a process-phase needs no autonomy and is simply outside the profile. The Koestlerian-agency analogue of a logic:ReductionTheory (which scopes the emergence calculus) and a logic:GovernanceRegime (which scopes downward constraint) — it scopes the autonomy/integration calculus rather than asserting agency foundation-wide (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:HolonicLevelIncoherence
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:MereologyConstraint ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Holonic Level Incoherence"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The coherence violation raised for a holon — an entity that occupies a holonic position (both a proper part of some whole and itself having a proper part) — that is DECLARED UNDER a logic:MereologyProfile (via logic:underMereologyProfile) yet occupies no logic:HolonicPosition. A holon's logic:holonicLevel is read off its logic:HolonicPosition, the canonical relational construct of which logic:Holon and a level are lossy projections; a profiled holon with no declared position has no path along which its compositional depth can be coherently measured, so its level is incoherent. It is enforced only within the profile a holon is declared under, never across all holons: a holon outside any logic:MereologyProfile is never charged, mirroring logic:WeakSupplementation. Parthood is profiled, not universal, and a holonic level is path-relative (recorded per path, e.g. as a min/max band), so a position is required only when a profile demands it. Note explicitly the non-conflation with the instantiation tower: logic:holonicLevel records mereological compositional depth in a whole/part DAG, whereas logic:orderedType is the HiLog deep-instantiation order numbering logic:instanceOf chains (an order-n type instantiates an order-(n+1) type); the two axes are orthogonal and must not be conflated. An entity high in the instantiation tower (via logic:instanceOf / logic:orderedType) but occupying no holonic position still fires this violation. Enforced by the stratified NAF rule in crates/logic/src/foundation.rs (C5; design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:HolonicPosition
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Holonic Position"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The canonical relational construct of holon-ness: an entity occupies a holonic position in a particular holarchy, under a particular context, over a particular interval, along a particular path (entity, holarchy, context, interval, path). Whether an entity is a holon is read off this position, never asserted of the entity alone; the unary logic:Holon is its lossy projection. It is reified with the role properties logic:positionEntity, logic:positionHolarchy, logic:positionContext, logic:positionInterval, and logic:positionPath, because the foundation relation is five-place and the arity-bounded reasoning surface carries it as an objectified position (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:HornFragment
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormulaFragment ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Horn Fragment"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The formula-fragment facet value selecting Horn clauses (at most one positive literal per clause). Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; the rule fragment over which least-model semantics is well-defined and, for the function-free case, terminating — the base on which the positive-Horn, stratified-negation and procedural presets build."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:InconsistencyPreserving
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PreservationKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Inconsistency Preserving"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A canonical inconsistency appears as an inconsistency in the projection: the projection does not silently mask a contradiction present in the canonical model. The inconsistency-direction polarity guaranteeing canonical → projection visibility."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:InconsistencyReflecting
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PreservationKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Inconsistency Reflecting"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An inconsistency in the projection implies an inconsistency in the canonical model: the projection raises no spurious contradiction absent from the canonical model. The inconsistency-direction polarity guaranteeing projection → canonical soundness, dual to logic:InconsistencyPreserving."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Individual
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Individual"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A particular: an entity that is NOT a logic:Type — it is instantiated by types (via logic:instanceOf) but has no instances of its own, sitting at the bottom of every instantiation chain (logic:orderedType 0). The counterpart of gufo:Individual; the root complementing logic:Type. Specialized by logic:ConcreteIndividual (in spacetime) and logic:AbstractIndividual (outside it). Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:IntegrationDeficient
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:AgencyVerdict ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Integration Deficient"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The agency-verdict value for the second Koestlerian pathology — a 'whole' that refuses to integrate: under the declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile, the holon bears an logic:selfAssertiveBasis value (it asserts itself as a whole) but bears no logic:integrativeBasis value, so its integrative (subordination-as-a-part) face has collapsed. Reached by negation-as-failure over the integrative marker while the self-assertive marker holds, so the verdict is profile-relative, never a bare default. The co-equal counterpart of logic:AutonomyDeficient (the opposite collapse); contrast logic:HolonIntegral (both faces) and logic:AgencyUnknown (neither evidenced) (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:JointOutcome
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Joint Outcome"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "One row of a logic:DependencyModel's explicit joint table: a single joint assignment of truth values to the model's correlated facts, together with logic:jointProbability for that assignment. The facts asserted true in this outcome are named by logic:outcomeAssignment; correlated facts not named are taken to be false in this outcome."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Kind
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Kind"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A rigid sortal that supplies a principle of identity to its instances and applies necessarily across every world in which an instance exists: an ultimate sortal under which an object falls for its whole existence. Every object instantiates exactly one ultimate Kind. Rigid (rigidlyAppliesTo) and identity-supplying (suppliesIdentity); contrast the anti-rigid Role and Phase."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:LeastModelSemantics
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ModelSemantics ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Least Model Semantics"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The model-semantics facet value selecting the unique least Herbrand model of a positive (or stratified) program. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; the monotonic semantics underlying the positive-Horn and stratified-negation presets, contrasted with the well-founded and stable-model values for unstratified negation."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:MaterialRelationshipType
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Material Relationship Type"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A logic:RelationshipType whose instances are material relations — relations founded on a logic:Relator that mediates the relata (marriage, employment, enrolment). The counterpart of gufo:MaterialRelationshipType; the relation it types holds in virtue of the mediating Relator existing (logic:mediates), so its instances are reducible to the relator and its mediation links. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:ComparativeRelationshipType, which needs no relator."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:McpActionSchema
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf logic:ActionSchema ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "MCP Action Schema"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A logic:ActionSchema that grounds an MCP (Model Context Protocol) tool action — the opt-in marker subtype that brings an action schema under the stricter MCP-action governance profile (logic:McpActionPolicyShape). Beyond the facets every action schema carries it must always declare a logic:compensation (rollback) because an MCP tool that mutates external state must be recoverable: the dogfood case where the canonical process model governs the agent's own tool calls. A plain logic:ActionSchema is NOT required to carry compensation; typing it logic:McpActionSchema is the explicit declaration that the governance profile applies."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:MereologyConstraint
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Mereology Constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A named profiled-mereology axiom a whole can violate — the family of mereological well-formedness constraints (weak supplementation and its kin) that hold only within a declared logic:MereologyProfile. Distinct from logic:Discipline, the closed set of OntoUML structural anti-patterns: mereology constraints are scoped to a profile, not asserted foundation-wide. Its named individuals are the labels a logic:violation fact may point at; the set is closed so a misspelt label names no declared constraint and is rejected rather than silently accepted."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:MereologyProfile
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Mereology Profile"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A declared scope within which the strong mereological axioms — weak supplementation above all — are taken to hold. Parthood is profiled, not universal: weak supplementation is true of functional complexes and quantities but false of many legitimate wholes (singleton-membered collectives, abstract aggregates, in-progress assemblies), so logic: scopes it to the MereologyProfile a whole is declared under (via logic:underMereologyProfile) rather than asserting it across all logic:properPartOf. A whole outside any profile is never charged with a logic:WeakSupplementation violation (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:MetaLevelFormula
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:NodeKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Meta-Level Formula"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A formula about formulas: a statement that quotes or ranges over other propositions, distinct from the propositions it mentions. Kept apart from the object level so a meta-level quotation cannot collapse into the object-level assertion it quotes; any holds or truth predicate over it is stratified so the IR cannot encode a self-referential paradox by accident."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:MixIden
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:Discipline ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Mixed Identity"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The OntoUML MixIden anti-pattern: a sortal inherits its principle of identity from exactly one Kind. A Kind specializing another Kind, or a non-Kind sortal tracing to zero or to two-or-more Kinds, violates it. The lowering of reasoning_lint.identity_overlap."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:MixRig
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:Discipline ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Mixed Rigidity"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The OntoUML MixRig anti-pattern: a rigid sortal (Kind or SubKind) must never specialize an anti-rigid type (Phase, Role, PhaseMixin, RoleMixin, Mixin), because a rigid type cannot inherit contingent instantiation. A rigid sortal with an anti-rigid-type ancestor violates it. The other half of the lowering of reasoning_lint.anti_rigidity_discipline."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Mixin
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Mixin"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A semi-rigid non-sortal that classifies instances of several Kinds, applying rigidly to some instances and anti-rigidly to others: a dispersive type whose rigidity is mixed across its extension. Identity-dispersive like a Category, but semi-rigid rather than uniformly rigid."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Mode
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Mode"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An aspect that is NOT directly measurable in a quality space — a belief, a skill, an intention, a symptom — whether intrinsic to a single bearer or relational across several. The counterpart of gufo:IntrinsicMode and gufo:ExtrinsicMode generalized: a logic:Aspect lacking a quality value (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge). Contrast logic:Quality, which is measurable."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:ModelSemantics
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Model Semantics"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The facet value class of the model-semantics facet: which models of a program are selected as authoritative. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. Its individuals are classical entailment, the least model, the well-founded model, and the stable models — the choice that settles which entailments hold over a rule program."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:MonotonicRevision
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:RevisionPolicy ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Monotonic Revision"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The revision-policy value under which new information only adds conclusions and never retracts them: there is nothing to revise because no conclusion is ever defeated. The degenerate revision policy of monotonic reasoning (the positive-Horn preset), contrasted with logic:EntrenchmentRevision and logic:TruthMaintenanceRevision, which absorb defeating information."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:NoArgumentation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ArgumentationSemantics ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "No Argumentation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The argumentation-facet value selecting no argumentation layer: conflicts are not resolved by an argumentation semantics. The default for contracts whose conflict resolution is handled by the model semantics or revision policy alone, contrasted with the grounded, preferred, and policy-specific argumentation values."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:ArgumentEvaluation .

logic:NoUncertainty
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:UncertaintyMeasure ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "No Uncertainty"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The uncertainty-measure value carrying no graded belief: reasoning is categorical. The default of the uncertainty set facet (the empty selection), contrasted with logic:ProbabilisticMeasure, logic:WeightedRankingMeasure, and logic:FuzzyMeasure, any combination of which may be in force at once."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:NodeKind
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Node Kind"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The typed-sum tag every node of the canonical logic: IR declares. The IR is a typed sum, not an untyped triple bag: each node names its kind, and the kind governs what may be done with it — keeping a constraint distinct from a derivation rule, a query operator from a program operator, and a meta-level quotation from the object-level assertion it quotes. Its individuals are the object-level formula, the meta-level formula, the constraint, the derivation rule, the query, the transaction program, the action schema, the validation shape, and the law-bearing correspondence."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:NonRigidType
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Non-Rigid Type"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A logic:Type that is not rigid: either anti-rigid (logic:AntiRigidType) or semi-rigid (logic:SemiRigidType). The counterpart of gufo:NonRigidType; the meta-type that is the union complement of logic:RigidType over the sorts — its instances are logic:Phase, logic:Role, logic:RoleMixin, logic:PhaseMixin (anti-rigid) and logic:Mixin (semi-rigid). Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. The negation of logic:RigidType, used where a discipline only needs 'not necessarily applying' rather than the stronger 'contingent for every instance'."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:NonSortal
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Non-Sortal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A logic:Type that aggregates instances of several different logic:Sortals and supplies NO principle of identity of its own — it spans Kinds dispersively. The counterpart of gufo:NonSortal; the meta-type whose instances are the dispersive sorts: logic:Category, logic:Mixin, logic:RoleMixin, logic:PhaseMixin. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Identity-dispersive (logic:suppliesIdentity holds for none of its instances); contrast logic:Sortal."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Object
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Object"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A substantial endurant that bears its own principle of identity and does not inhere in another individual — a person, an organization, a physical artefact. The counterpart of gufo:Object: an independent endurant, contrasted with the aspects that existentially depend on it. Every Object is a logic:Substantial and a logic:Endurant (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:ObjectLevelFormula
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:NodeKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Object-Level Formula"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An ordinary first-order formula over the domain of discourse: the object-level node kind. Its quantifiers range over individuals in the domain, some of which may be reified predicates or types, so the object level stays first-order even where it expresses what reads as quantification over predicates or types."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:OccurrentBoundary
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Occurrent Boundary"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed class of perdurant boundary values: the two-valued result a perdurant receives via logic:occurrentBoundary. Its named individuals are logic:Open (an on-going action over an open interval — the arriving) and logic:Closed (a completed unitary event over a closed interval — the arrival). The set is closed, so a misspelt value names no declared boundary and is rejected rather than silently accepted, mirroring logic:EmergenceVerdict and logic:ConstraintVerdict. The carrier of the YAMATO/Galton action(open)/event(closed) distinction as a value, not a subclass (Principle 9)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:OccurrentBoundaryMismatch
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:OccurrentConstraint ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Occurrent Boundary Mismatch"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The boundary-exclusivity axiom as an occurrent constraint: a perdurant must not be both on-going and completed — it must not carry both logic:occurrentBoundary logic:Open and logic:occurrentBoundary logic:Closed. The two halves of the action(open)/event(closed) distinction are mutually exclusive at a single standpoint; an occurrent bearing both is the logic:violation, entailed by the foundation lowering rather than asserted by hand."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:OccurrentChangeAsymmetry
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:OccurrentConstraint ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Occurrent Change Asymmetry"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The change-asymmetry axiom as an occurrent constraint: a completed unitary occurrent (logic:occurrentBoundary logic:Closed) must not vary — it must bear no time-varying logic:Fluent. Processes and on-going actions may change; an event, once whole, cannot (the YAMATO/Galton process-not-equal-event refinement, restoring the UFO-B four-dimensional account). A Closed occurrent that bears a logic:Fluent is the logic:violation, entailed by the foundation lowering rather than asserted by hand."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:OccurrentConstraint
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Occurrent Constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A named occurrent well-formedness axiom a perdurant can violate — the family of constraints governing the process/event change-asymmetry and the action(open)/event(closed) boundary. Distinct from logic:Discipline (the closed set of OntoUML structural anti-patterns) and from logic:MereologyConstraint (profiled-mereology axioms): occurrent constraints govern the four-dimensional semantics of perdurants. Its named individuals are the labels a logic:violation fact may point at; the set is closed so a misspelt label names no declared constraint and is rejected rather than silently accepted."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Open
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:OccurrentBoundary ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Open"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The occurrent-boundary value for an on-going action: a perdurant unfolding over an open temporal interval, not yet a completed whole — the arriving, the running, the prescribed-but-unexecuted plan. The action half of the YAMATO/Galton action(open)/event(closed) distinction; an occurrent that varies (bears a logic:Fluent) is properly Open, since only the unfinished can still change. Contrast logic:Closed."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:OpenWorldClosure
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ClosureValue ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Open-World Closure"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The open-world value of the closure map: for the predicate or context key it is bound to, absence of a fact means unknown rather than false. The default for any key not explicitly closed; the closure facet is a map, so this value is read per key, with logic:ClosedWorldClosure applied only inside a logic:WorldBoundary."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Outcome
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Outcome"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "One branch of the nondeterministic outcome set of a logic:ActionSchema: a single alternative result, naming via logic:outcomeSituation the successor situation it reaches and via the reused logic:compensation the action that recovers from THIS branch specifically. Reifying each branch as an Outcome is what lets compensation be outcome-indexed rather than a single generic undo across the schema, and what lets plan-success quantification (logic:planSuccessMode) range over the branches. A logic:ActionSchema points at its branches through logic:nondeterministicOutcome."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:OwlProjection
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ProjectionTarget ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "OWL Projection"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The projection-target value requesting the answer be rendered to an OWL surface (e.g. an EL or DL profile). One of several output targets a single contract may name at once; like every projection target it is a rendering request and never alters which entailments hold."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Participation
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Participation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The reified involvement of an endurant in a perdurant — an actor's participation in an event, a reactant's participation in a reaction. The counterpart of gufo:Participation: a relator-like reified link binding a logic:Endurant to the logic:Perdurant it takes part in, so the role and temporal scope of the involvement can be carried on the participation itself."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:PathContextAxis
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ContextAxis ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Path Context Axis"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The path index axis of the multi-dimensional context facet: a truth is relative to a transaction or execution path. One of several context axes that coexist on a single result — world, standpoint, time, and path index the same result simultaneously rather than being alternative values of one slot."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:PathInvocation
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Path Invocation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A by-name application of a logic:PathShape with concrete depth arguments — the canonical, reified form of a parametric call such as :nearbyOrgs(?maxDepth := 2). It carries logic:invokesPathShape (the shape applied) and logic:pathDepthArg (the value bound to the shape's logic:pathDepthParam), so a named, reusable traversal is instantiated at a specific bound without rewriting the shape. The surface syntax :name(?param := value) is a rendering of this individual, not a separate construct (Principle 17)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:PathShape
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Path Shape"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A named, parametric predicate-path traversal specification: a reusable description of how to walk the graph, invocable by name with a depth parameter. A PathShape carries a base step — either a named predicate (logic:pathStepPredicate) or a predicate wildcard (logic:pathWildcard true, optionally scoped by logic:pathNamespaceScope) — together with a bounded depth range (logic:pathMinDepth … logic:pathMaxDepth; an absent maximum means unbounded) and a declared depth parameter name (logic:pathDepthParam) bound at each logic:PathInvocation. It SUBSUMES and EXTENDS SPARQL 1.1 property paths (§9), which are fixed strings with no predicate wildcard, no bounded depth {1,n}, and no named or parameterized reuse: 'all nodes within n hops, by any predicate' becomes a first-class, reusable term. The PathShape is the canonical logic: form; an extended SPARQL property path and a depth-bounded Datalog program are its projections (Principle 17), and the native Datalog least-model fixpoint is its runtime."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Perdurant
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Perdurant"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An occurrent: an individual that unfolds in time by accumulating temporal parts, so that at any single moment only a part of it is present. The four-dimensional counterpart of the endurant; logic:Event and logic:Process are perdurants (every Event is a Perdurant — the supertype relation is stated here in prose rather than as an rdfs:subClassOf edge, matching how the foundation sorts are authored). Contrast logic:Endurant, which is wholly present at each moment."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Phase
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Phase"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An anti-rigid sortal an instance falls under during a stage of its existence determined by a change in its own intrinsic state — child, adult, vacant, occupied. Anti-rigid: there is a world of existence in which the instance lacks the Phase (the anti-rigidity witness). Contrast Role, whose change is relational rather than intrinsic."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:PhaseMixin
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Phase Mixin"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An anti-rigid non-sortal that abstracts an intrinsically-determined phase shared across instances of several Kinds — living thing (a person or an animal in its living phase). Anti-rigid and identity-dispersive: a Phase generalized to span multiple Kinds without supplying identity."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:PolicySpecificArgumentation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ArgumentationSemantics ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Policy-Specific Argumentation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The argumentation-facet value selecting a domain- or policy-specific conflict-resolution semantics rather than a standard Dung semantics — e.g. a declared preference or priority ordering proper to a normative or legal register. Contrast logic:GroundedArgumentation and logic:PreferredArgumentation, the standard abstract-argumentation semantics."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:ArgumentEvaluation .

logic:PositiveHornProfile
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ReasoningPreset ;
    logic:expandsToFacet logic:CertifiedFragmentResource ,
        logic:HornFragment ,
        logic:LeastModelSemantics ,
        logic:MonotonicRevision ,
        logic:OpenWorldClosure ;
    logic:defaultClosure logic:OpenWorldClosure ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Positive Horn Profile"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The monotonic Horn-rule semantics: least-model semantics over positive (negation-free) rules, always terminating for the function-free fragment. The base case against which every richer profile adds expressivity and cost."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:PreferredArgumentation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ArgumentationSemantics ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Preferred Argumentation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The preferred Dung argumentation semantics: acceptance over the maximal (with respect to set inclusion) admissible sets of arguments. The credulous counterpart of logic:GroundedArgumentation — a framework may have several preferred extensions, so it admits genuine choice where the grounded semantics is uniquely sceptical."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:ArgumentEvaluation .

logic:PreservationKind
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Preservation Kind"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The polarity of guarantee a reasoning projection makes about its answers relative to the canonical logic: model: the answer-preservation classification recorded in the loss ledger for each projection, distinct from and complementary to the complexity/decidability class. Its individuals range from exact preservation through sound under-approximation and complete over-approximation to validation-only, the unsupported floor (the construct cannot be expressed in the target at all), and the two inconsistency-direction kinds."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ProbabilisticMeasure
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:UncertaintyMeasure ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Probabilistic Measure"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The uncertainty measure carrying calibrated probabilities, requiring a declared logic:ProbabilityModel. One member of the uncertainty-measure set facet (it may coexist with logic:WeightedRankingMeasure or logic:FuzzyMeasure); it is a measure carried alongside the chosen model semantics, never a model-semantics value of its own, and never the default reading of a logic:confidence number."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ProbabilisticProfile
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ReasoningPreset ;
    logic:expandsToFacet logic:ProbabilisticMeasure ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Probabilistic Profile"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Probabilistic inference over logic:probability, ProbLog-style: requires an explicit independence or dependency model. Probabilistic inference is available only in this profile — it is not the default reading of every confidence number, and a logic:confidence annotation is never interpreted as a probability unless an explicit mapping to logic:probability is declared."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ProbabilityModel
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Probability Model"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A declared independence or dependency model governing probabilistic inference for a rule set or world. Probabilistic inference under logic:ProbabilisticProfile is available ONLY when such a model is declared via logic:probabilityModel: the model fixes the joint distribution over the logic:probability facts so that marginals are well-defined. Absent a declared model the profile refuses to infer probabilities — it never silently assumes independence, because treating un-modelled confidence metadata as a probability model is the named failure mode this vocabulary exists to prevent."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ProceduralExecution
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ResourcePolicy ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Procedural Execution"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The operational-execution property of a resource policy: SLD search control (cut) and builtins are permitted — an operational rather than purely declarative reading. This is the facet that licenses cut; cut-confinement (the AC-2 seal) is decided on it, never on the budget/bound property: a budget-bounded contract does not, by that fact alone, license cut. Only the procedural preset expands to it, but a contract assembled directly with this facet licenses cut even without the ProceduralPrologProfile preset name."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ProceduralPrologProfile
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ReasoningPreset ;
    logic:expandsToFacet logic:BudgetBoundedResource ,
        logic:HornFragment ,
        logic:ProceduralExecution ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Procedural Prolog Profile"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "SLD resolution with cut and builtins: an operational, not purely declarative, semantics in which procedural search control (cut) and order-sensitive evaluation are permitted. Cut lives only here; artifacts using it must not project as declarative rules without recording the loss, because cut can change a program's answer set and defeats faithful-by-construction explanation."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Process
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Process"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A perdurant with internal dynamics: an occurrent composed of sub-processes and phases that unfold over its temporal extent — a manufacturing run, a negotiation, a fermentation. A logic:Perdurant richer than a punctual event (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge); part of the native four-dimensional treatment that restores the UFO-B account gUFO scales back (criticism 3). Dissective: any temporal part of a process is itself that same process, and a process MAY vary over its extent (it bears time-varying logic:Fluents) — the change-bearing half of the process-not-equal-event asymmetry."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:ProjectionTarget
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Projection Target"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The facet value class of a projection target: a surface the answer is rendered to. The projection facet is an output request that may name one or more targets (canonical, OWL, Datalog, Common Logic, validation-only) at once; it is a standing request, not a semantic selection, and never alters which entailments hold."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:PropertyPathProjection
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ProjectionTarget ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Property Path Projection"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The projection-target value requesting that a logic:PathShape (or a rule's path-structured body) be rendered to a SPARQL property-path surface — extended by GMEOW past SPARQL 1.1 §9 with bounded depth {n,m} and a predicate wildcard. One of several output targets a single contract may name at once; like every projection target it is a rendering request and never alters which entailments hold. A consumer restricted to standard SPARQL §9 receives the unrolled or approximated form, and that loss is declared in the loss ledger rather than hidden."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Quality
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Quality"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An aspect whose value is a point or region in a quality space — a mass, a temperature, a colour hue — an intrinsic, directly measurable moment. The counterpart of gufo:Quality; a logic:Aspect that takes a logic:QualityValue in a logic:QualitySpace (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge). Contrast logic:Mode, which is not directly measurable."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:QualitySpace
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Quality Space"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The structured space of possible values for a kind of quality — the mass scale, the temperature scale, a colour solid — within which a logic:Quality's logic:QualityValue is located. The conceptual-space structure (ordering, metric, dimensions) against which quality values are compared; it supplies the geometry a bare value would lack."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:QualityValue
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Quality Value"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A point or region within a quality space that a logic:Quality takes as its value — 80 kg, 37 °C, the hue at coordinate (h,s,v). The counterpart of gufo:QualityValue; a logic:AbstractIndividual situated in a logic:QualitySpace (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Quantity
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Quantity"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An amount of stuff individuated by its constitution rather than by a count of members — a portion of water, a lump of clay, a quantity of gold. The counterpart of gufo:Quantity; its identity tracks the matter that constitutes it (maximally self-connected portions of a substance), not a number of discrete units. Contrast logic:Collection, individuated by its members."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Query
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:NodeKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Query"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A goal to be resolved, carried together with its answer shape: the node kind that asks a question of the IR rather than asserting or deriving. Distinct from logic:DerivationRule and logic:TransactionProgram so a query operator is never read as a program operator."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:RdfEqualityPolicy
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:EqualityPolicy ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "RDF Equality Policy"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The equality-policy value under which term identity is RDF node identity — two IRIs are equal exactly when they are the same node, and distinct IRIs are not assumed to co-refer absent an asserted equality. The baseline graph reading; contrast logic:ExplicitEqualityPolicy and logic:UniqueNameEqualityPolicy."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ReasoningContract
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Reasoning Contract"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A compositional specification of the reasoning semantics a rule set is interpreted under: an independent selection across orthogonal facets (formula fragment, model semantics, truth/inconsistency semantics, negation operators, closure, context, evolution, uncertainty, argumentation, revision, equality) plus two standing requests (resource policy, projection targets). The canonical form GMEOW reasons over; the historical named profiles are presets that expand to a full facet selection. Replaces the single monolithic semantic-profile axis: 'sound' is meaningless until the full contract is fixed."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:ReasoningPreset
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Reasoning Preset"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:subClassOf logic:ReasoningContract ;
    skos:definition "A named ReasoningContract that fixes a common, supported facet selection — sugar the compiler expands to the full facet bundle before reasoning. The historical profile names (positive-Horn, stratified-negation, well-founded, stable-model, procedural, probabilistic) survive only as presets, not as indivisible alternatives."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:ReductionTheory
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Reduction Theory"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A declared theory of part-whole reducibility, relative to which an logic:EmergenceAssessment is made. It carries, via logic:reductionBasis, the property-values it treats as part-reducible — reconstructible from the proper parts that bear them. Emergence is always relative to such a theory: the same whole property may be logic:Aggregate under one ReductionTheory and logic:Emergent under another, and an logic:Emergent verdict can be overturned by a later, stronger theory without contradiction precisely because the assessment records which theory it was relative to. The systems-theory analogue of a logic:MereologyProfile — it scopes the emergence calculus rather than asserting reducibility foundation-wide (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:RelComp
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:Discipline ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Relator Completeness"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The OntoUML RelComp anti-pattern: a concrete Relator must mediate at least two distinct relata. A concrete Relator (one with no logic: subclass to defer its mediations to) that mediates fewer than two distinct entities violates it. The lowering of reasoning_lint.relator_mediation."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:RelationshipType
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Relationship Type"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A logic:Type whose instances are relationships (relators or comparative relations): the type-level classifier of how two or more entities are related. The counterpart of gufo:RelationshipType; specialized by logic:MaterialRelationshipType (founded on a logic:Relator) and logic:ComparativeRelationshipType (grounded in the relata's qualities, with no relator). Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Relator
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Relator"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A truthmaker of a material relation: an objectified relationship — a marriage, an employment, an enrolment — that mediates two or more relata and existentially depends on each of them. A Relator must mediate at least two distinct entities (the relator-mediation discipline, RelComp); the relation it grounds holds in virtue of the Relator existing."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:ResourcePolicy
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Resource Policy"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The facet value class of the resource facet: the engine's execution discipline. It is a structured execution policy holding several independent properties together — whether a certified-complete, terminating fragment is required AND what budget or bound applies — not a single complete-vs-bounded toggle, and not a semantic selection. A contract may carry both a certified-fragment requirement and a budget at once."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:RevisionPolicy
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Revision Policy"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The facet value class of the revision facet: how a body of conclusions absorbs change. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. Its individuals range from monotonic (nothing retracted) through entrenchment-ordered belief revision to truth-maintenance."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:RigidType
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Rigid Type"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A logic:Type that applies necessarily to each of its instances — in every world in which an instance exists it instantiates the type (logic:rigidlyAppliesTo holds for all its instances). The counterpart of gufo:RigidType; the meta-type whose instances are the rigid sorts: logic:Kind and logic:SubKind are each a logic:RigidType and a logic:Sortal, logic:Category is a logic:RigidType and a logic:NonSortal. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:AntiRigidType."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Role
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Role"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An anti-rigid sortal an instance falls under contingently, by virtue of a relation it bears to some other entity — student, employee, defendant. Anti-rigid: there is a world of existence in which the instance lacks the Role (the anti-rigidity witness). Identity-dependent on the underlying Kind; contrast Phase, whose change is intrinsic rather than relational."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:RoleMixin
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Role Mixin"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An anti-rigid non-sortal that abstracts a relationally-acquired property shared across instances of several Kinds — customer (a person or an organization), insured party. Anti-rigid and identity-dispersive: a Role generalized to span multiple Kinds without supplying identity."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:RuleNoClosedWorldInCounterfactual
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:CompatibilityRule ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Rule: No Closed-World Closure In Counterfactual States"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The compatibility rule forbidding logic:ClosedWorldClosure — whether the contract's logic:defaultClosure or any per-key closure entry value — together with counterfactual entrenchment revision (logic:EntrenchmentRevision is the contract-internal indicator that counterfactual closest-world states are generated). The counterfactual states are open-ended, so reading absence as falsehood inside them is unsound; a contract that names both is unsupported. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); this individual is a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:RuleNoParaconsistentCounterfactualRevision
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:CompatibilityRule ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Rule: No Paraconsistent Truth Under Counterfactual Revision"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The compatibility rule forbidding a paraconsistent valuation — a gap/glut-admitting logic:admissibleValuation (logic:AdmitAllFour, logic:ForbidGap, or logic:ForbidGlut) OR the logic:BelnapBilattice truth algebra — together with counterfactual entrenchment revision (logic:EntrenchmentRevision, the contract-internal indicator of counterfactual closest-world generation). The closest-world selection that generates the counterfactual states is not defined over gappy or glutty valuations; a contract that names both is unsupported. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); this individual is a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:RuleNoProbabilisticStableModel
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:CompatibilityRule ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Rule: No Probabilistic Measure Over Stable-Model Semantics"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The compatibility rule forbidding logic:ProbabilisticMeasure in the uncertainty-measure set together with logic:StableModelSemantics as the model semantics. A calibrated probability mass is not well-defined over the multiple incomparable answer sets the stable-model semantics admits; a contract that names both is unsupported. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); this individual is a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:RuleProbabilisticRequiresModel
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:CompatibilityRule ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Rule: Probabilistic Measure Requires A Declared Probability Model"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The graph-dependent compatibility rule requiring that whenever a contract carries logic:ProbabilisticMeasure, the source graph declares a logic:ProbabilityModel (via logic:probabilityModel or an individual typed logic:ProbabilityModel). Absent a declared model the contract is unsupported: a probabilistic measure is never inferred from confidence metadata and independence is never silently assumed. Because it inspects the surrounding graph it is enforced in the front-end rather than the contract-internal rule table; authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust), projected here lossily (Principle 17)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:SemiRigidType
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Semi-Rigid Type"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A logic:Type that is rigid for some of its instances and anti-rigid for others — logic:rigidlyAppliesTo holds for part of its extension and fails for the rest. The counterpart of gufo:SemiRigidType; its sole foundation instance is logic:Mixin (a logic:SemiRigidType and a logic:NonSortal). Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. A logic:SemiRigidType is a logic:NonRigidType but not a logic:AntiRigidType (which requires contingency for every instance)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Situation
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Situation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A reified configuration of entities and their properties standing in a state of affairs at a time — the DOLCE Description-and-Situation sense: a snapshot of how things are that can satisfy a described state (a goal-world realized by a Situation). The static counterpart of the dynamic Event."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Sortal
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Sortal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A logic:Type that carries a principle of identity for its instances — it answers what counts as the same instance over time. The counterpart of gufo:Sortal; the meta-type whose instances are the identity-bearing sorts: logic:Kind (which supplies identity, via logic:suppliesIdentity), logic:SubKind, logic:Phase, and logic:Role (which inherit it). Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:NonSortal, which supplies no identity."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:SoundUnderApproximation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PreservationKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Sound Under-Approximation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Anything the projection entails is canonically valid, but the projection may miss canonical answers: sound but incomplete. The projection never overclaims a derivation; it may under-derive."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:StableModelProfile
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ReasoningPreset ;
    logic:expandsToFacet logic:DefaultNegation ,
        logic:StableModelSemantics ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Stable Model Profile"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Answer-set / stable-model semantics: a program may have several stable models (possibly none), and entailment is over those models. NP-hard in the worst case; the profile that admits genuine non-determinism and disjunctive reasoning."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:StableModelSemantics
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ModelSemantics ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Stable Model Semantics"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The model-semantics facet value selecting answer-set (stable-model) semantics: a program may have several stable models, or none, and entailment is taken over that model set. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; the non-deterministic, NP-hard semantics for unstratified negation, contrasted with the unique well-founded model and the unique least model."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:StandpointContextAxis
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ContextAxis ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Standpoint Context Axis"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The standpoint index axis of the multi-dimensional context facet: a truth is relative to a standpoint (a perspective in the sharpening poset). One of several context axes that coexist on a single result — world, standpoint, time, and path index the same result simultaneously rather than being alternative values of one slot."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:StateTransitionEvolution
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:EvolutionMode ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "State-Transition Evolution"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The evolution-facet value under which state changes across discrete transitions between successive states, each a configuration reasoned over in turn. The state-change mode between the static default and the full transaction-path semantics; independent of the model-semantics facet."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:StaticEvolution
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:EvolutionMode ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Static Evolution"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The evolution-facet value under which no state change occurs — reasoning is over a single, degenerate one-state path. The default evolution mode; contrast logic:StateTransitionEvolution and logic:TransactionPathEvolution."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:StereotypeCardinality
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:Discipline ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Stereotype Cardinality"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The discipline that every class carries exactly one stereotype: a class with no meta-class pun, or with two or more distinct meta-class puns, violates it. The lowering of reasoning_lint.exactly_one_stereotype — the precondition every other discipline assumes."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:StratifiedNAFProfile
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ReasoningPreset ;
    logic:expandsToFacet logic:DefaultNegation ,
        logic:HornFragment ,
        logic:LeastModelSemantics ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Stratified Negation-As-Failure Profile"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Negation-as-failure under stratification: a unique perfect model with PTIME data complexity, where negated literals are evaluated only over strata already settled. Adds well-behaved negation without the multiple models of the stable-model semantics."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:SubKind
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Sub Kind"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A rigid sortal that specializes a Kind without supplying its own independent principle of identity: it carries the identity criterion inherited from the Kind it specializes. Rigid like a Kind, but identity-dependent rather than identity-supplying."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Substantial
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Substantial"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An endurant that does NOT inhere in another individual: an independent bearer that can exist on its own and onto which aspects inhere. The complement of logic:Aspect within the endurant category; every logic:Object is a Substantial (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:TimeContextAxis
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ContextAxis ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Time Context Axis"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The time index axis of the multi-dimensional context facet: a truth is relative to a time (a narrative or temporal reference frame). One of several context axes that coexist on a single result — world, standpoint, time, and path index the same result simultaneously rather than being alternative values of one slot."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:TransactionPathEvolution
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:EvolutionMode ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Transaction-Path Evolution"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The evolution-facet value selecting the Transaction-Logic state-change semantics of LOGIC-TRANSACTION.md — serial conjunction (⊗), executional entailment over a path of states, and elementary updates as supersession. It is a facet value, never a seventh profile, and is independent of the model-semantics facet; its full semantics are specified in LOGIC-TRANSACTION.md."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ElementaryUpdate
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Elementary Update"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A single Transaction-Logic state-transition primitive over a path of WorldStore snapshots. Its two concrete forms are `ins(F)`, which makes a support hold in the successor state, and `del(F)`, which retires one active support in the successor state without deleting the historical assertion. Conflicting same-fact updates are resolved by the declared entrenchment ordering."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:DeleteUpdate
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Delete Update"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:subClassOf logic:ElementaryUpdate ;
    skos:definition "An elementary Transaction-Logic update of the `del(F)` kind: it retires one active support from the successor state while retaining the historical support in the path record. `del` is supersession, not physical erasure; state validity changes by moving to a successor snapshot, while displayability remains a separate disclosure decision."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:InsertUpdate
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Insert Update"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:subClassOf logic:ElementaryUpdate ;
    skos:definition "An elementary Transaction-Logic update of the `ins(F)` kind: it asserts one support into the successor state of a path. Insertion advances the path by materializing the support in the successor snapshot; it does not mutate the predecessor state."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:TransactionProgram
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:NodeKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Transaction Program"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A state-changing composite over the path semantics of the transaction layer — insertion, deletion, hypothetical execution, and supersession rather than erasure. Its combinators are typed apart from formula connectives: serial composition is not conjunction, so a program operator is never confused with a logical one."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:TruthAlgebra
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Truth Algebra"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The facet value class of the truth algebra: the lattice of truth values over which valuations range. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. It is one of the three independent components of the truth/inconsistency facet — algebra, admissible-valuation policy, designated values — that together separate FDE, LP, K3 and classical logic; its values are the four-valued Belnap bilattice and the classical two-valued algebra."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:TruthMaintenanceRevision
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:RevisionPolicy ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Truth-Maintenance Revision"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The revision-policy value under which derived conclusions are tracked by their justifications, so retracting a premise automatically retracts the conclusions that depended on it (a truth-maintenance system). The dependency-directed counterpart of logic:EntrenchmentRevision; contrast logic:MonotonicRevision, which never retracts."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Type
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Type"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A universal: a type whose instances share a common feature, reified as a first-order individual so it can itself be the object of logic:instanceOf and carry a logic:orderedType. The counterpart of gufo:Type; first-order (its instances are logic:Individuals, logic:orderedType 1) or higher-order (its instances are themselves types). The root of the type taxonomy, complementing logic:Individual; every foundation sort (logic:Kind, logic:Role, …) and every meta-type below is a logic:Type."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:UncertaintyMeasure
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Uncertainty Measure"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The facet value class of the uncertainty facet: how graded belief is carried. Set-valued on a ReasoningContract — several measures (probabilistic, weighted/ranking, fuzzy) may be in force on the same result at once, or none. Its individuals record the measures in force, not a single chosen one."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:UniqueNameEqualityPolicy
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:EqualityPolicy ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Unique-Name Equality Policy"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The equality-policy value imposing the unique-name assumption: distinct names denote distinct entities unless equality is explicitly asserted. The optional strengthening of logic:RdfEqualityPolicy; contrast logic:ExplicitEqualityPolicy, which neither assumes distinctness nor unifies beyond what is declared."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Unsupported
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PreservationKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Unsupported"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The weakest preservation polarity: the construct cannot be expressed in the target at all. A formula that lowers to unsupported is carried and flagged in the loss ledger, never silently dropped, and every result downstream of the lowering discloses which formulas the target did not evaluate. The legalization floor — a lowering is a total function into legal output plus flagged residue, and an unsupported construct is residue, never loss in silence."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ValidationOnly
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PreservationKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Validation Only"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The projection detects some invalidity but is not an entailment relation: it can flag ill-formedness without computing canonical consequences. The honest label for bridge views (e.g. BFO/DOLCE) that constrain but do not reason; they carry this or no preservation claim, never logic:ExactPreservation."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ValidationOnlyProjection
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ProjectionTarget ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Validation-Only Projection"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The projection-target value requesting a validation-only surface: it detects ill-formedness without computing canonical consequences (the honest output for bridge views that constrain but do not reason). One of several output targets a single contract may name at once; it never alters which entailments hold."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ValidationShape
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:NodeKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Validation Shape"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world data-shape condition: the SHACL-shaped subset of the IR, evaluated against a dataset rather than as an open-world entailment. The node kind for conditions checked under the closed-world reading where absence may be read as falsity."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:VariableCollection
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Variable Collection"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A logic:Collection whose membership may change over time while the collection retains its identity — a club whose roster gains and loses members, a playlist edited over the years. The counterpart of gufo:VariableCollection. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Its time-varying logic:memberOf is naturally carried as a logic:Fluent (membership indexed to time/world) rather than as the static membership of a logic:FixedCollection — the four-dimensional treatment of changing membership."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:WeakSupplementation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:MereologyConstraint ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Weak Supplementation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The weak-supplementation axiom as a profiled-mereology constraint: a whole with a proper part must have another proper part disjoint from the first. It is enforced only within the logic:MereologyProfile a whole is declared under (logic:underMereologyProfile), never across all parthood; a whole with a lone proper part and no disjoint co-part, declared under a profile, is the logic:violation. The prerequisites logic:overlaps and logic:disjoint are settled first, so the axiom is never applied where overlap is undefined (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:WeightedRankingMeasure
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:UncertaintyMeasure ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Weighted Ranking Measure"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The uncertainty measure carrying weighted or ranking preferences over derivations. One member of the uncertainty-measure set facet (it may coexist with logic:ProbabilisticMeasure or logic:FuzzyMeasure); distinct from a calibrated probability — a ranking weight carries no probabilistic meaning unless one is separately declared."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:WellFoundedProfile
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ReasoningPreset ;
    logic:expandsToFacet logic:DefaultNegation ,
        logic:WellFoundedSemantics ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Well-Founded Profile"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The well-founded semantics: a three-valued (true/false/undefined), total, polynomial-time semantics for normal logic programs that assigns a unique well-founded model even with unstratified negation, leaving genuinely circular literals undefined rather than branching."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:WellFoundedSemantics
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ModelSemantics ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Well-Founded Semantics"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The model-semantics facet value selecting the well-founded semantics: a unique, three-valued (true/false/undefined), total, polynomial-time model for normal programs, leaving genuinely circular literals undefined rather than branching. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; the deterministic counterpart of the non-deterministic logic:StableModelSemantics for unstratified negation."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Path
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Path"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An ordered run of states — a history — over which the typed accessibility relation logic:temporallySucceeds is read; the typed context of the context algebra that carries the Transaction-Logic state sequence, whose edges logic:transitionFromState and logic:transitionToState walk and whose positions are gmeow:State configurations, each realizing a logic:Situation. 'History' is the documented synonym. One of the distinct typed contexts (alongside logic:PossibleWorld, gmeow:EpistemicContext, gmeow:Standpoint, gmeow:Scenario, gmeow:State, gmeow:ReferenceFrame, gmeow:NarrativeReferenceFrame); no inference may cross into it by walking the bare logic:accessibleFrom superproperty, and its relation to states and situations is stated in prose, not as a subclass edge."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:PossibleWorld
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Possible World"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A typed alethic context — a logic:World of alethic possibility, one of the distinct typed contexts of the context algebra (alongside the doxastic gmeow:EpistemicContext, the perspectival gmeow:Standpoint, the hypothesized gmeow:Scenario, the gmeow:State along a logic:Path, the gmeow:ReferenceFrame, and the gmeow:NarrativeReferenceFrame). The contexts its typed accessibility relation logic:epistemicallyPossible ranges over; the modal operators (necessity, possibility) are the standard translation over that typed relation, never over a blurred union. It is a logic:World of the alethic world-type (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge), so no inference may cross into it by walking the bare logic:accessibleFrom superproperty."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:World
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "World"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A reified, named context relative to which truth is evaluated — a possible world in the Kripke sense, realized by GMEOW's materialized contextual index (standpoints, narrative reference frames, goal-, ought-, feared-, and counterfactual-worlds). Truth is world-relative and entailment is world-indexed: a contradiction within one world is a witness, a contradiction across worlds is not an inconsistency in the model. Carries a world-type taxonomy (epistemic, doxastic, telic, deontic, alethic, representational, counterfactual)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:WorldBoundary
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "World Boundary"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A scoped region within which the closed-world assumption applies: it demarcates where what is not derivable may be read as false, leaving the rest of the model under the open-world assumption. The scoping construct of the hybrid open/closed feature (LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md §Greenfield feature map): the closed-world (CWA) lane realized by the built-in SHACL is confined to what a WorldBoundary encloses, while logic: outside it stays open-world. Enforcement is seamed to the engine."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:WorldContextAxis
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ContextAxis ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "World Context Axis"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The world index axis of the multi-dimensional context facet: a truth is relative to a logic:World (a Kripke-style possible world in the materialized contextual index). One of several context axes that coexist on a single result — world, standpoint, time, and path index the same result simultaneously rather than being alternative values of one slot."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:accessibleFrom
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "accessible from"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The generic Kripke accessibility abstraction between worlds: relates a world to a world from which it is reachable, generalizing the standpoint sharpening poset. It exists for uniform traversal and provenance, not for inference — the modal operators are NOT translated over this bare relation. Necessity and possibility are evaluated over the appropriate named, typed accessibility relation (necessity is truth in every accessible context of that type, possibility truth in some), never over the blurred union of all of them. That evaluation is bounded universal quantification because the world set is the finite, materialized contextual index, not the unbounded space of all logically possible worlds. logic:accessibleFrom is the generic superproperty of the six typed accessibility relations — logic:epistemicallyPossible, logic:doxasticallyAccessible, logic:deonticallyIdeal, logic:temporallySucceeds, logic:counterfactuallyCloser, and gmeow:sharpens — but only in prose: these are NOT asserted rdfs:subPropertyOf it, because the generic superproperty licenses no cross-type entailment by itself. An inference may follow a named, typed accessibility relation; it may not conclude anything by walking the bare superproperty across contexts of different types. The one pre-existing typed sub-relation, gmeow:sharpens, carries owl:TransitiveProperty in the standpoint slice, while the five logic: kernel relations assert no OWL characteristics and document their logical character in prose — an intentional asymmetry, not an oversight."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:epistemicallyPossible
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "epistemically possible"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The typed alethic accessibility relation between logic:PossibleWorlds — a world is epistemically (alethically) accessible from another. logic:accessibleFrom is its generic superproperty in prose only: it is NOT asserted rdfs:subPropertyOf logic:accessibleFrom, because the generic superproperty licenses no cross-type entailment and a subproperty edge would manufacture exactly that inference. The modal operators are the standard translation over THIS relation, never over a blurred union of accessibility relations. It asserts no OWL characteristic; its logical character is documented in prose, matching the kernel convention."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:doxasticallyAccessible
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "doxastically accessible"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The typed doxastic accessibility relation between gmeow:EpistemicContexts — what an agent's beliefs hold accessible. It need not be reflexive (an agent may believe a falsehood); this character is documented in prose, not asserted as an OWL characteristic, matching the kernel convention. logic:accessibleFrom is its generic superproperty in prose only — NOT asserted rdfs:subPropertyOf — so the bare superproperty licenses no cross-type entailment and what is believed never leaks into what is true."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:deonticallyIdeal
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "deontically ideal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The typed deontic accessibility relation: a context is deontically ideal — an ought-world — relative to an issuer. Deontic reasoning is a USE of typed contexts, not a separate context type: a deontic claim is truth in the deontically-ideal accessible contexts of an issuer. Deontic accessibility is serial — every context from which an obligation is read has at least one accessible ideal context — so the 'satisfied in every ideal context' condition is never vacuously true; an empty ideal set yields undetermined rather than vacuous truth. logic:accessibleFrom is its generic superproperty in prose only — NOT asserted rdfs:subPropertyOf — so what is ideal never leaks into what is."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:temporallySucceeds
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "temporally succeeds"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The typed temporal accessibility relation along a logic:Path: one gmeow:State succeeds another in the ordered run of states. A strict order (irreflexive and transitive) — its character is documented in prose, not asserted as OWL characteristics, matching the kernel convention. logic:accessibleFrom is its generic superproperty in prose only — NOT asserted rdfs:subPropertyOf — so the bare superproperty licenses no cross-type entailment across context types."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:counterfactuallyCloser
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "counterfactually closer"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The typed counterfactual accessibility relation under a declared closeness ordering (Lewis comparative similarity, a generalized closeness poset over contexts). Counterfactual reasoning is a USE of typed contexts: a counterfactual claim is truth in the counterfactually-closer accessible contexts under the ordering. Closeness is declared data, not a fixed semantics. logic:accessibleFrom is its generic superproperty in prose only — NOT asserted rdfs:subPropertyOf — so what would have been never leaks into what is by walking the bare superproperty."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

# === Teleology layer properties: action-theory facets, goal/occurrence links, =
# === decomposition, conflict, goal-evaluation axes and quantities ============
# Object properties carry gmeow:boxRBox, matching the module's object-property
# convention; the unit-interval quantity properties (logic:satisfactionDegree,
# logic:objectiveValue, logic:utility) are datatype properties with no rdfs:range,
# matching logic:confidence / logic:weight. Domains are stated in prose, matching
# the module's domain/range convention. Normative in design/LOGIC-TELEOLOGY.md.

# --- Action-theory facets (domain logic:ActionSchema, stated in prose) --------

logic:precondition
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "precondition"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to the situation that must hold for the action to apply — the gate on the elementary state transition the schema grounds. Domain logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose, matching the module's domain/range convention). One of the eight action-theory facets means–end reasoning reads."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:effect
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "effect"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to the change it introduces, expressed as the supersession primitives of the transaction layer (ins/del), NEVER as physical erasure — executing an occurrence is the elementary update whose ins/del a transaction path records. Domain logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). One of the eight action-theory facets."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:invariant
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "invariant"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to what the action must preserve across its execution — the condition that holds before, during, and after. Domain logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). One of the eight action-theory facets, distinct from logic:precondition (what must hold to begin) and logic:effect (what changes)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:capability
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "capability"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to what an agent must be able to do to execute it — the executional precondition on the actor rather than on the state. Domain logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). One of the eight action-theory facets, distinct from logic:precondition (a precondition on the situation, not the agent)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:nondeterministicOutcome
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "nondeterministic outcome"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to one of its alternative effects, each reified as a logic:Outcome node naming via logic:outcomeSituation the distinct successor situation it reaches — multi-valued, so an action whose result is not fixed is represented faithfully rather than collapsed to a single effect. The outcome set this enumerates is why plan success must be quantified (logic:planSuccessMode) and why compensation is outcome-indexed: each logic:Outcome branch carries its own logic:compensation. Domain logic:ActionSchema, range logic:Outcome (stated in prose). One of the eight action-theory facets."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:boundSituationType
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "bound situation type"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates an atomic, achievement, maintenance, or avoidance logic:GoalExpression to the logic:Situation type it targets — the situation whose obtaining (via logic:situationObtains at a state along the path) decides the goal. Domain logic:GoalExpression, range logic:Situation (stated in prose). Part of a goal expression's STRUCTURAL identity together with its kind and operands."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:deadlineWindow
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "deadline window"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a deadline-window logic:GoalExpression to the bounding interval after which its window closes — until the window closes the evaluation is logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined, and once it closes the judgment becomes conclusive. Domain logic:GoalExpression (stated in prose); the range is the bounding interval, left open in this standalone module. The companion of the goal's operand (its achievement or maintenance target)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:guardSituation
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "guard situation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a conditional logic:GoalExpression to the logic:Situation type that guards it — the goal's target (its operand) applies only when the guard holds (via logic:situationObtains). Domain logic:GoalExpression, range logic:Situation (stated in prose). When the guard is false the conditional goal prescribes nothing: the evaluation reflects does-not-apply rather than asserting satisfied or violated."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:operand
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "operand"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a compositional logic:GoalExpression (conjunctive, disjunctive, conditional, or deadline-window) to one of its sub-expressions — multi-valued, so a conjunction or disjunction over several sub-goals is carried faithfully. Domain logic:GoalExpression, range logic:GoalExpression (stated in prose). For a conjunctive goal every operand must be satisfied; for a disjunctive goal any one suffices; a conditional or deadline-window goal carries its single guarded/windowed target as its operand."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:outcomeSituation
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "outcome situation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:Outcome (one branch of an action schema's nondeterministic outcome set) to the successor logic:Situation it reaches. Domain logic:Outcome, range logic:Situation (stated in prose). The branch's own logic:compensation recovers from this specific successor, so recovery is outcome-indexed rather than a single generic undo."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:situationObtains
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "situation obtains"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a gmeow:State (a configuration along a logic:Path) to a logic:Situation type that obtains at it — the engine reads this to decide whether an atomic goal's logic:boundSituationType, or a conditional goal's logic:guardSituation, holds at a given state. Domain gmeow:State, range logic:Situation (stated in prose). It records that a situation type is realized at a state without mutating that state, mirroring the prose 'each gmeow:State realizes a logic:Situation' on logic:Path."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:observation
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "observation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to what executing the action reveals — the seam to the cognitive layer (design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md). A plan whose next action is chosen from what an earlier action's observation reveals is a policy. Domain logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). One of the eight action-theory facets; a NEW facet, not a reuse of any cognition term."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:compensation
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "compensation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to the action that undoes this one — the basis for recoverable transactions. Tied to the realized outcome, not the schema as a whole: when the outcome set is nondeterministic each branch names the compensation that recovers from IT, so recovery matches what actually happened rather than applying one generic undo across every branch. Domain logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). One of the eight action-theory facets."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:actionResource
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "action resource"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to what the action consumes or requires — the seam to the resource-competing goal conflict (logic:competesForResource), where two goals draw on a resource an action schema declares and the supply is insufficient for both. Domain logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). One of the eight action-theory facets. DISTINCT from logic:resourcePolicy, which is a ReasoningContract→ResourcePolicy engine-budget property — a different concept that must not be conflated with an action's consumable resource."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

# --- Action-theory facet evaluation seams (stated in prose) -------------------
# The representation-level properties the native teleology evaluator reads to
# evaluate the effect, observation, and actionResource facets. Each is a pure
# data property over the given structure; none drives a real engine-lock.

logic:resourceSupply
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "resource supply"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a state to a resource it supplies, recording resource availability at that state for the logic:actionResource facet. The native evaluator gates an action whose required logic:actionResource a state does not supply (or that is flagged logic:resourceExhausted). Domain a state, range the supplied resource (stated in prose). This is the representation-level resource seam to logic:competesForResource — it evaluates the represented resource facet only and is NOT a real build engine-lock."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:resourceExhausted
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "resource exhausted"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A boolean marker on a resource that has been depleted: a resource flagged logic:resourceExhausted \"true\" is unavailable even where a state supplies it (logic:resourceSupply), so an action requiring it via logic:actionResource is gated. Domain a resource, range xsd:boolean (stated in prose). The depletion half of the representation-level resource facet, kept distinct from engine-budget exhaustion."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:reveals
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "reveals"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates the observation value an action schema names through logic:observation to the situation that executing the action reveals. The native evaluator surfaces the revealed situation in the materialized output so a policy can branch on it. Domain the logic:observation value, range the revealed logic:Situation (stated in prose). The reading half of the observation facet's seam to the cognitive layer (design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:planBranch
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "plan branch"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a plan to one of its observation-conditioned branches. A plan that carries logic:planBranch branches whose choice depends on what an earlier action's logic:observation reveals is a POLICY — a reading of a plan, not a separate class (see logic:Plan). Domain a plan, range a branch (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:branchObservation
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "branch observation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a policy branch to the observation value its selection is conditioned on — the observation whose logic:reveals decides whether this branch fires. Domain a policy branch, range the logic:observation value (stated in prose). What makes a plan's branching observation-conditioned rather than fixed in advance."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:branchGuard
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "branch guard"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a policy branch to the revealed situation that selects it: when the branch's logic:branchObservation reveals (logic:reveals) this situation, the branch is selected. Domain a policy branch, range the guarding logic:Situation (stated in prose). The guard the native evaluator matches against the observation's revealed situation."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:branchActionSchema
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "branch action schema"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a policy branch to the logic:ActionSchema it invokes when selected — the next action the policy takes for this observation. Domain a policy branch, range logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). The native evaluator surfaces it as logic:nextActionSchema on the policy when the branch's logic:branchGuard matches the observation."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:selectedBranch
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "selected branch"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a policy to the branch the native evaluator selected because its logic:branchGuard matched the situation an earlier action's observation revealed (logic:reveals). Domain a policy, range the selected branch (stated in prose). The materialized record of an observation-conditioned policy decision."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:nextActionSchema
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "next action schema"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a policy to the logic:ActionSchema its selected branch invokes — the next action chosen from what an observation revealed. Domain a policy, range logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). Surfaced by the native evaluator alongside logic:selectedBranch so a policy reading is possible from the materialized output."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:GateProbe
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Gate Probe"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A node pairing a logic:ActionSchema (via logic:probesSchema) with the state (via logic:probesState) the action-gate verdict is computed against, plus the capabilities the state makes available (logic:capabilityAvailable). The native evaluator emits a logic:gateVerdict — logic:GateAdmitted or logic:GateDenied — surfacing the precondition, capability, invariant-breach, and resource-exhaustion gates as recorded findings rather than silent passes."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:probesSchema
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "probes schema"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:GateProbe to the logic:ActionSchema it gates. Domain logic:GateProbe, range logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:probesState
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "probes state"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:GateProbe to the state the schema is gated against — the state whose logic:situationObtains and logic:resourceSupply facts the gate reads. Domain logic:GateProbe, range a state (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:capabilityAvailable
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "capability available"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a state to a capability the actor holds at it — the executional capability the gate matches an action schema's logic:capability against. Domain a state, range the available capability (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:gateVerdict
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "gate verdict"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:GateProbe to its action-gate verdict, one of logic:GateAdmitted or logic:GateDenied. Domain logic:GateProbe (stated in prose). The materialized verdict of the precondition / capability / invariant / resource gate."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:gateDenialReason
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "gate denial reason"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A human-readable reason on a denied logic:GateProbe naming the failing gate — the unmet precondition, the unavailable capability, the breached invariant, or the unavailable resource. Domain logic:GateProbe, range a string literal (stated in prose). A breach is a surfaced verdict, never a silent pass."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:gateCompensation
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "gate compensation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a denied logic:GateProbe to the logic:compensation (rollback) the schema would run on denial. Domain logic:GateProbe, range the compensation action (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:GateAdmitted
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Gate Admitted"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:gateVerdict value for an action the gate admits: every precondition holds, every capability is available, every invariant is preserved, and every required resource is available."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:GateDenied
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Gate Denied"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:gateVerdict value for an action the gate denies: a precondition, capability, invariant, or resource gate failed. The probe carries a logic:gateDenialReason naming the failing gate and, when declared, the logic:gateCompensation rollback."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:TransactionStep
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Transaction Step"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An elementary update / transaction-path step that instantiates an action schema (logic:instantiatesSchema) and carries the path edge from a predecessor state (logic:transitionFromState) to a successor state (logic:transitionToState). The native evaluator applies the schema's logic:effect over the step, computing the successor situation's support as ins/del supersession: inserted supports become active, deleted supports are recorded via the append-only supersession quartet (logic:activeInState, logic:validUntilState, logic:retiredByTransaction, logic:supersededBy) and never erased."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

# --- Goal / occurrence links --------------------------------------------------

logic:hasGoalCondition
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "has goal condition"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a gmeow:Goal to the logic:GoalExpression carrying the compositional structure of its target. Domain gmeow:Goal, range logic:GoalExpression (stated in prose, matching the module's domain/range convention). The flat gmeow:hasGoal and conclusive gmeow:satisfiedBy edges are the surface views this richer condition generates; gmeow:intentionGoal stays functional and ranges over gmeow:Goal — goal structure lives on the goal through this property, leaving the functional edge untouched."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:planGoal
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "plan goal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:Plan to the gmeow:Goal that is its success criterion — the goal the plan's steps, invoking action schemas, are arranged to reach. Domain logic:Plan, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). The plan's success against this goal is quantified over nondeterministic outcomes through logic:planSuccessMode."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:instantiatesSchema
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "instantiates schema"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a gmeow:Event (an action occurrence — a particular event executed along a particular path) to the logic:ActionSchema it instantiates. Domain gmeow:Event, range logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). The occurrence is the same perdurant an intentional moment links to through gmeow:motivates; the schema is the reusable type it instantiates. The schema names what an action does; the path records that it was done and what changed."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

# --- Goal decomposition (gmeow:Goal -> gmeow:Goal, satisfaction dependency) ----

logic:refinesGoal
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "refines goal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a sub-gmeow:Goal to a coarser gmeow:Goal it makes precise. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of the four decomposition relations carrying satisfaction dependency, typed apart from gmeow:properPartOf (structural part-hood): a sub-goal may be both a proper part and refine its parent, yet part-hood alone does not express the refinement."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:contributesTo
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "contributes to"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a sub-gmeow:Goal whose satisfaction advances a gmeow:Goal without settling it. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of the four decomposition relations carrying satisfaction dependency; weaker than logic:necessaryFor (required) and logic:sufficientFor (settles on its own), and distinct from gmeow:properPartOf, which carries only structural part-hood."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:necessaryFor
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "necessary for"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a sub-gmeow:Goal that must be satisfied for a gmeow:Goal to be satisfied. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). The relation an logic:AndDecomposition groups: all necessary sub-goals must hold together. One of the four decomposition relations carrying satisfaction dependency, typed apart from gmeow:properPartOf (structural part-hood) — the satisfaction dependency planning needs that part-hood alone does not express."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:sufficientFor
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "sufficient for"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a sub-gmeow:Goal whose satisfaction settles a gmeow:Goal on its own. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). The relation an logic:OrDecomposition groups: any one sufficient sub-goal settles the parent. One of the four decomposition relations carrying satisfaction dependency, distinct from gmeow:properPartOf (structural part-hood)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

# --- Goal conflict (gmeow:Goal -> gmeow:Goal; weaker than gmeow:counterGoal) ---

logic:contradictoryGoal
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "contradictory goal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates two gmeow:Goals in contradictory conflict: satisfying one entails violating the other in EVERY world. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of seven conflict relations between independently-meaningful goals, each WEAKER than gmeow:counterGoal — the strongest, constitutive opposition that partly defines what a goal means. A witnessed conflict is surfaced as a context-indexed finding, never silently resolved."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:contraryGoal
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "contrary goal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates two gmeow:Goals in contrary conflict: the two cannot both be satisfied, though both may fail. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of seven conflict relations between independently-meaningful goals, weaker than gmeow:counterGoal (constitutive opposition) and than logic:contradictoryGoal (which also forces one to be violated when the other is satisfied)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:preventsGoal
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "prevents goal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates two gmeow:Goals where achieving one closes the path to the other. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of seven conflict relations between independently-meaningful goals, weaker than gmeow:counterGoal (constitutive opposition). Distinct from logic:contradictoryGoal: prevention closes a path, it does not entail violation in every world."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:competesForResource
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "competes for resource"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates two gmeow:Goals that both draw on a resource an action schema declares (logic:actionResource), where the supply is insufficient for both. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). The seam between goal conflict and the action-theory resource facet. One of seven conflict relations between independently-meaningful goals, weaker than gmeow:counterGoal (constitutive opposition)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:temporallyIncompatible
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "temporally incompatible"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates two gmeow:Goals each achievable on its own but not within the windows both require. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of seven conflict relations between independently-meaningful goals, weaker than gmeow:counterGoal (constitutive opposition); the conflict is in the scheduling, not in the goals' content."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:deonticallyIncompatible
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "deontically incompatible"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates two gmeow:Goals whose conjunction a norm makes impermissible even where it is physically reachable. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of seven conflict relations between independently-meaningful goals, weaker than gmeow:counterGoal (constitutive opposition). Deontic force arrives with the norms vocabulary, which ranges over goals — the dependency points toward the goal layer, never the reverse."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:lowerPriorityUnderPolicy
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "lower priority under policy"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates two gmeow:Goals where, under a governing priority ordering established by an applicable policy, one goal is deprioritised in favour of the other — a conflict resolved by policy precedence rather than by logical, temporal, or deontic impossibility. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of seven conflict relations between independently-meaningful goals, weaker than gmeow:counterGoal (constitutive opposition). Distinct from logic:deonticallyIncompatible: the conjunction is not normatively impermissible — it is merely ranked lower by the policy ordering; and distinct from logic:competesForResource: the deprioritisation is a priority decision, not an exhaustion of supply."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

# --- GoalEvaluation axes, links, and quantities -------------------------------

logic:satisfactionStatus
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "satisfaction status"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the logic:SatisfactionStatus it carries — the satisfaction axis of the factored outcome. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation, range logic:SatisfactionStatus (stated in prose). Varies independently of feasibility, lifecycle, and goal-evaluation status."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:feasibilityStatus
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "feasibility status"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the logic:FeasibilityStatus it carries — the feasibility axis of the factored outcome. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation, range logic:FeasibilityStatus (stated in prose). Varies independently of satisfaction, lifecycle, and goal-evaluation status."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:lifecycleStatus
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "lifecycle status"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the logic:LifecycleStatus it carries — the lifecycle axis of the factored outcome. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation, range logic:LifecycleStatus (stated in prose). Varies independently of satisfaction, feasibility, and goal-evaluation status."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:goalEvaluationStatus
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "goal evaluation status"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the logic:GoalEvaluationStatus it carries — whether the evaluation is conclusive. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation, range logic:GoalEvaluationStatus (stated in prose). Together with satisfaction status logic:Satisfied, the value logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted is the condition under which a gmeow:satisfiedBy edge is generated. DISTINCT from logic:resultEvaluation, which carries the engine-computation logic:EvaluationStatus of a logic:ReasoningResult."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:goalExpressionKind
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "goal expression kind"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:GoalExpression to its logic:GoalExpressionKind — which of the nine compositional variants it is. Domain logic:GoalExpression, range logic:GoalExpressionKind (stated in prose). The engine reads this to dispatch the compositional evaluation."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:satisfactionDegree
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "satisfaction degree"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The quantity carried on a logic:GoalEvaluation for a goal met to a degree rather than crisply — how much of the goal is achieved. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose). The range is intentionally left open (no rdfs:range), matching the other quantitative axes (logic:confidence, logic:probability, logic:weight, logic:evidenceStrength): the value is a unit-interval decimal. DISTINCT from those uncertainty measures and from logic:objectiveValue and logic:utility — how much of the goal is met is never how sure the evaluator is, never the measure an optimization goal extremizes, and never how desirable the outcome is; none substitutes for another."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:objectiveValue
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "objective value"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The measured quantity an optimization goal extremizes, carried on a logic:GoalEvaluation. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose). The range is intentionally left open (no rdfs:range), matching the module's quantitative axes; its direction and unit/frame are carried by logic:objectiveDirection. NEVER folded into a truth value and never into an uncertainty measure — DISTINCT from logic:confidence, logic:probability, logic:weight, logic:evidenceStrength, from logic:satisfactionDegree, and from logic:utility. A probability over outcomes is never the objective value being optimized."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:objectiveDirection
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "objective direction"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates an optimization-goal logic:GoalEvaluation to the direction and unit/frame against which its logic:objectiveValue is read — whether the measure is to be maximized or minimized, and in what units the value is stated. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose); the range is left open so the direction/unit-frame may be carried as a structured value. The companion of logic:objectiveValue: a value without its direction and frame is uninterpretable."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:utility
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "utility"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The preference quantity carried on a logic:GoalEvaluation — how desirable an outcome is. The ONE preference term: utility and preference are one concept here, so no separate preference property is minted. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose). The range is intentionally left open (no rdfs:range), matching the module's quantitative axes. DISTINCT from the uncertainty measures (logic:confidence, logic:probability, logic:weight, logic:evidenceStrength) and from logic:satisfactionDegree and logic:objectiveValue — desirability is never sureness, never how much of the goal is met, and never the measure an optimization goal extremizes; none substitutes for another."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:evaluatesGoal
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "evaluates goal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the gmeow:Goal it judges. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of the subjects in the identifying tuple of an evaluation (goal, situation/world, evaluator, time, criterion)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:evaluatedAgainst
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "evaluated against"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the situation or world it is judged against. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose); the range ranges over a situation (logic:Situation) or a world/context, left open in this standalone module. One of the subjects in the identifying tuple of an evaluation."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:evaluationCriterion
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "evaluation criterion"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the criterion applied in reaching its judgment — the standard against which satisfaction, feasibility, and the quantities are read. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose). One of the subjects in the identifying tuple of an evaluation; two evaluations differing only in criterion are distinct records."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:evaluationTime
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "evaluation time"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:definition "The time of judgment component of the logic:GoalEvaluation identifying tuple: when this evaluation was made. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose); range xsd:dateTime (a full ISO-8601 instant, never xsd:date). Two evaluations of the same goal, situation, evaluator, and criterion made at different times are distinct records. When no explicit time is recorded the identifying tuple component is absent, not defaulted — absence means the time of judgment is unspecified rather than unknown."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:evaluationEvaluator
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "evaluation evaluator"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the vantage holding the judgment — the evaluator the record is attributed to. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose). Aligns with gmeow:accordingTo: a goal evaluation is a vantage-indexed claim, never a global verdict, so two evaluators who disagree are two coexisting evaluations rather than one elected winner (Principle 9). One of the subjects in the identifying tuple of an evaluation."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:planSuccessMode
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "plan success mode"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:Plan to the logic:PlanSuccessMode quantifying its success over the nondeterministic outcomes of its action schemas. Domain logic:Plan, range logic:PlanSuccessMode (stated in prose). The quantification exists because the bare executional-success reading of the transaction layer would count one favourable path as success; this declares whether some, every, or every fair execution must reach the goal."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:planFlowEdge
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "plan flow edge"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:Plan to a reified flow edge (logic:ControlFlowEdge or logic:DataFlowEdge) that constitutes its FLOW-GRAPH — the binary-edge form the DAG-workflow acyclicity certifier runs Tarjan SCC over, each edge mediating a source (logic:flowFrom) and a target (logic:flowTo) process node. MULTI-valued: a plan gathers all the control-flow and dataflow edges of its process graph. The canonical-plan counterpart of the build pipeline's gmeow:hasStage stage-membership — where a pipeline gathers gmeow:PipelineStage members whose gmeow:dataflowConsumes edges form its graph, a logic:Plan gathers its reified flow edges directly — so a plan's flow graph is reachable from the plan rather than left as free-standing edges. A plan whose planFlowEdge closure is acyclic is certified logic:CompleteForFragment under logic:DagWorkflowResource; a cyclic closure resolves to the `unsupported` verdict (logic:EvaluationUnsupported) with the offending members disclosed by logic:dagCycleWitness, never silently truncated. Domain logic:Plan, range logic:ControlFlowEdge or logic:DataFlowEdge (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:planBody
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "plan body"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:Plan to the ROOT node of its program TREE — the structured-program form an interpreter walks, distinct from logic:planFlowEdge, which gathers the binary-edge FLOW-GRAPH form the Tarjan acyclicity certifier runs over. The root is normally a transaction-program combinator (logic:SerialConjunction, logic:Choice, logic:ConcurrentComposition, logic:Fallback, or logic:Iteration), but a single-step plan roots directly at a logic:ActionSchema leaf — no synthetic wrapper combinator is required. Single-valued: a plan has one program root, from which the whole tree is reachable through logic:leftOperand / logic:rightOperand / logic:iterationBody / logic:iterationCondition. A plan whose program tree carries a logic:Iteration loop is OUTSIDE the certified acyclic DAG fragment by construction — the loop is legitimate canonical program structure, not a well-formedness defect — so such a plan does NOT run logic:executedUnderContract the DAG-workflow profile. Domain logic:Plan, range a transaction-program combinator node OR a logic:ActionSchema leaf (stated in prose, matching the module's domain/range convention)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:planCertification
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "plan certification"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:Plan to the logic:ReasoningResult recording its DAG-workflow certification verdict — the result the acyclicity certifier emits when the plan runs logic:executedUnderContract a contract requesting logic:DagWorkflowResource. The result carries logic:resultEvaluation (logic:EvaluationCompleted on an acyclic plan, logic:EvaluationUnsupported on a cyclic one) and logic:resultCompleteness (logic:CompleteForFragment when certified), and on a cyclic plan it discloses the offending cycle members through logic:dagCycleWitness — so the `unsupported` verdict and its witness are reachable from the plan rather than computed and discarded. Domain logic:Plan, range logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose). The plan stays valid canonically under a non-DAG contract; this link records only what the DAG profile certified over it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:activationBasis
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:GovernanceRegime ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "activation basis"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:GovernanceRegime to a constrained state it activates as binding: the regime holds that a logic:DownwardConstraint whose logic:constraintState is this value binds its target (logic:ConstraintBinding) rather than lapsing to logic:ConstraintUnknown. The carrier that makes governance regime-relative — a state in one regime's activation basis and absent from another's receives opposite verdicts with no contradiction. Without a matching basis entry, a constraint over that state is logic:ConstraintUnknown under the regime. The governance analogue of logic:reductionBasis (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:admissibleValuation
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "admissible valuation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy it selects — the gap/glut policy fixing which Belnap values a valuation may assign. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy (stated here in prose, matching the module's domain/range convention). It is one of the three independent truth-facet components and must not be conflated with logic:designatedValues."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:agencyHolon
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:AgencyAssessment ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "agency holon"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The holon role of an logic:AgencyAssessment: the entity whose Janus-faced holonic agency is being assessed — the holon that bears (logic:bearsProperty) the self-assertive and integrative values the profile reasons over. One of the two role properties (with logic:agencyProfile) that reify the agency-assessment relation onto the arity-bounded reasoning surface, mirroring logic:assessmentWhole and the logic:HolonicPosition role properties. It is also a well-formedness existence guard: every verdict rule re-binds it, so a malformed assessment naming no holon receives no verdict (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:agencyProfile
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:AgencyAssessment ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "agency profile"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range logic:HolonicAgencyProfile ;
    skos:definition "The profile role of an logic:AgencyAssessment: the logic:HolonicAgencyProfile the assessment is relative to. Holonic agency is never absolute — the verdict (logic:HolonIntegral / logic:AutonomyDeficient / logic:IntegrationDeficient / logic:AgencyUnknown) is read only against this declared profile's logic:selfAssertiveBasis and logic:integrativeBasis. An assessment that omits this role, or whose profile declares no basis at all, cannot evidence either tendency and receives logic:AgencyUnknown. One of the two role properties (with logic:agencyHolon) that reify the agency-assessment relation, mirroring logic:assessmentReductionTheory and logic:constraintRegime (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:agencyVerdict
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:AgencyAssessment ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "agency verdict"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range logic:AgencyVerdict ;
    skos:definition "The engine-derived outcome of an logic:AgencyAssessment: the four-valued logic:AgencyVerdict (logic:HolonIntegral, logic:AutonomyDeficient, logic:IntegrationDeficient, or logic:AgencyUnknown) the foundation lowering entails for it. Never asserted by hand — it is computed by the stratified agency rules from the assessment's holon and declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile, the convenient OWL-projectable surface of the assessment exactly as logic:assessmentVerdict is for emergence and logic:constraintVerdict for governance. The two pathology values are reached by negation-as-failure over the two co-equal tendency markers, so each verdict is genuinely profile-relative rather than a bare default (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:argumentation
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "argumentation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:ArgumentationSemantics it selects — how conflicts among defeasible arguments are resolved. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ArgumentationSemantics (stated in prose, matching the module's domain/range convention)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:assessmentProperty
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:EmergenceAssessment ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "assessment property"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The property role of an logic:EmergenceAssessment: the property-value whose emergence is being assessed — the thing the whole bears (logic:bearsProperty) and whose reducibility to the parts is in question. One of the three role properties (with logic:assessmentWhole and logic:assessmentReductionTheory) that reify the emergence-assessment relation onto the arity-bounded reasoning surface, mirroring the logic:HolonicPosition role properties (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:assessmentReductionTheory
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:EmergenceAssessment ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "assessment reduction theory"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range logic:ReductionTheory ;
    skos:definition "The theory role of an logic:EmergenceAssessment: the logic:ReductionTheory the assessment is relative to. Emergence is never absolute — the verdict (logic:Aggregate / logic:Emergent / logic:EmergenceUnknown) is read only against this declared theory's logic:reductionBasis, and recording it is what lets a stronger theory overturn an logic:Emergent verdict without contradiction. An assessment that omits this role cannot pose the reducibility question and receives logic:EmergenceUnknown. One of the three role properties (with logic:assessmentWhole and logic:assessmentProperty) that reify the emergence-assessment relation (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:assessmentVerdict
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:EmergenceAssessment ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "assessment verdict"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range logic:EmergenceVerdict ;
    skos:definition "The derived outcome of an logic:EmergenceAssessment: the logic:EmergenceVerdict (logic:Aggregate, logic:Emergent, or logic:EmergenceUnknown) the foundation lowering entails for it. Never asserted by hand — it is computed by the stratified emergence rules from the assessment's whole, property, and declared logic:ReductionTheory, the convenient OWL-projectable surface of the assessment exactly as logic:isHolon projects holon-ness. logic:Emergent is reached by negation-as-failure over the aggregate derivation, so the verdict is genuinely theory-relative rather than a bare 'unflagged' default (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:assessmentWhole
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:EmergenceAssessment ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "assessment whole"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The whole role of an logic:EmergenceAssessment: the entity whose property is being assessed for emergence — the whole that bears the property and stands over the proper parts the reduction is attempted from. One of the three role properties (with logic:assessmentProperty and logic:assessmentReductionTheory) that reify the emergence-assessment relation onto the arity-bounded reasoning surface, mirroring the logic:HolonicPosition role properties (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:asymmetricProperty
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "asymmetric property"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic: property-characteristic marker for asymmetry: a property P such that P(a,b) entails ¬P(b,a). The logic: analogue of owl:AsymmetricProperty, minted standalone so it can co-occur with logic:transitiveProperty on the same property — the transitive ∧ asymmetric combination OWL 2 DL bars for decidability but logic: keeps and reasons over (criticism 7)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:bearsProperty
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "bears property"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates an entity to a property-value it carries, for the purpose of the emergence calculus: a whole and its proper parts each bearsProperty the values an logic:EmergenceAssessment reasons over. A deliberately thin logic-layer relation — NOT a metaphysical inherence claim; the bearer relation for logic:Modes and dispositions is asserted with their own domain properties (Principle 5), and gufo:inheresIn is never asserted. Whether a borne whole property reduces to the parts that bear it is exactly what logic:EmergenceAssessment decides; crucially, no rule propagates bearsProperty down logic:properPartOf, so an logic:Emergent whole property never reaches its parts (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:builtinArithmetic
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:Builtin ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "arithmetic builtin"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The native basic-math builtin: derives a value by the arithmetic operations (add, subtract, multiply, divide, compare) over numeric arguments. A derivational builtin (Principle 12, in-logic): the lightweight math a foundation needs, NOT heavy numerical domain computation (n-dimensional vector operations, SLAM, trajectory updates), which stays external by reference. Gated to logic:ProceduralPrologProfile; execution is seamed to the engine."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .

logic:builtinDateDifference
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:Builtin ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "date-difference builtin"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The native date-arithmetic builtin: derives the difference between two dates, e.g. legalAge = year(now) − year(birth). A derivational builtin (Principle 12, in-logic): the lightweight date arithmetic a foundation needs, NOT heavy temporal-domain computation (calendar/datum transforms), which stays external by reference. Gated to logic:ProceduralPrologProfile; execution is seamed to the engine."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .

logic:builtinStringConcat
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:Builtin ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "string-concat builtin"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The native string-concatenation builtin: derives a string by joining its arguments, e.g. fullName = firstName + \" \" + lastName. A derivational builtin (Principle 12, in-logic): the lightweight string derivation a foundation needs, NOT heavy domain text processing, which stays external by reference. Gated to logic:ProceduralPrologProfile; execution is seamed to the engine."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .

logic:causalPartOf
    a owl:ObjectProperty ,
        logic:transitiveProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "causal part of"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Causal parthood among perdurants: relates a sub-occurrent that causally contributes to a larger occurrent — the ignition is a causal part of the launch, the infection a causal part of the illness. A specialization of logic:temporalPartOf (stated in prose, not as an rdfs:subPropertyOf edge, matching how the foundation parthood relations are authored): every causal part is also a temporal part of the same whole, but NOT conversely — a merely temporally-nested sub-occurrent need carry no causal contribution (causal subset-of temporal, the YAMATO/Galton occurrent-mereology refinement). Transitive (a causal part of a causal part causally contributes to the whole) but deliberately NOT asymmetric or irreflexive, since causal feedback loops are legal among occurrents — contrast logic:properPartOf, the strict-order endurant parthood. Distinct from the temporal-only nesting carried at the domain level by gmeow:subEventOf."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:closedUnder
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "closed under"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Declares a predicate or shape closed within a logic:WorldBoundary: the closed-world-assumption toggle that says, for the named predicate inside the boundary, that the materialized extension is complete and absence may be read as falsity. The per-predicate CWA switch of the hybrid open/closed construct, enforced by the built-in SHACL (the CWA lane); outside any boundary, or for predicates not closed under one, the open-world reading holds. Enforcement is seamed to the engine."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:closureEntry
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "closure entry"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to a logic:ClosureEntry — a per-key override of the closure map binding a predicate or context key to an open- or closed-world value. The closure facet is a map, not a global flag: logic:defaultClosure gives the default for unlisted keys, while each logic:closureEntry overrides one key. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ClosureEntry (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:closureKey
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "closure key"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ClosureEntry to the predicate-or-context key it scopes: the string key whose closure value the entry fixes. Domain logic:ClosureEntry (stated in prose, matching the module's convention); range xsd:string. The key together with logic:closureValue forms one binding of the closure map."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:closureValue
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "closure value"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ClosureEntry to the logic:ClosureValue (open- or closed-world) it assigns to its key. Domain logic:ClosureEntry, range logic:ClosureValue (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). Together with logic:closureKey it forms one binding of the closure map."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:complexityClass
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "complexity class"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The complexity / decidability class a projection or profile certifies — EL → PTIME, DL → decidable/N2EXPTIME, Datalog → terminating/PTIME-data — recorded alongside the preservation polarity in the loss ledger. Decidability is a projection guarantee bought by projecting down, not a canonical-layer promise: the canonical layer is maximally expressive and only semi-decidable."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:confidence
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "confidence"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Epistemic confidence assigned to a statement by a source or process — how sure the asserter is. Normatively distinct from logic:probability: a confidence score is NOT a probability and MUST NOT be interpreted as one unless an explicit mapping to logic:probability is declared. Also distinct from logic:weight (a solver ranking) and logic:evidenceStrength (evidential warrant)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:constraintOverride
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:DownwardConstraint ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "constraint override"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The override role of a logic:DownwardConstraint: the declared exception token whose presence on the constrained target defeats the constraint. When the target bears this token (logic:bearsProperty), the constraint receives logic:ConstraintOverridden rather than logic:ConstraintBinding — a structured, declared escape hatch, not an ad-hoc one. An override quiets a governing limit; it never unmakes the part (constraint, not causation). One of the role properties that reify the downward-constraint relation onto the arity-bounded reasoning surface (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:constraintRegime
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:DownwardConstraint ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "constraint regime"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range logic:GovernanceRegime ;
    skos:definition "The regime role of a logic:DownwardConstraint: the logic:GovernanceRegime the constraint is relative to. Governance is never absolute — the verdict (logic:ConstraintBinding / logic:ConstraintOverridden / logic:ConstraintUnknown) is read only against this declared regime's logic:activationBasis, and recording it is what lets a different regime quiet a binding without contradiction. A constraint that omits this role, or whose constrained state is not in the regime's basis, cannot be shown to bind and receives logic:ConstraintUnknown. One of the role properties (with logic:constraintWhole, logic:constraintTarget, logic:constraintState, and logic:constraintOverride) that reify the downward-constraint relation, mirroring logic:assessmentReductionTheory (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:constraintState
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:DownwardConstraint ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "constraint state"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:seeAlso gmeow:Goal ;
    skos:definition "The constrained-state role of a logic:DownwardConstraint: the permissible role or state the governing whole limits on the target part — what the part may be or do within the whole. This is typically the part's functional role or gmeow:Goal set in the context of its super-whole: a part's teleological role is fixed relative to the holon it serves, which is exactly the downward face of holonic governance (cf. gmeow:Goal in the teleology slice, linked via rdfs:seeAlso). A constraint binds this state only when the declared logic:GovernanceRegime activates it (logic:activationBasis). One of the role properties that reify the downward-constraint relation onto the arity-bounded reasoning surface (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:constraintTarget
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:DownwardConstraint ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "constraint target"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The target role of a logic:DownwardConstraint: the proper part the governing whole constrains — the part whose permissible state is limited. The verdict is derived only for this explicitly named target; because the constraint names its target rather than cascading down logic:properPartOf, governance is NON-TRANSITIVE by default (ME9) — a constraint onto a part says nothing automatic about the part's own sub-parts. One of the role properties (with logic:constraintWhole) that reify the downward-constraint relation, mirroring logic:assessmentWhole (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:constraintVerdict
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:DownwardConstraint ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "constraint verdict"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range logic:ConstraintVerdict ;
    skos:definition "The engine-derived outcome of a logic:DownwardConstraint: the tri-valued logic:ConstraintVerdict (logic:ConstraintBinding, logic:ConstraintOverridden, or logic:ConstraintUnknown) the reasoner computes for the constraint from its role properties, the holarchy, and the declared logic:GovernanceRegime. Never asserted by hand — it is what the stratified downward-constraint rules conclude — mirroring logic:assessmentVerdict for emergence (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:constraintWhole
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:DownwardConstraint ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "constraint whole"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The governing-whole role of a logic:DownwardConstraint: the enclosing holon that imposes the constraint — the whole over the proper part named by logic:constraintTarget. The whole bounds the part's permissible state but does not produce it (constraint, not causation). One of the role properties (with logic:constraintTarget, logic:constraintState, logic:constraintRegime, and logic:constraintOverride) that reify the downward-constraint relation, mirroring logic:assessmentWhole and the logic:HolonicPosition role properties (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:contextAxis
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "context axis"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to a logic:ContextAxis its results are indexed by. The context facet is multi-dimensional, so a contract may carry several logic:contextAxis values (world, standpoint, time, path) that coexist on one result rather than being alternative values of one slot. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ContextAxis (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:correlates
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:DependencyModel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "correlates"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:DependencyModel to a logic:probability-annotated fact (the reified base triple) that participates in the model's explicit joint distribution. The set of correlated facts is the support over which logic:jointOutcome enumerates joint assignments; any logic:probability fact NOT correlated by the model is treated as independent. The range is intentionally left open (no rdfs:range): a correlated fact is a reified logic:probability statement, which carries no dedicated class in this standalone module."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:counterfactualOf
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "counterfactual of"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a constructed counterfactual world to the base world it minimally revises: the surface for Lewis/Stalnaker counterfactuals, where the antecedent-world is computed by a revision rule rather than asserted and its contents must not leak into the base graph. Closeness is declared data (a generalized sharpening poset), not a fixed semantics; under the default Deterministic Revision Profile a declared entrenchment ordering yields a single revised world, and a genuine tie returns unknown rather than branching."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:defaultClosure
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "default closure"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:ClosureValue that is the default of its closure map — the open- or closed-world reading applied to any predicate or context key not overridden by a logic:closureEntry. The closure facet is a map; this is its default, normally open-world, with closed-world confined to keys inside a logic:WorldBoundary. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ClosureValue (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:designatedValues
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "designated values"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:DesignatedValueSet it selects — which truth values count as holding for consequence. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:DesignatedValueSet (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). One of the three independent truth-facet components; it must not be conflated with logic:admissibleValuation, since FDE and LP share a designated set and differ only in their admissible valuations."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:dischargeObligation
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "discharge obligation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates an individual to an anti-rigid type it instantiates contingently, carrying the standing obligation to construct or cite a world of existence in which the individual lacks that type (the anti-rigidity witness). The instance-level diagnostic the anti-rigidity lowering emits under the witness-obligation policy (the default; LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md §Anti-rigidity needs a witness policy): for an individual x typed by an anti-rigid Role or Phase T in a world, a logic:dischargeObligation fact is entailed in that world. It is an obligation, NOT a violation — anti-rigid instantiation is licensed on the promise that the counter-world is satisfiable on demand (its construction happens on demand); the lighter schema-only policy emits nothing instance-level, the stricter witness-required policy emits logic:witnessRequiredViolation instead. Like the other derived diagnostics it is never asserted by hand."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:disjoint
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "disjoint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Mereological disjointness: two entities share no part — the negation of logic:overlaps. A primitive notion of profiled mereology, settled (alongside logic:overlaps) before weak supplementation is stated, so logic:WeakSupplementation is never applied to wholes for which overlap is undefined. The 'another part disjoint from the first' clause of weak supplementation is read against this relation (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:distinctBody
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Inequality body guard of a logic:Rule. Default-absent: a rule that needs no inequality carries no logic:distinctBody, so the existing corpus is byte-identical."@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "distinct body"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:Rule to an inequality body guard: a reified node carrying rdf:subject and rdf:object (two rule variables, and — unlike logic:body — no rdf:predicate) that must bind to DISTINCT values for the rule to fire, projecting to the Datalog/Nemo inequality constraint ?A != ?B. Parallel to logic:negatedBody as an additive rule-structural surface: it lets a rule detect 'at least two distinct values' (e.g. a class carrying more than one stereotype, or a relator mediating two distinct relata) that set-semantic Datalog cannot otherwise express. An inequality guard introduces no negative dependency edge, so it leaves a rule's stratification class unchanged."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:equalityPolicy
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "equality policy"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:EqualityPolicy it selects — when two terms denote one entity. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:EqualityPolicy (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:evidenceStrength
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "evidence strength"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Evidential support for a statement, provenance-derived and reusing the evidence-slice warrant axes (source tier, evidence class): how well-warranted a claim is by its evidence. Normatively distinct from logic:probability, logic:confidence, and logic:weight — an evidential warrant is not a calibrated probability, an asserter's confidence, or a solver ranking, and is not interchangeable with any of them."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:evolution
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "evolution"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:EvolutionMode it selects — whether and how state changes. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:EvolutionMode (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). Evolution is independent of the model-semantics facet, which is why state-change reasoning (logic:TransactionPathEvolution) is a facet value, never a parallel profile."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:executedUnderContract
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "executed under contract"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a transaction-program node — a transaction-program combinator root (logic:SerialConjunction, logic:Choice, logic:Fallback, or logic:Iteration) marked executable by logic:transitionFromState — to the logic:ReasoningContract it executes under, whose logic:executionMode selects whether the program's effects are committed (logic:CommittedExecution, the default) or discarded (logic:HypotheticalExecution, the sandbox operator). This is the link by which a program reaches the execution-commitment facet: without it the contract-level logic:executionMode could not select commit-versus-discard for a concrete run. Single-valued — a program names at most one governing contract; absence resolves to the default committed execution. Domain a transaction-program node, range logic:ReasoningContract (stated in prose, matching the module's domain/range convention)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:executionMode
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "execution mode"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:ExecutionMode it selects — whether transaction effects are committed (logic:CommittedExecution, the default) or discarded (logic:HypotheticalExecution, the sandbox operator). Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ExecutionMode (stated in prose, matching the module's domain/range convention). Independent of logic:evolution: a hypothetical run may compose with any evolution mode. This facet carries the sandbox operator, which is distinct from modal possibility — modal possibility is computed as the standard translation over the appropriate typed accessibility relation (logic:epistemicallyPossible / logic:doxasticallyAccessible), never over the bare logic:accessibleFrom superproperty and never reified as a possibility class."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:expandsToFacet
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "expands to facet"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Links a logic:ReasoningPreset to a facet value it expands to. A preset's full facet selection is the set of its logic:expandsToFacet values plus any facet-specific properties; the compiler expands the preset to this bundle before reasoning, so a preset reference and its expanded facet set are interchangeable. Domain logic:ReasoningPreset (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:formulaFragment
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "formula fragment"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:FormulaFragment it selects — the syntactic class of admitted formulae. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:FormulaFragment (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:hasHolonicPosition
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "has holonic position"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The derived marker that an entity occupies at least one logic:HolonicPosition within a holarchy. Never asserted by hand; it is entailed by the foundation lowering, settling in stratum 1 the moment any logic:positionEntity reifier names the entity. It is the negation-as-failure target that arms the logic:HolonicLevelIncoherence rule (a profiled holon occupying NO position is incoherent), and the positive companion to logic:multiplyPositioned (which fires when an entity occupies SEVERAL distinct positions). It tracks compositional positioning only and is orthogonal to the HiLog logic:orderedType instantiation tower — the two axes never feed one another."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:holonicLevel
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:HolonicPosition ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "holonic level"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    skos:definition "The compositional depth at which an entity sits within a holarchy, measured along one path: how many proper-part steps lie between the entity and a root whole. It is a literal read off a logic:HolonicPosition (hence rdfs:domain logic:HolonicPosition), never an intrinsic attribute of the entity — holarchies are DAGs, so an entity has no single global level; two paths may place the same entity at different depths and both are correct, and the level is therefore recorded per position (per path). The per-entity min/max band across an entity's positions is materialized separately as logic:holonicLevelMin and logic:holonicLevelMax. Distinct from logic:orderedType: logic:orderedType is the HiLog deep-instantiation order (an order-n type instantiates an order-(n+1) type), a property of the instantiation tower, whereas logic:holonicLevel is mereological compositional depth in a whole/part DAG; the two must not be conflated (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:holonicLevelMax
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "holonic level max"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    skos:definition "The deepest of the logic:holonicLevel values an entity carries across all the logic:HolonicPositions it occupies within a holarchy — the upper endpoint of the path-relative depth band. Because holarchies are DAGs, a single intrinsic level is ill-defined, so the band (min..max) is stored instead of one value. NOTE — honest scope: this endpoint is operator-asserted, NOT engine-verified. The all-IRI logic:StratifiedNAFProfile foundation chase cannot compare or aggregate the integer literals, so it cannot derive or check that this value is the true maximum of the borne per-position levels; the engine grounds only that a non-trivial band exists, via the derived marker logic:multiplyPositioned (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:holonicLevelMin
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "holonic level min"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    skos:definition "The shallowest of the logic:holonicLevel values an entity carries across all the logic:HolonicPositions it occupies within a holarchy — the lower endpoint of the path-relative depth band. Because holarchies are DAGs, a single intrinsic level is ill-defined, so the band (min..max) is stored instead of one value. NOTE — honest scope: this endpoint is operator-asserted, NOT engine-verified. The all-IRI logic:StratifiedNAFProfile foundation chase cannot compare or aggregate the integer literals, so it cannot derive or check that this value is the true minimum of the borne per-position levels; the engine grounds only that a non-trivial band exists, via the derived marker logic:multiplyPositioned (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:instanceOf
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "instance of"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "HiLog deep instantiation: relates an individual or a type to a (possibly higher-order) type it instantiates, across any number of meta-levels. The first-class multi-level primitive that replaces OWL punning (criticism 5): types are reified as first-order individuals so 'an instance of a type that is itself an instance of a metatype' is ordinary first-order quantification rather than a punning trick. The general relation of which logic:suppliesIdentity is the identity-supplying specialization."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:integrativeBasis
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:HolonicAgencyProfile ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "integrative basis"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:HolonicAgencyProfile to a property-value that evidences the integrative tendency: the profile holds that a holon bearing this value (logic:bearsProperty) subordinates itself as a part to a larger whole — Koestler's integrative face. The carrier that makes integration profile-relative, the co-equal twin of logic:selfAssertiveBasis (neither privileged, Principle 9). Without a borne integrative value a holon's integration face is not evidenced, contributing — together with the self-assertive face — to the logic:AgencyVerdict (logic:IntegrationDeficient or logic:HolonIntegral). The integration analogue of logic:reductionBasis and logic:activationBasis (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:invokesBuiltin
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "invokes builtin"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:Rule to a logic:Builtin it calls in its body: the dependency edge recording that a rule uses a native computational primitive, and therefore requires logic:ProceduralPrologProfile (where builtins are gated). Lets the compiler check that a rule invoking a builtin declares the procedural profile and records the loss when such a rule is projected to a declarative semantics."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:invokesPathShape
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:PathInvocation ;
    rdfs:range logic:PathShape ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "invokes path shape"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:PathInvocation to the logic:PathShape it applies by name: the dependency edge recording which reusable traversal a parametric call instantiates. Paired with logic:pathDepthArg, which supplies the concrete bound for the shape's logic:pathDepthParam."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:irreflexiveProperty
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "irreflexive property"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic: property-characteristic marker for irreflexivity: a property P such that P(a,a) holds for no a. The logic: analogue of owl:IrreflexiveProperty, used together with logic:transitiveProperty and logic:asymmetricProperty to make logic:properPartOf a genuine strict partial order (criticism 7)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:isHolon
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "is holon"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The derived marker that projects holon-ness onto an entity: it holds of an entity that, within a holarchy, is simultaneously a proper part of some whole and itself has a proper part. It is the reasoning-surface marker (mirroring logic:isClass-style stereotype markers) from which the unary logic:Holon class is the OWL projection; the faithful construct is the relational logic:HolonicPosition, of which both are lossy projections. Never asserted by hand; it is entailed by the foundation lowering."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:jointOutcome
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:DependencyModel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "joint outcome"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range logic:JointOutcome ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:DependencyModel to one logic:JointOutcome of its explicit joint table. The outcomes a model declares must be mutually exclusive and exhaustive over the assignments to its logic:correlates set, and their logic:jointProbability values must sum to one."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:jointProbability
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:JointOutcome ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "joint probability"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The probability mass a logic:DependencyModel assigns to one logic:JointOutcome — the joint probability of that exact assignment of truth values to the model's correlated facts. Distinct from logic:probability (a per-fact marginal): the joint outcomes of a model partition its correlated sample space and their logic:jointProbability values sum to one. The range is intentionally left open (no rdfs:range), matching the other quantitative axes (logic:probability, logic:confidence, logic:weight, logic:evidenceStrength), which this standalone module declares without an xsd range: the value is a unit-interval decimal."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:loadBearing
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "load bearing"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    skos:definition "Types an annotation as load-bearing (true) or droppable (false, the default). A droppable annotation — a display hint or scope note — must never carry correctness: dropping it only pessimizes a result, so a lowering may drop it silently. A load-bearing annotation — an in-band complement or a quantitative axis — is needed by the inverse leg for put after get to equal the identity, so a lowering must either preserve it or record its loss in the ledger. Without this bit a section / retraction (perfect-subsumption) claim cannot be verified, which is why it is part of the node from the start."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:mediates
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "mediates"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a Relator to one of the entities it connects: the relationship between an objectified relation and each of its relata, on which the Relator existentially depends. A Relator must mediate at least two distinct entities (the relator-mediation discipline, RelComp); the material relation the Relator grounds holds in virtue of these mediation links."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:memberOf
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "member of"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The member-collection relation: relates a member to a logic:Collection it belongs to, where the members are the relevant units of the whole. Distinct from logic:partOf and logic:properPartOf: collection membership is not mereological parthood — a team member is a member of, not a proper part of, the team, and membership does not inherit parthood's transitivity through the collection."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:modelSemantics
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "model semantics"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:ModelSemantics it selects — which models are authoritative. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ModelSemantics (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). Probabilistic reasoning is never a value here — graded belief is carried on logic:uncertaintyMeasure alongside whatever model semantics is in force."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:multiplyPositioned
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "multiply positioned"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The derived marker that an entity occupies two or more distinct logic:HolonicPositions — the structural signature of a DAG node sitting on multiple paths through a holarchy, the ground on which a non-trivial path-relative depth band (logic:holonicLevelMin .. logic:holonicLevelMax) exists. It is the positive companion to logic:HolonicLevelIncoherence: where the incoherence violation fires for a profiled holon that occupies NO position, this marker certifies that a holon occupies SEVERAL, so its level is genuinely path-relative rather than single-valued. Never asserted by hand; it is entailed by the foundation lowering by negation-of-equality over the position set (two distinct positionEntity reifiers for the same entity), all-IRI and without any numeric comparison. It grounds only the band's existence, not its endpoint values, which the logic:StratifiedNAFProfile chase cannot compute (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:negatedBody
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Negation-as-failure body atom of a logic:Rule. Default-absent: a positive Horn rule has only logic:body atoms and no logic:negatedBody, so the existing positive corpus is unaffected."@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "negated body"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:Rule to a negated (negation-as-failure) body atom: the antecedent literal that must NOT be derivable for the rule to fire. Parallel to logic:body (the positive antecedent atoms) but read under closed-world negation, so a rule with any logic:negatedBody atom requires at least logic:StratifiedNAFProfile rather than logic:PositiveHornProfile. The atom itself is a reified rdf:subject/rdf:predicate/rdf:object triple exactly as for logic:body; only its polarity differs."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:negationOperator
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "negation operator"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to a logic:NegationOperator its programs may use. Set-valued on the contract: a program may legitimately use explicit (strong) negation and negation-as-failure together, so this records the permitted operator set, not a single chosen operator. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:NegationOperator (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:occurrentBoundary
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:range logic:OccurrentBoundary ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "occurrent boundary"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a perdurant to its boundary value — logic:Open (an on-going action, an open temporal interval: the arriving) or logic:Closed (a completed unitary event, a closed interval: the arrival). The action(open)/event(closed) typing of the YAMATO/Galton refinement, carried as a VALUE rather than a subclass (Principle 9): the same occurrence is open while it unfolds and closed once whole, so boundedness is an indexed value, not a rigid kind. The formal name for the prescriptive-to-descriptive seam — an open action is the doing, the closed event its done record. An occurrent bearing both logic:Open and logic:Closed is the logic:OccurrentBoundaryMismatch violation."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:occurrentConstituent
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:Event ;
    rdfs:range logic:Process ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "occurrent constituent"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a unitary occurrent to a process that constitutes it: the change-stuff an event is made of — a marathon is constituted by the running, a fermentation-event by the fermenting. The constitutive reading of the YAMATO/Galton dictum that events are made of processes: distinct from temporal parthood (logic:temporalPartOf) and from causal parthood (logic:causalPartOf), and carries NO parthood-subsumption rule, so an event's constituting process is not thereby asserted a temporal part of it — constitution, not parthood. The bridge from the unitary, completed logic:Event to the dissective logic:Process whose unfolding it bounds."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:orderedType
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "ordered type"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    skos:definition "Relates a type to its order (level) in the multi-level hierarchy: a first-order type is order 1, a type whose instances are first-order types is order 2, and so on. Makes the deep-instantiation level explicit so logic:instanceOf chains can be checked for level coherence (an order-n type instantiates an order-(n+1) type), the well-formedness condition that keeps HiLog multi-level modeling stratified."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:outcomeAssignment
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:JointOutcome ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "outcome assignment"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:JointOutcome to a correlated logic:probability fact (the reified base triple) that is TRUE in this outcome. Correlated facts of the model that are not named by any logic:outcomeAssignment of an outcome are false in that outcome — the assignment is read as the positive set, the complement against the model's logic:correlates support. The range is intentionally left open (no rdfs:range), for the same reason as logic:correlates: its object is a reified logic:probability statement, which carries no dedicated class in this standalone module."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:overlaps
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "overlaps"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Mereological overlap: two entities share a common part. The primitive sharing notion that must be settled before disjointness or weak supplementation can be stated — logic:disjoint is its negation, and logic:WeakSupplementation is never applied where overlap is undefined. It is derived from logic:properPartOf: entities that share a proper part overlap, and a proper part overlaps its whole. Symmetric in intent (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:partOf
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "part of"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The general (reflexive) parthood relation: relates an entity to a whole it is part of, where every entity is trivially part of itself. The mereological base relation over which logic:properPartOf is the strict (irreflexive) restriction. Distinct from logic:memberOf, which relates a member to a collection without the part being a part of the whole in the mereological sense."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:pathDepthArg
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:PathInvocation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:positiveInteger ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "path depth argument"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The concrete depth bound supplied at a logic:PathInvocation for the named depth parameter of the invoked logic:PathShape (its logic:pathDepthParam): the value of ?maxDepth in :name(?maxDepth := 2). Bounds the traversal to at most this many hops for this invocation without altering the shape itself."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:pathDepthParam
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:PathShape ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "path depth parameter"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The name of the depth parameter a logic:PathShape exposes for parametric invocation — 'maxDepth' in :nearbyOrgs(?maxDepth := 2). A logic:PathInvocation binds this parameter with logic:pathDepthArg. Default-absent: a shape with a fixed depth and no exposed parameter carries no logic:pathDepthParam and is invoked without an argument."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:pathMaxDepth
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:PathShape ;
    rdfs:range xsd:positiveInteger ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "path maximum depth"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The inclusive upper bound on the traversal length of a logic:PathShape — the n in a bounded {min,n} path. Default-absent: a shape with no logic:pathMaxDepth is unbounded (the SPARQL-+ / transitive-closure reading), traversing arbitrarily many hops. When present it makes the path a bounded {1,n} traversal, which SPARQL 1.1 §9 cannot express directly."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:pathMinDepth
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:PathShape ;
    rdfs:range xsd:positiveInteger ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "path minimum depth"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The inclusive lower bound on the traversal length of a logic:PathShape — the min in a bounded {min,max} path. Default-absent: a shape with no logic:pathMinDepth starts at one hop (min = 1). Must not exceed logic:pathMaxDepth when both are present; a minimum above the maximum is a malformed shape and is rejected by the frontend, not silently repaired."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:pathNamespaceScope
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:PathShape ;
    rdfs:range xsd:anyURI ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "path namespace scope"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A predicate-namespace IRI prefix that scopes a wildcard step of a logic:PathShape: when logic:pathWildcard is true, only predicates whose IRI begins with this namespace are traversed. Bounds the fan-out of an otherwise any-predicate walk to a single vocabulary. Default-absent on a wildcard shape: the wildcard matches predicates in any namespace."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:pathStepPredicate
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:PathShape ;
    rdfs:range rdfs:Resource ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "path step predicate"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The named predicate that each hop of a logic:PathShape traverses. Present on a named-predicate path; absent on a wildcard path (where logic:pathWildcard is true instead). A shape that carries BOTH a logic:pathStepPredicate and logic:pathWildcard true is malformed — the base step is a named predicate XOR a wildcard — and is rejected by the frontend rather than silently resolved."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:pathWildcard
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:PathShape ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "path wildcard"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Marks a logic:PathShape whose step matches ANY predicate rather than one named predicate — the 'any predicate within n hops' traversal that SPARQL 1.1 §9 property paths cannot express. When true the step is unconstrained except by an optional logic:pathNamespaceScope; mutually exclusive with logic:pathStepPredicate. Default-absent (false): the path follows the named logic:pathStepPredicate."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:positionContext
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:HolonicPosition ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "position context"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The context role of a logic:HolonicPosition: the context under which the position is occupied. Holon-ness is contextual — an entity that is a holon under one context need not be under another. One of the five role properties (with logic:positionEntity, logic:positionHolarchy, logic:positionInterval, logic:positionPath) that reify the five-place holonic-position relation onto the arity-bounded reasoning surface."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:positionEntity
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:HolonicPosition ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "position entity"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The entity role of a logic:HolonicPosition: the individual that occupies the holonic position — the thing that is a holon along the position's path. One of the five role properties (with logic:positionHolarchy, logic:positionContext, logic:positionInterval, logic:positionPath) that reify the five-place holonic-position relation onto the arity-bounded reasoning surface."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:positionHolarchy
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:HolonicPosition ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "position holarchy"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range logic:Holarchy ;
    skos:definition "The holarchy role of a logic:HolonicPosition: the logic:Holarchy within which the position is occupied. Holon-ness is always relative to a holarchy; the same entity may occupy holonic positions in several holarchies. One of the five role properties (with logic:positionEntity, logic:positionContext, logic:positionInterval, logic:positionPath) that reify the five-place holonic-position relation."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:positionInterval
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:HolonicPosition ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "position interval"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The interval role of a logic:HolonicPosition: the interval over which the position is occupied. Holon-ness is temporally bounded — an entity may occupy a holonic position over one interval and not another. One of the five role properties (with logic:positionEntity, logic:positionHolarchy, logic:positionContext, logic:positionPath) that reify the five-place holonic-position relation."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:positionPath
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:HolonicPosition ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "position path"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The path role of a logic:HolonicPosition: the path through the holarchy along which the position is read. Holarchies are DAGs, so a holonic position — and the logic:holonicLevel measured at it — is meaningful only relative to a path; two paths may place the same entity at different depths, and both are correct. One of the five role properties (with logic:positionEntity, logic:positionHolarchy, logic:positionContext, logic:positionInterval) that reify the five-place holonic-position relation."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:preservationKind
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "preservation kind"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range logic:PreservationKind ;
    skos:definition "Relates a projection (or projection-report entry) to the logic:PreservationKind it claims: the machine-readable preservation polarity in the loss ledger. Lets a report say not just 'dropped modality' but, e.g., 'OWL-EL is a logic:SoundUnderApproximation for subclass entailments under profile X; PTIME'. The projections conformance category checks that each emitted projection matches its declared preservation kind."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:probability
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "probability"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A calibrated probability under probabilistic fact/event semantics, requiring an explicit independence or dependency model. Distinct from logic:confidence, logic:weight, and logic:evidenceStrength and not interchangeable with them: probabilistic inference is available only in logic:ProbabilisticProfile. A logic:confidence annotation is NOT a probability unless an explicit mapping to this property is declared."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:probabilityModel
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "probability model"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range logic:ProbabilityModel ;
    skos:definition "Links a rule set or world to the logic:ProbabilityModel that governs its probabilistic inference. Required for any probabilistic query under logic:ProbabilisticProfile: with no logic:probabilityModel declared, probabilistic inference returns unknown rather than assuming independence over the logic:probability facts."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:projectionTarget
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "projection target"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to a logic:ProjectionTarget it requests the answer be rendered to. A standing output request, possibly naming several targets at once (canonical, OWL, Datalog, Common Logic, validation-only); it is not a semantic selection and never alters which entailments hold. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ProjectionTarget (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:properPartOf
    a owl:ObjectProperty ,
        logic:asymmetricProperty ,
        logic:irreflexiveProperty ,
        logic:transitiveProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "proper part of"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "STRICT parthood: relates an entity to a whole it is part of but NOT identical to. Transitive, asymmetric, and irreflexive — a genuine strict partial order (proper-part-of, ancestor). This exact combination is illegal in OWL 2 DL, which globally forbids a property being both transitive and asymmetric (criticism 7, LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md §OWL 2 criticisms); logic: imposes no such global restriction and reasons over it completely, recovering decidability by projection rather than by crippling the canon. The deliberate OWL-2-criticism demonstrator."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:reductionBasis
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:ReductionTheory ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "reduction basis"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReductionTheory to a property-value it treats as part-reducible: the theory holds that a whole bearing this property has it in virtue of its proper parts bearing it, so under that theory the property is an logic:Aggregate rather than an emergent one. The carrier that makes emergence theory-relative — a property in one theory's reduction basis and absent from another's receives opposite verdicts with no contradiction. Without a matching basis entry, a borne whole property is assessed logic:Emergent under the theory (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:resourcePolicy
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "resource policy"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:ResourcePolicy it requests — the engine's execution discipline. A standing request, not a semantic selection; the resource policy holds several independent properties together (a certified-fragment requirement AND a budget), so a contract may carry both logic:CertifiedFragmentResource and logic:BudgetBoundedResource. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ResourcePolicy (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:revision
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "revision"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:RevisionPolicy it selects — how change is absorbed. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:RevisionPolicy (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:rigidityViolation
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "rigidity violation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates an individual to a rigid type it fails to persist as across worlds: the derived diagnostic of the positive cross-world rigidity discipline (the fourth OntoUML discipline, the one the type-only lint cannot express). For an individual x and a rigid type T, if x instantiates T in some world but still exists in another world where it is NOT typed T, a logic:rigidityViolation fact is entailed in that other world. Unlike logic:violation it is not produced by an in-world Datalog rule — rigidity quantifies over pairs of worlds and the chase is world-local, so it is evaluated by bounded closure over the finite materialized world set (LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md §Operational semantics). It is never asserted by hand; its presence is a machine-checkable proof that a rigid type's instantiation did not carry over to a world where the individual persists."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:rigidlyAppliesTo
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "rigidly applies to"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a rigid type to the individuals it necessarily classifies: for every individual and every pair of worlds in which the individual exists, if it instantiates the type in one world it instantiates it in the other. The modal rigidity constraint; a Kind rigidly applies to its instances, an anti-rigid Role or Phase does not (the same constraint negated). Lowered to a universally quantified, world-indexed rule evaluated by closure over the finite materialized world set, needing no native modal operator."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:selfAssertiveBasis
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:HolonicAgencyProfile ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "self-assertive basis"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:HolonicAgencyProfile to a property-value that evidences the self-assertive (autonomy) tendency: the profile holds that a holon bearing this value (logic:bearsProperty) asserts itself as a whole — Koestler's self-assertive face. The carrier that makes autonomy profile-relative, the co-equal twin of logic:integrativeBasis (neither privileged, Principle 9). Without a borne self-assertive value a holon's autonomy face is not evidenced, contributing — together with the integrative face — to the logic:AgencyVerdict (logic:AutonomyDeficient or logic:HolonIntegral). The autonomy analogue of logic:reductionBasis and logic:activationBasis (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:suppliesIdentity
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "supplies identity"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates an ultimate sortal to an individual whose principle of identity it supplies: the second-order identity-supply relation, reified as a first-order relation over punned type individuals (HiLog/F-logic style) so that 'every object instantiates exactly one ultimate sortal' becomes a first-order counting constraint. Kinds supply identity; SubKinds, Roles, and Phases inherit it; non-sortals (Category, Mixin, RoleMixin, PhaseMixin) supply none."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:temporalPartOf
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "temporal part of"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Parthood among perdurants: relates a temporal part of an occurrent to the larger occurrent it is a phase of — the first act is a temporal part of the play. The four-dimensional parthood relation, distinct from the endurant parthood of logic:partOf / logic:properPartOf: it carves a perdurant along its temporal extent into sub-occurrents."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:transitiveProperty
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "transitive property"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic: property-characteristic marker for transitivity: a property P such that P(a,b) ∧ P(b,c) entails P(a,c). The logic: analogue of owl:TransitiveProperty, minted standalone so logic: can combine it with logic:asymmetricProperty — a combination OWL 2 DL forbids globally (criticism 7) but logic: reasons over fully."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:truthAlgebra
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "truth algebra"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:TruthAlgebra it selects — the lattice of truth values over which valuations range. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:TruthAlgebra (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). One of the three independent truth-facet components, selected separately from logic:admissibleValuation and logic:designatedValues."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:uncertaintyMeasure
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "uncertainty measure"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to a logic:UncertaintyMeasure it carries — how graded belief is recorded. Set-valued on the contract: probabilistic, weighted/ranking, and fuzzy measures may coexist on the same result, so this records the set of measures in force, not one. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:UncertaintyMeasure (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:underMereologyProfile
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "under mereology profile"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range logic:MereologyProfile ;
    skos:definition "Relates a whole to the logic:MereologyProfile it is declared under — the scope within which the strong mereological axioms (weak supplementation) hold for it. A whole carries no logic:WeakSupplementation obligation unless declared under a profile via this relation; parthood is profiled, not universal (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:violation
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "violation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates an offending entity to the constraint it violates — a logic:Discipline (an OntoUML structural anti-pattern), a logic:MereologyConstraint (a profiled-mereology axiom such as logic:WeakSupplementation), or a logic:OccurrentConstraint (an occurrent well-formedness axiom such as logic:OccurrentChangeAsymmetry): the derived diagnostic the foundation lowering materializes, the logic: analogue of a reasoning_lint message. A logic:violation fact is never asserted by hand; it is entailed by the lowering rules over the stereotype, subsumption, mediation and parthood facts, so its presence is a machine-checkable proof that the entity breaks the named constraint."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:weight
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "weight"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A solver or ranking weight — a numeric preference used to order or score derivations — not necessarily probabilistic and not an epistemic confidence. Normatively distinct from logic:probability, logic:confidence, and logic:evidenceStrength: a ranking weight carries no calibrated probabilistic or evidential meaning unless one is separately and explicitly declared."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:witnessRequiredViolation
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "witness required violation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates an individual to an anti-rigid type it instantiates with no materialized counter-world to witness the anti-rigidity: the instance-level diagnostic the anti-rigidity lowering emits under the strict witness-required policy (LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md §Anti-rigidity needs a witness policy). For an individual x typed by an anti-rigid Role or Phase T in a world, if there is no other materialized world in which x exists but is NOT typed T, a logic:witnessRequiredViolation fact is entailed in the typing world; a counter-world that witnesses x existing untyped by T discharges the obligation and no violation is emitted. Unlike the default witness-obligation policy (which emits logic:dischargeObligation, an obligation rather than a violation) this policy treats a missing counter-world as a hard failure; the construction of the witness world itself happens on demand. It is never asserted by hand; its presence is a machine-checkable proof that an anti-rigid instantiation lacks the world of existence its anti-rigidity requires."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:activeInState
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "active in state"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a support/reified assertion to the path state in which that support was active. The transition oracle uses it to keep retired supports auditable: a `del` records the predecessor state where the support held, then advances to a successor where that support no longer holds."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:validUntilState
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "valid until state"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a support/reified assertion to the successor state at which it stops holding as an active support. It is the path-state counterpart of temporal valid-until metadata: a `del` records the state boundary where the support is retired, while the historical support remains retained."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:retiredByTransaction
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "retired by transaction"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a retired support/reified assertion to the elementary update or transaction-path step that retired it. It is transition provenance: it explains why the support no longer holds in the successor state without deleting the support from the historical path."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:supersededBy
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "superseded by"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a retired support/reified assertion version to the update or successor support that supersedes it in the append-only store. It is the missing counterpart that, together with logic:activeInState, logic:validUntilState, and logic:retiredByTransaction, makes every `del` a supersession rather than an erasure: the retired version is never removed, it is recorded as superseded by the version that took its place. The substrate therefore stays monotonic and append-only — a superseded assertion remains recoverable, and the supersession chain reconstructs the full history of what replaced what. Suppression-not-erasure: `del` removes a support, it does not destroy the historical record. Domain a retired support/reified assertion version, range the superseding update or successor support (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:transitionFromState
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "transition from state"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates an elementary update or transaction-path step to the predecessor state snapshot from which it starts. States are WorldStore named-graph snapshots; this relation records the path edge's source state without mutating that state."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:transitionToState
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "transition to state"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates an elementary update or transaction-path step to the successor state snapshot it materializes. The successor is a new named graph produced by the transition oracle from the predecessor plus the effective `ins`/`del` updates."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ins
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "ins"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:InsertUpdate to the support/fact it asserts. The `ins(F)` primitive makes F active in the successor state while leaving the predecessor state untouched."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:del
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "del"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:DeleteUpdate to the support/fact it retires. The `del(F)` primitive removes F from the active support set of the successor state, records supersession provenance, and leaves the predecessor state and historical support intact."@x-gmeow-english .

# ── ME2: the typed logic:ReasoningResult surface ─────────────────────────────────
# The single shared result model. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust,
# crates/logic/src/result.rs); these terms are the lossy documentation projection
# (Principle 17). The five orthogonal status fields and the conclusiveness
# invariant are normative in design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md §The reasoning result;
# logic:ResultAssurance is in design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md. Each value class is a
# CLOSED set: a misspelt value names no declared individual and is rejected.

logic:ReasoningResult
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Reasoning Result"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The single shared result a reasoning run produces and every consumer reads (ME2): a compositional status carrying FIVE orthogonal fields, each ranging over its own value class — logic:resultInput (well-formedness), logic:resultEvaluation (what the engine could do), logic:resultCompleteness (relative to what the answer is complete), logic:resultPreservation (the set of answer-preservation polarities the lowering claims, plus the constructs it could not carry), and logic:resultInformation (the four-valued Belnap verdict plus two explicit non-results). Several fields hold at once. It additionally carries the provenance bundle: logic:contractHash, logic:query/logic:conclusion, logic:resultProof/logic:resultCounterproof, the world/standpoint/time/path context, logic:engine, logic:consumedBudget, logic:certifiedFragment, logic:contradictionWitness, and logic:resultAssumption. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); this is a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17). Normative in design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, §The reasoning result."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:InputStatus
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Input Status"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed value class of the logic:resultInput field: was the request well-formed? Its individuals are logic:InputValid and logic:InputInvalid. The set is closed, so a misspelt value names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, §The reasoning result)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:InputValid
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:InputStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Input Valid"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:InputStatus value for a request whose sources parsed and type-checked: reasoning was attempted. Wire value `valid`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:InputInvalid
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:InputStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Input Invalid"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:InputStatus value for an ill-formed request: no reasoning was attempted and the other four fields are vacuous. Wire value `invalid`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:EvaluationStatus
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Evaluation Status"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed value class of the logic:resultEvaluation field (the computation axis): what the engine was ABLE to do. Its individuals are logic:EvaluationCompleted, logic:BudgetExhausted, and logic:EvaluationUnsupported. The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, §The reasoning result)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:EvaluationCompleted
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:EvaluationStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Evaluation Completed"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:EvaluationStatus value for a run that reached its natural end on the request — a conclusive evaluation. Wire value `completed`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:BudgetExhausted
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:EvaluationStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Budget Exhausted"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:EvaluationStatus value for a run that hit a declared resource budget or bound before finishing. Wire value `budget-exhausted`. The specific budget that tripped (answers/inference/depth) is carried alongside as consumed-budget detail so the historical answer-status strings remain a lossless projection."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:EvaluationUnsupported
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:EvaluationStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Evaluation Unsupported"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:EvaluationStatus value for a request the engine has no defined procedure for (an unsupported contract, or a missing required model such as a probabilistic dependency model). Wire value `unsupported`; the information field is then logic:InfoNotEvaluated, never logic:InfoNeither."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:CompletenessStatus
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Completeness Status"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed value class of the logic:resultCompleteness field: relative to what is the answer complete? Its individuals are logic:CompleteForFragment, logic:Incomplete, and logic:CompletenessUnknown. The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, §The reasoning result)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:CompleteForFragment
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:CompletenessStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Complete For Fragment"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:CompletenessStatus value for an answer complete for the certified fragment the contract pins — a conclusive evaluation even when the whole run did not otherwise complete. Wire value `complete-for-fragment`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Incomplete
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:CompletenessStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Incomplete"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:CompletenessStatus value for an answer whose search did not exhaust the space (a budget, answer cap, or depth bound was hit, or a DL construct was undecided). Wire value `incomplete`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:CompletenessUnknown
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:CompletenessStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Completeness Unknown"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:CompletenessStatus value when completeness is not a defined question for the request — e.g. a genuine incomparable-entrenchment revision tie. Wire value `unknown`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:InformationState
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Information State"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed value class of the logic:resultInformation field (the information axis): the four-valued Belnap verdict about the queried proposition plus two explicit non-results. Its individuals are logic:InfoSupported, logic:InfoOpposed, logic:InfoBoth, logic:InfoNeither (the Belnap four), logic:InfoUndetermined, and logic:InfoNotEvaluated. The three non-positive states are NEVER interchangeable: logic:InfoNeither requires a conclusive evaluation; logic:InfoUndetermined means no verdict was reached; logic:InfoNotEvaluated means the engine could not look. The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, §The reasoning result)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:InfoSupported
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:InformationState ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Information Supported"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:InformationState value when there is a proof and no counterproof. Wire value `supported`. Provisional when the evaluation is not conclusive (logic:Incomplete); conclusive within the fragment otherwise."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:supportSupported .

logic:InfoOpposed
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:InformationState ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Information Opposed"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:InformationState value when there is a counterproof and no proof — the FDE/paraconsistent evidence for the explicit negation. Wire value `opposed`."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:supportOpposed .

logic:InfoBoth
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:InformationState ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Information Both"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:InformationState value when a proof AND a counterproof exist — a witnessed contradiction (glut) within one context, carried with its logic:contradictionWitness graph. Wire value `both`. A correct `both` is HIGH-assurance about a contradictory input, not a defect, and is local to its world — never globalized to owl:Nothing."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:supportBoth .

logic:InfoNeither
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:InformationState ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Information Neither"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:InformationState value when neither proof nor counterproof exists, established by a CONCLUSIVE evaluation (a completed run or a complete-for-the-fragment answer) — a real four-valued verdict. Wire value `neither`. NEVER interchangeable with logic:InfoUndetermined (no verdict reached) or logic:InfoNotEvaluated (the engine could not look)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:supportNeither .

logic:InfoUndetermined
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:InformationState ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Information Undetermined"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:InformationState value when the evaluation did not reach a conclusive verdict — the search did not finish (budget exhausted), a partial-order tie, or a graded semantics with no discretization policy. Wire value `undetermined`. NOT the conclusive logic:InfoNeither."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:InfoNotEvaluated
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:InformationState ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Information Not Evaluated"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:InformationState value when no information semantics were available — the engine COULD NOT look (an unsupported contract, or a missing required model such as a probabilistic dependency model). Wire value `not-evaluated`. NOT the conclusive logic:InfoNeither."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ResultAssurance
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Result Assurance"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A reified assessment that targets one logic:ReasoningResult (via logic:assuresResult) and reads its fields JOINTLY: logic:InfoSupported with logic:Incomplete is provisional, whereas logic:InfoSupported with logic:CompleteForFragment is conclusive within that fragment; a correctly returned logic:InfoBoth is high-assurance about a contradictory input, not a defect. A result assurance is DISTINCT from a reliability assessment of the reasoner: the former judges one result, the latter judges a series of runs (a logic:CognitiveAssessment). Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); lossy documentation projection (Principle 17). Normative in design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:assuresResult
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "assures result"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ResultAssurance to the single logic:ReasoningResult it assesses. Domain logic:ResultAssurance, range logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:resultInput
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "result input"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to the logic:InputStatus it received. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult, range logic:InputStatus (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:resultEvaluation
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "result evaluation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to the logic:EvaluationStatus the engine reached (the computation axis). Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult, range logic:EvaluationStatus (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:resultCompleteness
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "result completeness"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to the logic:CompletenessStatus of its answer. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult, range logic:CompletenessStatus (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:resultInformation
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "result information"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to the logic:InformationState verdict about the queried proposition (the information axis). Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult, range logic:InformationState (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:resultPreservation
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "result preservation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to each logic:PreservationKind polarity that co-holds for it — MULTI-valued, because the preservation field is a SET of polarities, not a single choice (logic:ValidationOnly is excluded; it names a lowering's purpose, not an answer-preservation polarity). Domain logic:ReasoningResult, range logic:PreservationKind (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:unsupportedConstruct
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "unsupported construct"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Names a construct the lowering could not carry at all, carried on a logic:ReasoningResult's preservation field — MULTI-valued. A query whose constructs intersect this set is loss-affected (a derived diagnostic, never a stored field). Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:contractHash
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "contract hash"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The content-addressed identity of the reasoning contract a logic:ReasoningResult was produced under. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:engine
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "engine"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The engine identity + version that produced a logic:ReasoningResult. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:query
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "query"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The canonical query text a logic:ReasoningResult answers — part of the proof certificate. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:conclusion
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "conclusion"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The canonical conclusion text a logic:ReasoningResult's verdict is about — part of the proof certificate. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:resultProof
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "result proof"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to the derivation that proves its conclusion (a content-addressed handle into the explanation/proof tree), present iff the conclusion is derivable. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:resultCounterproof
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "result counterproof"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to the derivation that proves the explicit negation of its conclusion (the same machinery as logic:resultProof), present iff the negation is derivable. A result carrying BOTH a proof and a counterproof is logic:InfoBoth. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:contradictionWitness
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "contradiction witness"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to a within-world contradiction witness justifying a logic:InfoBoth verdict — MULTI-valued. The witness is local to its world; the base store is never globalized to owl:Nothing. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:consumedBudget
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "consumed budget"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The resource budget a logic:ReasoningResult consumed, against the contract's declared allowance. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:certifiedFragment
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "certified fragment"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The certified-complete fragment reference backing a logic:CompleteForFragment claim on a logic:ReasoningResult. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:resultAssumption
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "result assumption"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A declared closure/identity/revision/witness-policy assumption a logic:ReasoningResult rests on (e.g. closed-world, unique-name, entrenchment-revision, skolem-witness) — MULTI-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

# ── Semantics-aware validator findings + the scoped coherence certificate ───────
# Two halves. First, logic:FindingCategory: an ORTHOGONAL axis to a finding's
# severity that records what KIND of finding it is — because not all findings are
# failures. A witnessed, disclosed contradiction under a glut-admitting contract is
# a logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict, coherent rather than a defect. Second,
# the contract-scoped coherence outcome: a logic:CoherenceCertificate (only from a
# CONCLUSIVE check) or the strictly weaker logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation (from a
# bounded/incomplete check). Coherence means "no forbidden integrity violation and
# no undisclosed contradiction under the governing contract", NEVER "contradiction-
# free". Authored canonically in crates/logic + crates/diagnostics (Rust); this is a
# lossy documentation projection (Principle 17). Normative in
# design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md, §The coherence certificate.

logic:FindingCategory
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Finding Category"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed value class of a validator finding's KIND — an axis orthogonal to its severity, because not all findings are failures. Its individuals are logic:FindingDataShapeViolation, logic:FindingModelingDisciplineViolation, logic:FindingContradictionWitness, logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict, logic:FindingUnsupportedSemanticFeature, logic:FindingIncompleteCheck, logic:FindingProjectionLoss and logic:FindingPolicyWarning. The set is closed; a misspelt value names no declared kind and is rejected. The load-bearing case is logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict: a disclosed, witnessed contradiction permitted by a glut-admitting contract is coherent and does NOT fail the gate (design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md, §The coherence certificate)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:FindingDataShapeViolation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FindingCategory ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Finding Data-Shape Violation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:FindingCategory for a closed-world data-shape constraint breach — a SHACL shape an instance failed. A failure. Wire value `data-shape-violation`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:FindingModelingDisciplineViolation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FindingCategory ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Finding Modeling-Discipline Violation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:FindingCategory for an ontology modeling-discipline breach — a structural/gUFO-tier rule the vocabulary itself violates, or an unsatisfiable class surfaced by reasoning. A failure. Wire value `modeling-discipline-violation`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:FindingContradictionWitness
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FindingCategory ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Finding Contradiction Witness"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:FindingCategory for a within-world contradiction (a logic:InfoBoth glut) that the governing contract FORBIDS — an unpermitted, integrity-violating inconsistency. A failure. Distinguished from logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict purely by the contract's logic:contradictionPolicy. Wire value `contradiction-witness`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FindingCategory ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Finding Permitted Epistemic Conflict"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:FindingCategory for a disclosed, witnessed contradiction that a glut-admitting contract PERMITS — exactly the behaviour the paraconsistent contract anticipates. NOT a failure: it is coherent, surfaced for transparency, and does NOT block a logic:CoherenceCertificate. The load-bearing case for the principle that not all findings are failures. Wire value `permitted-epistemic-conflict`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:FindingUnsupportedSemanticFeature
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FindingCategory ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Finding Unsupported Semantic Feature"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:FindingCategory for a construct the engine has no defined procedure for under the governing contract — a logic:EvaluationUnsupported outcome on a feature outside the certified fragment. A disclosure, not a defect of the data. Wire value `unsupported-semantic-feature`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:FindingIncompleteCheck
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FindingCategory ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Finding Incomplete Check"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:FindingCategory for a check that did not run to completion — a logic:BudgetExhausted or logic:Incomplete evaluation. Records that the search was bounded; it is the reason a bounded run yields a logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation rather than a logic:CoherenceCertificate. Not a failure of the data. Wire value `incomplete-check`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:FindingProjectionLoss
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FindingCategory ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Finding Projection Loss"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:FindingCategory for a construct a lowering could not carry exactly — a warning that an answer was produced through a projection whose preservation claim drops or approximates some constructs (the loss ledger). Not a failure; a fidelity disclosure. Wire value `projection-loss`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:FindingPolicyWarning
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FindingCategory ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Finding Policy Warning"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:FindingCategory for a trust/policy advisory — an untrusted signer, a missing-but-not-required attestation, a soft governance note. Advisory, not a hard failure. Wire value `policy-warning`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:CoherenceCertificate
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Coherence Certificate"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The contract-scoped assertion, issued ONLY from a CONCLUSIVE check (the summarized logic:ReasoningResult has logic:EvaluationCompleted, or logic:CompleteForFragment), that over the certified fragment the inspection was COMPLETE and found no forbidden integrity violation and no undisclosed contradiction. Scoped by contract (logic:contractHash on the linked result), fragment (logic:certifiedFragment), budget (logic:consumedBudget) and bundle (logic:bundleHash, logic:axiomHash). Coherence means 'every contradiction present is permitted under the contract and disclosed, or has been reported as a violation' — NEVER 'this bundle contains no contradiction'. A complete check is the only thing entitled to the word certify; a bounded check yields a logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation instead. Carries logic:permittedConflictWitness for disclosed gluts and logic:forbiddenViolationWitness (necessarily empty for an issued certificate). Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17). Normative in design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md, §The coherence certificate."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Coherence Check Attestation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The strictly weaker outcome a BOUNDED or INCOMPLETE coherence check issues (the summarized logic:ReasoningResult has logic:BudgetExhausted, or logic:Incomplete / logic:CompletenessUnknown): it records only that no forbidden integrity violation and no undisclosed contradiction was found WITHIN the completed search. A budget-exhausted run produces an attestation, NEVER a logic:CoherenceCertificate, because it cannot rule out a contradiction it never reached. Honest evidence, not a certification of coherence. Carries the same scoped payload (logic:summarizesResult, logic:bundleHash, logic:contradictionPolicy, logic:checkIssuedAt). Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17). Normative in design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md, §The coherence certificate."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:summarizesResult
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "summarizes result"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a coherence outcome (logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation) to the single logic:ReasoningResult whose completion status, contract (logic:contractHash), certified fragment (logic:certifiedFragment), consumed budget (logic:consumedBudget), assumptions (logic:resultAssumption) and preservation losses it certifies over. The completeness gate (certificate vs attestation) reads this result's logic:resultEvaluation and logic:resultCompleteness. Single-valued. Domain logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation, range logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:bundleHash
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "bundle hash"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The content-addressed identity (a blake3 digest) of the exact bundle a coherence outcome was checked over. The outcome is invalid for any bundle whose canonical hash differs. Single-valued. Domain logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:axiomHash
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "axiom hash"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A content-addressed digest of an axiom set inside the checked bundle, pinning exactly which axioms the coherence outcome ranged over — MULTI-valued, one per certified fragment component. Domain logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:contradictionPolicy
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "contradiction policy"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a coherence outcome to the logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy that decides, for the governing contract, whether a within-world glut is a forbidden violation (logic:ForbidGlut, logic:ForbidGapAndGlut) or a permitted disclosed conflict (logic:AdmitAllFour, logic:ForbidGap). The pivot that classifies each contradiction witness. Single-valued. Domain logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation, range logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:checkIssuedAt
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "check issued at"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The xsd:dateTime a coherence outcome was issued. INJECTED, never sampled in the deterministic fold core, so re-running with the same inputs and timestamp is byte-identical. Single-valued. Domain logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:permittedConflictWitness
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "permitted conflict witness"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a coherence outcome to a disclosed, witnessed contradiction the contract PERMITS (a logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict) — MULTI-valued. Present permitted witnesses do NOT block a logic:CoherenceCertificate; they are surfaced for transparency. Domain logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:forbiddenViolationWitness
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "forbidden violation witness"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a coherence outcome to a within-world contradiction the contract FORBIDS (a logic:FindingContradictionWitness) — MULTI-valued. A NON-EMPTY set blocks issuance: a logic:CoherenceCertificate is issued only when this set is empty. Domain logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

# ── The typed logic:ResultShape surface ─────────────────────────────────────────
# A schema-level type contract on a SPARQL SELECT result set: the declared columns
# (variable + term-kind + optional datatype + binding requiredness) and the row-set
# cardinality, plus the shape a query expects on its input. The row-schema facet of
# logic:ReasoningResult. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); this is a
# lossy documentation projection (Principle 17). Normative in
# design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, §The result row schema.

logic:ResultShape
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Result Shape"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A schema-level type contract on a SPARQL SELECT result set: the declared columns it carries (logic:declaresColumn) and the row-set cardinality (logic:shapeCardinality, with logic:shapeRowCount in count mode). The same construct types a query's expected INPUT (logic:expectsInputShape) and its guaranteed OUTPUT (logic:producesResultShape), so a query's input→output contract is checkable before execution. It generalises the test-DSL example-row idiom: an ExpectedRow is an example-instance of the ResultShape its competency question declares. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); this is a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17). Normative in design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, §The result row schema."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:ResultColumn
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Result Column"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "One typed column of a logic:ResultShape: a declared SELECT variable (logic:columnVariable), its term-kind (logic:columnTermKind, mandatory — an untyped column is the bag this contract eliminates), an optional pinned datatype for literal columns (logic:columnDatatype), and whether it is bound in every row (logic:columnBinding). Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); this is a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:TermKind
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Term Kind"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed value class of the logic:columnTermKind facet: the RDF term kind a result column binds. Its individuals are logic:TermKindIri, logic:TermKindLiteral and logic:TermKindBlankNode. The set is closed, so a misspelt value names no declared kind and is rejected (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, §The result row schema)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:TermKindIri
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:TermKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Term Kind IRI"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:TermKind value for a column whose values are IRIs (named nodes). Wire value `iri`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:TermKindLiteral
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:TermKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Term Kind Literal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:TermKind value for a column whose values are literals. A literal column may further pin its datatype with logic:columnDatatype; absent that, any literal conforms. Wire value `literal`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:TermKindBlankNode
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:TermKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Term Kind Blank Node"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:TermKind value for a column whose values are blank nodes. Wire value `blank-node`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ColumnBinding
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Column Binding"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed value class of the logic:columnBinding facet: whether a column's variable is bound in every row. Its individuals are logic:BindingRequired and logic:BindingOptional. The set is closed, so a misspelt value names no declared binding and is rejected."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:BindingRequired
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ColumnBinding ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Binding Required"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:ColumnBinding value for a column bound in every result row. An unbound required column is a hard contract violation. Wire value `required`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:BindingOptional
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ColumnBinding ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Binding Optional"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:ColumnBinding value for a column that may be unbound in some rows (e.g. projected from a SPARQL OPTIONAL). Wire value `optional`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:RowCardinality
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Row Cardinality"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed value class of the logic:shapeCardinality facet: the row-set contract a result shape declares. Its individuals are logic:RowsExact (the declared example rows are the complete set), logic:RowsContains (the declared rows must all appear; extras permitted) and logic:RowsCount (only the count is pinned, via logic:shapeRowCount). The set is closed, so a misspelt value names no declared mode and is rejected."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:RowsExact
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:RowCardinality ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Rows Exact"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:RowCardinality value pinning the declared example rows as the complete, exact result set. Wire value `exact`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:RowsContains
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:RowCardinality ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Rows Contains"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:RowCardinality value requiring the declared example rows to all appear, with extra rows permitted. Wire value `contains`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:RowsCount
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:RowCardinality ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Rows Count"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:RowCardinality value pinning only the result row count (carried by logic:shapeRowCount), with no per-row content contract. Wire value `count`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:resultRowSchema
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "result row schema"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to the logic:ResultShape its bindings are contracted to — the row-schema facet of the typed result. Single-valued; absent for surfaces with no row schema (e.g. a pure DL-consistency verdict). The schema is the caller's DECLARED contract, validated against the bindings, never synthesised from them. Domain logic:ReasoningResult, range logic:ResultShape (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:declaresColumn
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "declares column"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ResultShape to a logic:ResultColumn it declares. Set-valued: a shape declares one column per SELECT variable it types. Domain logic:ResultShape, range logic:ResultColumn (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:shapeCardinality
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "shape cardinality"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ResultShape to the logic:RowCardinality it declares — the row-set contract. Single-valued. Domain logic:ResultShape, range logic:RowCardinality (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:shapeRowCount
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "shape row count"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The pinned result row count for a logic:ResultShape in logic:RowsCount mode. Single-valued, xsd:nonNegativeInteger. Domain logic:ResultShape (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:columnVariable
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "column variable"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The bare SPARQL variable name (no leading '?') a logic:ResultColumn types. Single-valued, xsd:string. Domain logic:ResultColumn (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:columnTermKind
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "column term kind"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ResultColumn to the logic:TermKind it requires — the mandatory RDF term kind of the column's values. Single-valued. Domain logic:ResultColumn, range logic:TermKind (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:columnDatatype
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "column datatype"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a literal logic:ResultColumn to the datatype IRI it pins. Single-valued and OPTIONAL: a literal column with no logic:columnDatatype accepts any literal (a declared loosening, not a half-typed column); a non-literal column carries none. Domain logic:ResultColumn, range a datatype IRI (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:columnBinding
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "column binding"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ResultColumn to the logic:ColumnBinding it declares — whether the variable is bound in every row. Single-valued. Domain logic:ResultColumn, range logic:ColumnBinding (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:expectsInputShape
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "expects input shape"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a query (or a competency question) to the logic:ResultShape its input is expected to satisfy. The producer feeding the query must satisfy this shape (structural input→output compatibility) BEFORE execution; a mismatch is a hard, surfaced error. Single-valued. Range logic:ResultShape (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:producesResultShape
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "produces result shape"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a query (or a competency question) to the logic:ResultShape its result set is guaranteed to satisfy. The query's bindings are validated against this shape after execution; a mismatch is a hard, surfaced error. Single-valued. Range logic:ResultShape (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english .

# ── The typed formalization-governance surface (CBox) ───────────────────────────
# The prose-to-axiom transition, made executable. Every extracted statement enters
# as a typed logic:FormalizationCandidate with a lifecycle; only a reviewer-promoted
# candidate becomes a canonical axiom. Deliberate non-assertions are first-class,
# machine-checked logic:NonEntailmentObligations. The home box is CBox (constraints
# and shapes). Normative in design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization
# governance.

logic:FormalizationCandidate
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Formalization Candidate"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A typed, reviewable proposal to turn a prose constraint into a formal axiom: the governed unit of the prose-to-axiom transition. It carries its source-text hash (logic:candidateSourceHash), extraction provenance (logic:candidateExtractionProvenance), intended scope (logic:candidateScope) and reasoning contract (logic:candidateContract, ME1), its logic:FormalizationCategory, its logic:CandidateLifecycleState and reviewer decision (logic:reviewedBy), a positive competency case and a negative countermodel (logic:candidatePositiveCase / logic:candidateNegativeCase), any required logic:NonEntailmentObligation (logic:candidateNonEntailment), its projection behaviour (logic:candidateProjectionBehavior) and its logic:SemanticRiskClass. An LLM extraction always enters as a candidate, never directly as an accepted axiom; only a candidate promoted through review becomes canonical (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox .

logic:NonEntailmentObligation
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Non-Entailment Obligation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A first-class, executable record of a conclusion the foundation must NEVER draw: a deliberate non-assertion the engine is held to, not a comment the axioms happen to respect. It names the forbidden predicate (logic:obligationForbiddenPredicate), the logic:DischargeCondition under which absence-of-proof is conclusively checkable, and the logic:DischargeVerdict the check returns. Because the canonical logic is semi-decidable, an obligation is conclusively discharged only within a stated fragment or bound; outside it the verdict is logic:ObligationUnknown, carried forward, never 'proved absent'. The two standing obligations are 'intent must not be derived from structural deception' and 'counterpart must not become transitive' (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox .

# The two STANDING obligations the charter names verbatim — foundation commitments
# resident in the reasoned graph, so the verify gate checks them over the real
# shipped foundation (not merely over a fixture). Each forbids an assertion-only
# predicate from EVER becoming a foundation rule head (Arm A) or appearing as a
# derived edge (Arm B): gmeow:deceptiveIntentClaim and gmeow:counterpartOf are
# attributed / asserted, never entailed.

logic:IntentNotFromDeceptionObligation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:NonEntailmentObligation ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "intent must not be derived from structural deception"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The standing non-entailment obligation that the presence of a held≠projected gap is EVIDENCE, never ENTAILMENT, of deceptive intent: the foundation must never derive gmeow:deceptiveIntentClaim (an attributed, defeasible standpoint claim) from a structural deception gap. Enforced by syntactic reachability over the rule strata (no rule head produces the predicate) and finite closure over the materialized derivation graph (the predicate appears in no DERIVED edge). Guards the deception slice held/projected model (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:obligationForbiddenPredicate "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/deceptiveIntentClaim"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    logic:obligationDischargeCondition
        logic:DischargeSyntacticReachability ,
        logic:DischargeFiniteClosure ;
    logic:obligationDischargeVerdict logic:ObligationDischarged .

logic:CounterpartNonTransitivityObligation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:NonEntailmentObligation ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "counterpart must not become transitive"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The standing non-entailment obligation that cross-realm counterpart identity (gmeow:counterpartOf) stays non-transitive: it is symmetric but deliberately not transitive, so the foundation must never derive it (any derivation, transitive or otherwise, is forbidden — it is assertion-only). Discharged by syntactic reachability over the counterpart rule heads (no rule head produces the predicate). Guards the coreference slice (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:obligationForbiddenPredicate "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/counterpartOf"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    logic:obligationDischargeCondition logic:DischargeSyntacticReachability ;
    logic:obligationDischargeVerdict logic:ObligationDischarged .

# ── Closed value class: the eleven formalization categories ──────────────────────

logic:FormalizationCategory
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Formalization Category"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed eleven-member value class of the logic:candidateCategory facet: the kind of force a prose constraint was meant to carry. Its individuals are logic:CategoryEquivalenceDefinition, logic:CategoryNecessaryCondition, logic:CategorySufficientCondition, logic:CategoryIntegrityConstraint, logic:CategoryDerivationRule, logic:CategoryDefeasibleDefault, logic:CategoryTypicality, logic:CategoryRecommendation, logic:CategoryNonEntailmentObligation, logic:CategoryDeliberateOverlap and logic:CategoryDocumentationOnly. The set is closed and atomic (Principle 9: necessary and sufficient are two categories, not one), so a misspelt label names no declared category and is rejected rather than silently accepted (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:CategoryEquivalenceDefinition
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormalizationCategory ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Equivalence Definition"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:FormalizationCategory for prose stating the necessary-and-sufficient identity of a term — a definitional equivalence. Wire value `equivalence-definition`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:CategoryNecessaryCondition
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormalizationCategory ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Necessary Condition"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:FormalizationCategory for prose stating a one-directional necessary condition (the term implies the condition). Wire value `necessary-condition`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:CategorySufficientCondition
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormalizationCategory ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Sufficient Condition"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:FormalizationCategory for prose stating a one-directional sufficient condition (the condition implies the term). Wire value `sufficient-condition`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:CategoryIntegrityConstraint
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormalizationCategory ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Integrity Constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:FormalizationCategory for an integrity condition whose violation is a finding, not a derivation — a CBox constraint rather than a productive rule. Wire value `integrity-constraint`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:CategoryDerivationRule
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormalizationCategory ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Derivation Rule"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:FormalizationCategory for a productive rule whose head is entailed — content that adds to the reasoned closure. Wire value `derivation-rule`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:CategoryDefeasibleDefault
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormalizationCategory ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Defeasible Default"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:FormalizationCategory for defeasible content a more specific fact may override — default-logic force, distinct from plain typicality. Wire value `defeasible-default`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:CategoryTypicality
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormalizationCategory ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Typicality"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:FormalizationCategory for generic, what-normally-holds content — kept distinct from logic:CategoryDefeasibleDefault, whose force is override rather than genericity. Wire value `typicality`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:CategoryRecommendation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormalizationCategory ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Recommendation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:FormalizationCategory for advisory content that is never enforced — guidance carried but not reasoned over. Wire value `recommendation`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:CategoryNonEntailmentObligation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormalizationCategory ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Non-Entailment Obligation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:FormalizationCategory for a deliberate non-assertion — prose recording a conclusion the foundation must never draw, realized as a logic:NonEntailmentObligation. Wire value `non-entailment-obligation`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:CategoryDeliberateOverlap
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormalizationCategory ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Deliberate Overlap"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:FormalizationCategory for a mereological sharing fact deliberately admitted — an intended overlap rather than an accidental one. Wire value `deliberate-overlap`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:CategoryDocumentationOnly
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormalizationCategory ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Documentation Only"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:FormalizationCategory for explanatory prose that is NOT to be formalized at all — the category that records a deliberate decision to leave content unaxiomatized. Wire value `documentation-only`."@x-gmeow-english .

# ── Closed value class: the candidate lifecycle states ───────────────────────────

logic:CandidateLifecycleState
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Candidate Lifecycle State"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed value class of the logic:candidateLifecycle facet: the four-state machine a logic:FormalizationCandidate moves through. Its individuals are logic:CandidateProposed (entry; every extraction lands here), logic:CandidateUnderReview, logic:CandidateAccepted (canonical, axiom-bearing) and logic:CandidateRejected. logic:CandidateAccepted is reachable only through logic:CandidateUnderReview with a recorded logic:reviewedBy decision, never directly. The set is closed, so a misspelt state names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:CandidateProposed
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:CandidateLifecycleState ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Proposed"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The lifecycle entry state: a candidate freshly extracted and not yet reviewed. An LLM extraction ALWAYS enters here; it carries no canonical force. Wire value `proposed`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:CandidateUnderReview
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:CandidateLifecycleState ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Under Review"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The lifecycle state of a candidate a reviewer is actively adjudicating — the mandatory waypoint between logic:CandidateProposed and logic:CandidateAccepted. Wire value `under-review`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:CandidateAccepted
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:CandidateLifecycleState ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Accepted"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The canonical, axiom-bearing lifecycle state: a candidate a reviewer has promoted, reachable only through logic:CandidateUnderReview with a recorded logic:reviewedBy decision. A candidate asserted as accepted without that review is a checked governance violation, not a soft warning. Wire value `accepted`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:CandidateRejected
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:CandidateLifecycleState ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Rejected"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The terminal lifecycle state for a candidate review declined to formalize — recorded rather than deleted, so the decision (and its negative case) is auditable. Wire value `rejected`."@x-gmeow-english .

# ── Closed value class: the five discharge conditions ────────────────────────────

logic:DischargeCondition
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Discharge Condition"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed five-member value class of the logic:obligationDischargeCondition facet: the condition under which a logic:NonEntailmentObligation's absence-of-proof is conclusively checkable. Its individuals are logic:DischargeCertifiedFragment, logic:DischargeFiniteClosure, logic:DischargeSyntacticReachability, logic:DischargeConservativeExtension and logic:DischargeBoundedCorpus. The foundation engine wires logic:DischargeSyntacticReachability and logic:DischargeFiniteClosure; the other three are named but not yet engine-backed, so an obligation declaring one of them is a hard error rather than a silent pass. The set is closed, so a misspelt condition names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:DischargeCertifiedFragment
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:DischargeCondition ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Certified Fragment"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The discharge condition holding when the check runs within a certified complete fragment (e.g. a Datalog stratum or EL profile over which the chase terminates and is complete). Named in the closed set but not yet engine-backed. Wire value `certified-fragment`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:DischargeFiniteClosure
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:DischargeCondition ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Finite Closure"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The discharge condition holding when a finite materialized derivation graph is available and complete: the obligation is discharged by checking the forbidden predicate is absent from that closure. Engine-backed (the foundation chase over an adversarial fixture). Wire value `finite-closure`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:DischargeSyntacticReachability
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:DischargeCondition ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Syntactic Reachability"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The discharge condition holding when a syntactic dependency/reachability analysis over the rule heads shows the forbidden predicate is unreachable — no rule head unifies with it, directly or through any chain of rule applications. Engine-backed (reachability over the foundation rule strata). Wire value `syntactic-reachability`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:DischargeConservativeExtension
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:DischargeCondition ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Conservative Extension"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The discharge condition holding when a conservative-extension proof establishes the added axioms cannot introduce the forbidden conclusion. Named in the closed set but not yet engine-backed. Wire value `conservative-extension`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:DischargeBoundedCorpus
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:DischargeCondition ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Bounded Corpus"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The discharge condition holding when the obligation is explicitly bounded to a declared corpus or mutation-test space and exhaustive checking within that bound is complete. Named in the closed set but not yet engine-backed. Wire value `bounded-corpus`."@x-gmeow-english .

# ── Closed value class: the discharge verdict ────────────────────────────────────

logic:DischargeVerdict
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Discharge Verdict"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed three-value class of the logic:obligationDischargeVerdict facet: the result an obligation check returns. Its individuals are logic:ObligationDischarged, logic:ObligationUnknown (carried forward, never 'proved absent') and logic:ObligationViolated. The set is closed, so a misspelt verdict names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:ObligationDischarged
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:DischargeVerdict ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Discharged"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The discharge verdict for an obligation conclusively checked within its declared logic:DischargeCondition: the forbidden conclusion is provably not drawn within the stated fragment or bound. Wire value `discharged`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ObligationUnknown
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:DischargeVerdict ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Unknown"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The discharge verdict outside any wired discharge condition: not 'proved absent' but not-yet-discharged, carried forward to the next evaluation cycle or stronger fragment. The honest verdict the semi-decidable canonical logic demands. Wire value `unknown`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ObligationViolated
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:DischargeVerdict ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Violated"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The discharge verdict when the forbidden predicate IS reachable or present in the closure: the obligation is broken and the check is a hard error. Wire value `violated`."@x-gmeow-english .

# ── Closed value class: the semantic-risk class ──────────────────────────────────

logic:SemanticRiskClass
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Semantic Risk Class"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed value class of the logic:candidateSemanticRisk facet: how far a wrong formalization of a candidate would propagate, which makes the reviewer gate proportionate. Its individuals are logic:RiskCoreContaminating, logic:RiskProjectionOnly and logic:RiskAdvisory. The set is closed, so a misspelt class names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:RiskCoreContaminating
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:SemanticRiskClass ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Core Contaminating"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The semantic-risk class for a candidate whose wrong formalization would corrupt the reasoned core — the highest risk, demanding the strictest review. Wire value `core-contaminating`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:RiskProjectionOnly
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:SemanticRiskClass ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Projection Only"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The semantic-risk class for a candidate whose blast radius is confined to a lossy projection surface, leaving the reasoned core intact. Wire value `projection-only`."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:RiskAdvisory
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:SemanticRiskClass ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Advisory"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The semantic-risk class for a candidate with no entailment consequence at all — advisory content, the lightest review. Wire value `advisory`."@x-gmeow-english .

# ── Candidate carrier properties (RBox) ──────────────────────────────────────────

logic:candidateSourceHash
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:FormalizationCandidate ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "candidate source hash"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The content hash of the source text a logic:FormalizationCandidate was extracted from: the anchor that ties the candidate back to the exact prose it formalizes and detects drift if that prose changes. Single-valued, xsd:string. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:candidateExtractionProvenance
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:FormalizationCandidate ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "candidate extraction provenance"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The provenance of a candidate's extraction — what produced it (an extractor identifier, run, or model invocation reference). Records that an automated extraction is exactly that, so it enters at logic:CandidateProposed and earns no canonical force without review. Single-valued, xsd:string. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:candidateScope
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:FormalizationCandidate ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "candidate scope"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The intended scope of a candidate's axiom — the terms, slice, or context it is meant to constrain. Read together with logic:candidateContract (the reasoning semantics it is interpreted under). Single-valued, xsd:string. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:candidateContract
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:FormalizationCandidate ;
    rdfs:range logic:ReasoningContract ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "candidate contract"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to the logic:ReasoningContract (ME1) its proposed axiom would be interpreted under — the semantics that make 'sound' meaningful for it. Single-valued. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate, range logic:ReasoningContract."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:candidateCategory
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:FormalizationCandidate ;
    rdfs:range logic:FormalizationCategory ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "candidate category"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to the logic:FormalizationCategory recording what kind of force its prose carried. Single-valued and REQUIRED: a candidate with no category resolving to the closed set is a hard governance error, never silently bucketed. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate, range logic:FormalizationCategory."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:candidateLifecycle
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:FormalizationCandidate ;
    rdfs:range logic:CandidateLifecycleState ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "candidate lifecycle"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to its current logic:CandidateLifecycleState. Single-valued. logic:CandidateAccepted is the canonical state and is legitimate only with a recorded logic:reviewedBy decision. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate, range logic:CandidateLifecycleState."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:reviewedBy
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:FormalizationCandidate ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "reviewed by"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to the reviewer decision that promoted it — a provenance/agent individual recording who reviewed it and when (range stated in prose, a reviewer provenance node, so the keystone gate is machine-auditable rather than trusting a free literal). Its presence is what a logic:CandidateAccepted candidate is checked against. Single-valued. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:candidatePositiveCase
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:FormalizationCandidate ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "candidate positive case"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to a positive competency case its proposed axiom must satisfy — a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion whose expected answer the axiom should produce (range gmeow:CompetencyQuestion, stated in prose). Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:candidateNegativeCase
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:FormalizationCandidate ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "candidate negative case"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to a negative case or countermodel — a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion the axiom must NOT satisfy, recording the boundary the formalization must respect (range gmeow:CompetencyQuestion, stated in prose). Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:candidateNonEntailment
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:FormalizationCandidate ;
    rdfs:range logic:NonEntailmentObligation ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "candidate non-entailment"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to a logic:NonEntailmentObligation its axiom is required to respect — the forbidden conclusion the formalization must not let the engine draw. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate, range logic:NonEntailmentObligation."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:candidateProjectionBehavior
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:FormalizationCandidate ;
    rdfs:range logic:PreservationKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "candidate projection behavior"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to the logic:PreservationKind its axiom would carry under projection — how faithfully it survives down-projection to OWL/Datalog/SHACL. Reuses the loss-ledger preservation polarity rather than minting a parallel note. Single-valued. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate, range logic:PreservationKind."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:candidateSemanticRisk
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:FormalizationCandidate ;
    rdfs:range logic:SemanticRiskClass ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "candidate semantic risk"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to its logic:SemanticRiskClass — how far a wrong formalization would propagate, which sets how strict the reviewer gate must be. Single-valued. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate, range logic:SemanticRiskClass."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

# ── Obligation carrier properties (RBox) ─────────────────────────────────────────

logic:obligationForbiddenPredicate
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:NonEntailmentObligation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:anyURI ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "obligation forbidden predicate"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The IRI of the predicate a logic:NonEntailmentObligation forbids the closure from ever containing (and forbids any rule head from producing). The check reads this IRI, then either proves it unreachable over the rule strata (logic:DischargeSyntacticReachability) or absent from the materialized closure (logic:DischargeFiniteClosure). Single-valued, xsd:anyURI. Domain logic:NonEntailmentObligation."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:obligationDischargeCondition
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:NonEntailmentObligation ;
    rdfs:range logic:DischargeCondition ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "obligation discharge condition"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:NonEntailmentObligation to the logic:DischargeCondition under which its absence-of-proof is conclusively checkable. An obligation declaring a condition the engine does not wire (anything other than logic:DischargeSyntacticReachability or logic:DischargeFiniteClosure) is a hard error, never a silent pass. Domain logic:NonEntailmentObligation, range logic:DischargeCondition."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:obligationDischargeVerdict
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:NonEntailmentObligation ;
    rdfs:range logic:DischargeVerdict ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "obligation discharge verdict"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:NonEntailmentObligation to the logic:DischargeVerdict the check returned — logic:ObligationDischarged, logic:ObligationUnknown or logic:ObligationViolated. Computed by the engine, not asserted by hand. Domain logic:NonEntailmentObligation, range logic:DischargeVerdict."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:ProjectionLoss
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Projection Loss"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An in-band declaration that a lossy projection dropped structure its source carried — emitted into the projected graph itself, never a sidecar. GTS stays lossless; loss is declared only at the exit gate (Principle 17 / Principle 4). A loss-aware SPARQL CONSTRUCT mints one when its template omits an RDF-1.2 reification layer that its WHERE matched, so a downstream consumer of the projection can see exactly what was shed."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:lossCode
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "loss code"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "The stable machine code of a logic:ProjectionLoss — reifier-layer-dropped, annotation-layer-dropped, or standpoint-scope-dropped — naming exactly which structure the projection shed. The codes are shared verbatim with the conversion loss ledger so in-band and contract-level loss declarations agree."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:lostReifies
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:ProjectionLoss ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "lost reifies"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Points from a logic:ProjectionLoss to the RDF-1.2 triple term whose reifier (and any annotations) the projection dropped, so a consumer can recover which statement lost its reification layer. The object is a quoted triple term; its range is intentionally left open (stated in prose) to keep the OWL down-projection DL-clean."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

# ── The Correspondence calculus (the ninth node kind's spine) ─────────────────────
# Cross-ontology alignment as a first-class, law-bearing logic: object. A
# logic:Correspondence (declared above as the ninth logic:NodeKind) wraps a logic:Lens —
# its executable get/put core — in a meta-formula envelope: a typed
# logic:CorrespondenceRelation on an ordered lattice, an algebraic logic:MorphismClass on
# the ordered law-spine, the separated quantitative axes (logic:confidence,
# logic:evidenceStrength, logic:weight, logic:probability) plus logic:Determinacy, the
# claimed logic:LawClaim constraints (whose discharge reuses the logic:DischargeVerdict /
# logic:DischargeCondition vocabulary of the foundation), and a standpoint index. SSSOM,
# EDOAL, FnO, SPARQL CONSTRUCT and the OWL-alignment axioms are generated lowerings of this
# one object, never second sources (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md).

logic:Lens
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Lens"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The executable asymmetric core a logic:Correspondence wraps: a get / put leg pair between a rich source S and a derived view V, with get : S → V the down-projection and put : V × S → S the up-projection. GMEOW is always the source S and the external vocabulary the view V, so down-projection (GMEOW → external) is the get leg and up-projection (external → GMEOW) is the put leg. The view is the smaller, derived thing; put folds a possibly-fresh view back into the rich source, and the ingest-with-no-prior-state case (S empty) is exactly where a witness must travel in the view — the mnemomorphism a logic:Correspondence records with logic:mnemomorphic. Both legs are logic:TransactionProgram bodies over the path semantics of the transaction layer and logic:PathShape — no new pattern language is introduced. Distinguished from logic:Correspondence, which wraps this lens with the relation, the quantitative axes, the law claims and the standpoint envelope (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, the orientation-convention section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:CorrespondenceRelation
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Correspondence Relation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The typed, closed value class of a logic:Correspondence's relation, on an ordered lattice rather than a free string: logic:Equiv ⊐ { logic:Subsumes, logic:SubsumedBy } ⊐ logic:Overlaps ⊐ logic:RelatedMatch, with logic:Disjoint the negative pole. From one authored relation the compiler derives the SSSOM predicate, the EDOAL relation symbol and the OWL-alignment-axiom strength, so the generated alignment artifacts cannot drift apart. The set is closed, so a misspelt relation names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, the relation-lattice section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Equiv
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:CorrespondenceRelation ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "equivalent"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The top of the correspondence-relation lattice: the source pattern and the view pattern denote one and the same extension. Lowers to sssom:exactMatch and (when the logic:MorphismClass and logic:LawClaim set support it) owl:equivalentClass; the strongest claim, never licensed for a commitment-shifting bridge."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Subsumes
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:CorrespondenceRelation ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "subsumes"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The source pattern is broader than the view: every view instance is a source instance but not conversely. Lowers to sssom:broadMatch and an owl:subClassOf with the view as the subclass. One of the two mid-lattice directional relations under logic:Equiv."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:SubsumedBy
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:CorrespondenceRelation ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "subsumed by"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The source pattern is narrower than the view: every source instance is a view instance but not conversely. Lowers to sssom:narrowMatch and an owl:subClassOf with the source as the subclass. The converse direction of logic:Subsumes, the second mid-lattice relation under logic:Equiv."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Overlaps
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:CorrespondenceRelation ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "overlaps"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Source and view share instances without either subsuming the other: a partial, caveated alignment. Lowers to sssom:closeMatch (an OWL equivalence is unsupported and the overclaim gate refuses one). Below the directional band, above logic:RelatedMatch. Distinct from the mereological relation logic:overlaps (shared parts of one whole); this is a relation between two aligned patterns."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:RelatedMatch
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:CorrespondenceRelation ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "related match"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The weakest positive relation: source and view are associated (curatorially relevant) but neither equivalent, subsuming nor reliably overlapping. Lowers to sssom:relatedMatch only; no logical alignment axiom is emitted. The floor of the positive lattice, above only the negative pole logic:Disjoint."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Disjoint
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:CorrespondenceRelation ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "disjoint match"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The negative pole of the correspondence-relation lattice: source and view share no instances, an asserted non-alignment. Lowers to owl:disjointWith. Distinct from the mereological relation logic:disjoint (two entities sharing no part); this records that two aligned patterns are deliberately kept apart."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:MorphismClass
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Morphism Class"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The ordered law-spine of a logic:Correspondence: how much invertibility it may lawfully claim, where each rung caps the laws the correspondence may assert. From strongest to floor the seven rungs are logic:Isomorphism, logic:SectionRetraction, logic:WellBehavedLens, logic:LossyLens, logic:Prism, logic:AffineCorrespondence and logic:BridgeView. The spine fuses the profunctor-optic lattice with the categorical subobject notion; composition can only weaken the rung, never strengthen it, and a logic:mnemomorphic witness is what lets a correspondence climb it. The set is closed, so a misspelt class names no declared rung and is rejected (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, the ordered-law-spine section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Isomorphism
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:MorphismClass ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Isomorphism"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The top rung: an iso, get ∘ put = id and put ∘ get = id, a full round-trip in both directions. The only rung that licenses a confidence-1.0 equivalence. Caps: both round-trip laws claimable."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:SectionRetraction
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:MorphismClass ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Section / Retraction"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Perfect subsumption: a split mono with put ∘ get = id_S and get ∘ put idempotent on V ⊕ complement. The source embeds losslessly into the view, the augmentation being S ∖ im(get) carried in the in-band complement. Caps: the section law (lossless source recovery), but not full bidirectional iso."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:WellBehavedLens
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:MorphismClass ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Well-Behaved Lens"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An asymmetric lens: a structured-to-flat downcast with sound update. Caps: logic:GetPut and logic:PutGet claimable (logic:PutPut optional). The workhorse rung for a faithful but non-embedding projection."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:LossyLens
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:MorphismClass ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Lossy Lens"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A lens with non-injective get: one direction is faithful but the inverse needs a witness, a co-authored put-with-claim, or declared defaults. Most schema.org / FOAF downcasts live here. Caps: a single faithful direction; the put leg may not claim recovery without a logic:mnemomorphic witness."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Prism
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:MorphismClass ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Prism"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A partial map S → V + S that matches and builds only on the in-focus case of a sum or optional: the optic for 'this correspondence applies when the source is of a particular variant, otherwise it passes through.' Caps: match / build laws on the in-focus case only. Paired with logic:AffineCorrespondence as the partial-alignment band below logic:LossyLens."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:AffineCorrespondence
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:MorphismClass ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Affine Correspondence"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A co-projection onto a shared component: the 'similar but not quite' alignment, where source and view agree on a common part but neither embeds in the other. The companion of logic:Prism in the partial-alignment band — a Prism focuses an optional variant, an affine correspondence focuses a shared sub-structure. The correct rung for a logic:Vague logic:Determinacy target, NOT a low-confidence logic:Equiv. Caps: laws on the shared component only."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:BridgeView
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:MorphismClass ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Bridge View"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The floor rung: a commitment-shifting comorphism with NO satisfaction-preservation claim — the alignment to BFO, DOLCE, SUMO or YAMATO. A bridge view carries logic:morphismKind logic:CommitmentShiftingBridge, and the loss ledger refuses to emit owl:equivalentClass for it. Caps: no preservation law; the alignment is a by-reference bridge, never an identity."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:MorphismKind
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Morphism Kind"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed two-value qualifier, orthogonal to the logic:MorphismClass rung, recording the institution-theoretic split between a satisfaction-preserving morphism (logic:InstitutionMorphism) and a commitment-shifting bridge (logic:CommitmentShiftingBridge). This is the distinction the foundation already draws between a truth-preserving down-projection and a by-reference bridge; the loss ledger refuses owl:equivalentClass for the bridge kind. The set is closed, so a misspelt kind names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, the ordered-law-spine section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:InstitutionMorphism
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:MorphismKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Institution Morphism"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A satisfaction-preserving morphism between theories presented as institutions: truth in the source maps to truth in the view, so logical alignment axioms (up to owl:equivalentClass when the rung allows) are licensed. The morphism kind of a faithful down-projection."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:CommitmentShiftingBridge
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:MorphismKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Commitment-Shifting Bridge"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A bridge that shifts ontological commitment rather than preserving satisfaction: the kind borne by a logic:BridgeView alignment to a top-level ontology (BFO, DOLCE, SUMO, YAMATO). The loss ledger refuses to emit owl:equivalentClass for it; the bridge is adopted by reference (Principle 5), never as an identity collapse."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Determinacy
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Determinacy"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed two-value axis recording whether the TARGET RELATIONSHIP a logic:Correspondence asserts is ontically crisp (logic:Crisp) or vague (logic:Vague). It is separate from logic:confidence: 'similar but not quite' is logic:Vague determinacy with a logic:AffineCorrespondence class, NOT a low-confidence logic:Equiv. Conflating the two destroys the distinction between an uncertain sharp claim and a confident fuzzy one. The set is closed, so a misspelt value names no declared determinacy and is rejected (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, the quantitative-and-contextual-axes section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Crisp
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:Determinacy ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "crisp"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The target relationship is ontically sharp: the alignment either holds or does not, with no borderline cases. The determinacy of an equivalence or a clean subsumption."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Vague
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:Determinacy ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "vague"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The target relationship is ontically fuzzy: it holds to a degree or only on a shared component, with genuine borderline cases. Paired with a logic:AffineCorrespondence class for the 'similar but not quite' alignment — vagueness in the world, not uncertainty in the curator."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:CorrespondenceLaw
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Correspondence Law"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed value class of the lens laws a logic:Correspondence can claim through a logic:LawClaim: logic:GetPut, logic:PutGet, logic:PutPut and logic:SectionLaw. Which laws are claimable is capped by the correspondence's logic:MorphismClass rung, and each claim carries a logic:DischargeVerdict. The set is closed, so a misspelt law names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, the ninth-node-kind section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:GetPut
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:CorrespondenceLaw ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "GetPut"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The lens law put(get(s), s) = s: getting a view from a source and immediately putting it back leaves the source unchanged. Claimable from the logic:WellBehavedLens rung upward; the acquisition-stability law."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:PutGet
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:CorrespondenceLaw ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "PutGet"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The lens law get(put(v, s)) = v: putting a view into a source and reading it back yields exactly that view. Claimable from the logic:WellBehavedLens rung upward; the update-faithfulness law."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:PutPut
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:CorrespondenceLaw ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "PutPut"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The very-well-behaved lens law put(v2, put(v1, s)) = put(v2, s): a later put overwrites an earlier one with no residue. Optional even at the logic:WellBehavedLens rung; claimed only by correspondences whose put leg is genuinely history-free."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:SectionLaw
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:CorrespondenceLaw ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Section Law"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The perfect-subsumption law put ∘ get = id_S: the source is recovered exactly from its view because the in-band complement retained everything the retraction needs (a logic:mnemomorphic witness). Claimable only at the logic:SectionRetraction rung or above; the CI-checkable form of 'GMEOW perfectly subsumes this vocabulary.'"@x-gmeow-english .

logic:LawClaim
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Law Claim"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A claim that a logic:Correspondence satisfies a particular logic:CorrespondenceLaw (named by logic:lawClaimed), together with the discharge state of that claim: a logic:DischargeVerdict via logic:lawDischargeVerdict and, when applicable, the logic:DischargeCondition under which it was checked via logic:lawDischargeCondition. It reuses the foundation's executable discharge vocabulary rather than a parallel status enum: a law proved within a certified fragment is logic:ObligationDischarged under logic:DischargeCertifiedFragment; a refuted law is logic:ObligationViolated with its countermodel; an authored-but-unchecked or inconclusive law is logic:ObligationUnknown, carried forward. The overclaim gate fires when a correspondence claims a law its lowered legs do not satisfy (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, the preservation-is-the-lens-law-framework section)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Dialect
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Dialect"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A named sub-language of the canonical logic: IR, in the MLIR sense of a dialect with its own node verifiers and progressive lowering (not an LLVM-style substrate). The one F1 dialect is logic:RelationalCore, the logical-to-physical lowering waist between the full IR and the native execution engine."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:RelationalCore
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:Dialect ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Relational Core"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logical-to-physical lowering waist of the correspondence calculus: a first-class Datalog±-with-stratified-negation sub-language (with aggregation and existentials — the chase) between the full-FOL logic: IR and the native execution engine. Every execution strategy, the incremental layer and the semiring annotation that carries the quantitative axes target this one dialect, so a get leg compiles to a join plan and a put / chase to a semi-naive fixpoint with existentials over the same core (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md and design/LOGIC-IR.md, the IR-commitments section)."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:hasLens
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:range logic:Lens ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "has lens"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:Correspondence to the logic:Lens that is its executable get / put core. Single-valued: each correspondence wraps exactly one lens, around which it adds the relation, axes, law claims and standpoint envelope. Range logic:Lens (domain stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:getLeg
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:Lens ;
    rdfs:range logic:TransactionProgram ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "get leg"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:Lens to the logic:TransactionProgram that realizes its get leg — the down-projection get : S → V from the GMEOW source to the external view. Reuses the transaction layer's path semantics and logic:PathShape; no new pattern language. Domain logic:Lens, range logic:TransactionProgram."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:putLeg
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:Lens ;
    rdfs:range logic:TransactionProgram ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "put leg"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:Lens to the logic:TransactionProgram that realizes its put leg — the up-projection put : V × S → S folding a view back into the rich GMEOW source. A lawful put comes only from a logic:mnemomorphic witness or a co-authored put-with-claim; naive backward execution of the get leg is a candidate preimage, never a lawful put. Domain logic:Lens, range logic:TransactionProgram."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:correspondenceRelation
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:range logic:CorrespondenceRelation ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "correspondence relation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:Correspondence to its logic:CorrespondenceRelation on the ordered lattice (equiv ⊐ subsumes / subsumedBy ⊐ overlaps ⊐ relatedMatch, disjoint the negative pole). The single authored relation from which the SSSOM predicate, EDOAL symbol and OWL-alignment strength are derived. Range logic:CorrespondenceRelation (domain stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:morphismClass
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:range logic:MorphismClass ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "morphism class"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:Correspondence to its rung on the ordered law-spine (logic:MorphismClass), which caps the logic:CorrespondenceLaw values it may claim. Composition can only weaken this rung. Range logic:MorphismClass (domain stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:morphismKind
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:range logic:MorphismKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "morphism kind"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:Correspondence to its logic:MorphismKind — the satisfaction-preserving / commitment-shifting split orthogonal to the rung. A logic:CommitmentShiftingBridge value makes the loss ledger refuse owl:equivalentClass. Range logic:MorphismKind (domain stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:hasDeterminacy
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:range logic:Determinacy ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "has determinacy"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:Correspondence to its logic:Determinacy — whether the target relationship is ontically logic:Crisp or logic:Vague. Kept separate from logic:confidence so a vague-but-confident alignment is not mis-recorded as a low-confidence equivalence. Range logic:Determinacy (domain stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:mnemomorphic
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "mnemomorphic"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Whether a logic:Correspondence's forward get leg retains a source witness — factoring through the graph of the correspondence so that put is obtained by projecting along the retained witness rather than synthesizing a plausible source. The bit is orthogonal to the logic:MorphismClass rung but is what lets a correspondence climb it: a retained witness is what discharges put ∘ get = id (the logic:SectionLaw), the dividing line between recoverable subsumption and reconstructed approximation. True or false (default false); a false value bars any section / retraction claim. Range xsd:boolean (domain left open, like logic:loadBearing)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:hasLawClaim
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:range logic:LawClaim ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "has law claim"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:Correspondence to a logic:LawClaim it makes — a claimed logic:CorrespondenceLaw with its discharge state. Multi-valued: a correspondence may claim several laws, each capped by its logic:MorphismClass rung. Range logic:LawClaim (domain stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:lawClaimed
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:LawClaim ;
    rdfs:range logic:CorrespondenceLaw ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "law claimed"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:LawClaim to the logic:CorrespondenceLaw it asserts (logic:GetPut, logic:PutGet, logic:PutPut or logic:SectionLaw). Domain logic:LawClaim, range logic:CorrespondenceLaw."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:lawDischargeVerdict
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:LawClaim ;
    rdfs:range logic:DischargeVerdict ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "law discharge verdict"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:LawClaim to the logic:DischargeVerdict its check returned — logic:ObligationDischarged, logic:ObligationUnknown or logic:ObligationViolated. Reuses the foundation's discharge-verdict value class (the law-claim analogue of logic:obligationDischargeVerdict, which is domain-locked to logic:NonEntailmentObligation): an unchecked or inconclusive law is logic:ObligationUnknown, never silently passed. Domain logic:LawClaim, range logic:DischargeVerdict."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:lawDischargeCondition
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:LawClaim ;
    rdfs:range logic:DischargeCondition ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "law discharge condition"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:LawClaim to the logic:DischargeCondition under which its logic:lawDischargeVerdict is conclusively checkable (for example logic:DischargeCertifiedFragment for a law proved within a certified complete fragment). Optional: a law carrying logic:ObligationUnknown with no condition is an authored-but-unverified claim. Reuses the foundation's discharge-condition value class. Domain logic:LawClaim, range logic:DischargeCondition."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

# ── Cognitive assessment: the canonical multidimensional cognitive record ────────
# A reified, vantage-indexed, multidimensional assessment of how good some reasoning
# is or how capable a reasoner is. The single ordinal knowledge ladder of the
# cognition slice is a generated coarse view of this; the factored assessment is the
# canonical record. Normative in design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md.

logic:CognitiveAssessment
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Cognitive Assessment"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The canonical record of how good some reasoning is, or how capable a reasoner is: a reified, vantage-indexed node naming exactly one logic:AssessmentDimension and carrying its assessed agent (logic:assessedAgent), subject and granularity (logic:assessmentSubject with logic:subjectGranularity), task or context (logic:assessmentContext), scale and level (logic:assessmentScale with logic:assessmentLevel), evaluator and standpoint (logic:assessmentEvaluator, attributed via gmeow:accordingTo), evidence (logic:assessmentEvidence), method (logic:assessmentMethod), valid interval (carried by gmeow:duringInterval) and the strength with which the judgment itself is held (carried by logic:confidence). The dimensions vary independently, so a single ordinal familiarity-to-mastery scale collapses exactly the distinctions an assessment exists to draw; the construct keeps them factored. A self-assessment and an observer's assessment of the same agent are two coexisting records, never reconciled into one verdict, and because the node is reified an assessment is itself a subject another assessment can range over — an evaluation of the evaluator — with no new machinery. The convenient ordinal reading is the lossy coarse-ladder projection of this assessment, exactly as logic:AgencyAssessment projects the unary 'this holon is integral'; a reliability assessment is a logic:CognitiveAssessment on the reliability dimension over a series of runs, distinct from the single-run logic:ResultAssurance. Normative in design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:AssessmentDimension
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Assessment Dimension"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The value-vocabulary class of the factored axis a logic:CognitiveAssessment judges, named via logic:assessmentDimension. An OPEN value vocabulary (individuals, never subclasses): a new dimension is a new individual rather than a reshaping of the construct, the same orthogonal-factorization discipline the foundation applies to claim modality and contextual scope. The dimensions vary independently — an assessment on one says nothing about another — and an assessment names exactly one."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:SubjectGranularity
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Subject Granularity"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The value-vocabulary class of the grain of a logic:CognitiveAssessment's subject, named via logic:subjectGranularity: a single inference, a body of reasoning, a domain of competence, or the reasoner as a whole. An OPEN value vocabulary (individuals, never subclasses), since competence is judged at different grains and a new grain is a new individual."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:AssessmentLevel
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Assessment Level"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The value-vocabulary class of an ordinal level on an assessment's scale, the object of logic:assessmentLevel and logic:thresholdLevel when the scale is ordinal. An OPEN, ordered value vocabulary (logic:levelNone ≺ logic:levelEmerging ≺ logic:levelCompetent ≺ logic:levelStrong), ordered by logic:levelAtOrAbove so that 'a level at or above a threshold' is well-defined for the coarse-ladder projection without a numeric comparison (which would force a procedural profile). An assessment whose scale is continuous carries a literal logic:assessmentLevel instead; the ordinal levels are the projection scale."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:assessedAgent
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:CognitiveAssessment ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "assessed agent"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The agent role of a logic:CognitiveAssessment: whose cognition is judged. Range gmeow:Agent (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). A well-formedness existence guard — every projection rule re-binds it, so a malformed assessment naming no agent receives no ladder edge."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:assessmentSubject
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:CognitiveAssessment ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "assessment subject"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The subject role of a logic:CognitiveAssessment: what the assessment is about — a single inference, a body of reasoning, a domain of competence, or the agent as a whole. Its grain is carried by logic:subjectGranularity. Range is left open (stated in prose), since the subject may be reasoning, a domain entity, or the reasoner itself."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:subjectGranularity
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:CognitiveAssessment ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "subject granularity"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:CognitiveAssessment to the logic:SubjectGranularity individual recording the grain of its logic:assessmentSubject (inference, body-of-reasoning, domain, or agent). Range logic:SubjectGranularity (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:assessmentContext
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:CognitiveAssessment ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "assessment context"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The task or context a logic:CognitiveAssessment holds for, since competence is context-relative: the same agent may be competent on one task and not on another, so an assessment without a context underdetermines what it claims. Range is left open (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:assessmentDimension
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:CognitiveAssessment ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "assessment dimension"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The single factored axis a logic:CognitiveAssessment judges: a logic:AssessmentDimension individual. An assessment names exactly one; the dimensions vary independently. Range logic:AssessmentDimension (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:assessmentScale
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:CognitiveAssessment ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "assessment scale"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The named scale, ordinal or continuous, on which a logic:CognitiveAssessment's logic:assessmentLevel is read. Range is left open (stated in prose), since a scale may be the native ordinal logic:AssessmentLevel vocabulary or a foreign scale (Bloom's, SOLO, a Brier-scored continuous range)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:assessmentLevel
    a rdf:Property ;
    rdfs:domain logic:CognitiveAssessment ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "assessment level"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The value a logic:CognitiveAssessment takes on its logic:assessmentScale: an ordinal logic:AssessmentLevel individual when the scale is ordinal (the case the coarse-ladder projection reads), or a continuous literal otherwise (a Brier or logarithmic score on a continuous scale). Because the range spans both an individual and a literal it is a plain rdf:Property, not an owl:ObjectProperty (which could not carry the continuous literal) — the same open-range convention the module states in prose elsewhere."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:assessmentEvaluator
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:CognitiveAssessment ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "assessment evaluator"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Who holds the judgment of a logic:CognitiveAssessment: the standpoint is attributed via gmeow:accordingTo, so a self-assessment (evaluator = assessed agent) and an observer's assessment coexist as two records rather than collapsing into one verdict. Range gmeow:Agent (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:assessmentEvidence
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:CognitiveAssessment ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "assessment evidence"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The reasoning, observations, or recorded episode a logic:CognitiveAssessment rests on — the inference commitments it cites, the gmeow:ModelInvocation that produced the reasoning, the results it grades — so an assessment is auditable against the reasoning it judges rather than standing apart from it. Range is left open (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:assessmentMethod
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:CognitiveAssessment ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "assessment method"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "How the judgment of a logic:CognitiveAssessment was reached — a test, a review, a scoring rule applied to a forecast series, an introspective report. Range is left open (stated in prose), so the method may be a named procedure or a free description."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:levelAtOrAbove
    a owl:ObjectProperty ,
        owl:TransitiveProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:AssessmentLevel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "level at or above"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range logic:AssessmentLevel ;
    skos:definition "Orders the ordinal assessment scale: relates a logic:AssessmentLevel to itself and to every level it surpasses (logic:levelStrong logic:levelAtOrAbove logic:levelCompetent). Reflexive-and-transitive on the levels, so the coarse-ladder projection can test 'the assessed level is at or above the threshold level' by a single body atom, with no numeric comparison (which would force a procedural profile). The full reflexive-transitive closure is asserted on the level individuals so the test needs no transitive computation in the rule engine."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

# The eight factored dimensions of design §The factored dimensions, plus the
# separately-introduced reliability dimension of design §Result assurance and
# reasoner reliability are distinct — nine logic:AssessmentDimension individuals.

logic:dimensionAwareness
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:AssessmentDimension ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "dimension: awareness"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The awareness dimension: whether the agent registers the subject at all. The shallowest factored axis; the source of the gmeow:isAwareOf rung of the coarse knowledge ladder under a declared threshold."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:dimensionDeclarativeFamiliarity
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:AssessmentDimension ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "dimension: declarative familiarity"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The declarative-familiarity dimension: what the agent knows THAT — the facts it can state about the subject. The source of the gmeow:knowsAbout rung of the coarse knowledge ladder under a declared threshold."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:dimensionConceptualUnderstanding
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:AssessmentDimension ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "dimension: conceptual understanding"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The conceptual-understanding dimension: whether the agent grasps WHY — the structure behind the facts, beyond reciting them. The source of the gmeow:understands rung of the coarse knowledge ladder under a declared threshold."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:dimensionProceduralCompetence
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:AssessmentDimension ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "dimension: procedural competence"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The procedural-competence dimension: what the agent knows HOW to do — its working command of the subject. Read together with the transfer dimension, the source of the gmeow:hasMastered rung of the coarse knowledge ladder under a declared threshold."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:dimensionTransfer
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:AssessmentDimension ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "dimension: transfer"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The transfer dimension: whether competence in one context carries to another — the axis a single ordinal ladder most conspicuously hides, since fluency in a narrow task says nothing about generalization. Read together with procedural competence, the source of the gmeow:hasMastered rung of the coarse knowledge ladder under a declared threshold."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:dimensionExplanatoryAbility
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:AssessmentDimension ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "dimension: explanatory ability"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The explanatory-ability dimension: whether the agent can produce an account others can follow and check — the seam to the solver-layer gmeow:explanatoryScore and gmeow:systematicity measurements, which feed this dimension but are never asserted as reasoned axioms."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:dimensionCalibration
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:AssessmentDimension ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "dimension: calibration"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The calibration dimension: whether the agent's confidence matches its accuracy. Assessed against an explicit forecast protocol (a forecast/outcome series, a scoring rule, a reference class and observation window), kept apart from a single logic:confidence value and from the metacognition vocabulary's qualitative gmeow:CalibrationStatus."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:dimensionMetacognition
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:AssessmentDimension ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "dimension: metacognition"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The metacognition dimension: whether the agent models its own competence, including the limits of its own knowledge. Reads the metacognition vocabulary's second-order posture — gmeow:awareOfNotKnowing, gmeow:epistemicSelfTrust, and reflection that can defeat one's own inference — as its subject."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:dimensionReliability
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:AssessmentDimension ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "dimension: reliability"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The reliability dimension: how dependably an agent or engine reasons as a disposition, relative to a reference class (a task, domain, or distribution) and read from MANY results with their expected or observed outcomes — a metric over the series (accuracy, soundness-violation rate, recall, calibration, robustness) across a stated interval. Distinct from the single-run logic:ResultAssurance: a reliable reasoner may correctly return a contradiction verdict on contradictory input, and a completed internally-supported result may still be wrong, so reliability is never read from one result's assurance. The dimension design §Result assurance and reasoner reliability are distinct introduces alongside the eight factored dimensions."@x-gmeow-english .

# Subject granularity — four grains at which competence is judged.

logic:granularityInference
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:SubjectGranularity ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "granularity: inference"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The finest grain of an assessment subject: a single inference — one logic:InferenceProcess or commitment being judged."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:granularityBodyOfReasoning
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:SubjectGranularity ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "granularity: body of reasoning"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An intermediate grain of an assessment subject: a connected body of reasoning — a derivation, a proof, an episode of inference — judged as a whole rather than one step."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:granularityDomain
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:SubjectGranularity ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "granularity: domain"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A broad grain of an assessment subject: a domain of competence — the agent's standing in a field rather than on any one episode."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:granularityAgent
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:SubjectGranularity ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "granularity: agent"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The coarsest grain of an assessment subject: the reasoner as a whole — the grain at which a reliability assessment of an agent or engine is made."@x-gmeow-english .

# The ordinal projection scale — four levels, reflexive-transitively ordered by
# logic:levelAtOrAbove so a threshold test is a single body atom.

logic:levelNone
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:AssessmentLevel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "level: none"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The lowest ordinal assessment level: the dimension is not evidenced at all. Clears no ladder rung's threshold."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:levelAtOrAbove logic:levelNone .

logic:levelEmerging
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:AssessmentLevel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "level: emerging"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The second ordinal assessment level: the dimension is weakly evidenced. Surpasses logic:levelNone on the logic:levelAtOrAbove order."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:levelAtOrAbove logic:levelEmerging ,
        logic:levelNone .

logic:levelCompetent
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:AssessmentLevel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "level: competent"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The third ordinal assessment level: the dimension is solidly evidenced. Surpasses logic:levelEmerging and logic:levelNone on the logic:levelAtOrAbove order."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:levelAtOrAbove logic:levelCompetent ,
        logic:levelEmerging ,
        logic:levelNone .

logic:levelStrong
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:AssessmentLevel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "level: strong"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The highest ordinal assessment level: the dimension is strongly evidenced. Surpasses every lower level on the logic:levelAtOrAbove order."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:levelAtOrAbove logic:levelStrong ,
        logic:levelCompetent ,
        logic:levelEmerging ,
        logic:levelNone .

# ── The coarse knowledge ladder as a generated projection ───────────────────────
# The cognition slice's gmeow:isAwareOf … gmeow:hasMastered ladder is a generated
# coarse VIEW of the multidimensional logic:CognitiveAssessment: each ladder edge
# instance is rule-materialized from assessments under a declared per-dimension
# threshold profile (logic:LadderProjectionProfile). The factored assessment stays
# the canonical record; the ladder is the readable ordinal projection. The shipped
# projection rules are positive Horn, so they materialize under the engine's default
# semantics and fold into gmeow.gts and the datalog/N3/Nemo program projections.
# Normative in design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md §Projection to the coarse knowledge ladder.

logic:LadderProjectionProfile
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Ladder Projection Profile"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A declared per-dimension threshold profile governing the generated coarse projection of the multidimensional logic:CognitiveAssessment onto the gmeow:isAwareOf … gmeow:hasMastered knowledge ladder: a set of logic:DimensionThreshold rows (logic:hasThresholdRow), each binding a ladder edge to its source dimension and the minimum logic:AssessmentLevel an assessment must clear for the edge to be emitted. Making the thresholds an explicit profile keeps the ordinal chain a projection a consumer that needs one number can read, while the factored assessment stays canonical — the ladder never re-establishes mastery, understanding, knowledge and awareness as a single ordinal entailment chain in place of the independent dimensions."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:DimensionThreshold
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Dimension Threshold"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "One row of a logic:LadderProjectionProfile: a logic:projectsLadderEdge ladder property paired with the logic:sourceDimension it reads and the minimum logic:thresholdLevel an assessment on that dimension must clear (by the logic:levelAtOrAbove order) for the edge to be emitted. The gmeow:hasMastered rung is the only one with two rows — procedural competence and transfer — both of which must clear, so mastery of one narrow task no longer implies broad command of a subject."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:hasThresholdRow
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:LadderProjectionProfile ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "has threshold row"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:LadderProjectionProfile to one of its logic:DimensionThreshold rows. Range logic:DimensionThreshold (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:projectsLadderEdge
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:DimensionThreshold ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "projects ladder edge"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The ladder property a logic:DimensionThreshold row emits when its dimension clears its threshold: gmeow:isAwareOf, gmeow:knowsAbout, gmeow:understands or gmeow:hasMastered. Range is left open (the gmeow: ladder properties), stated in prose to keep the OWL down-projection clean."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:sourceDimension
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:DimensionThreshold ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "source dimension"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:AssessmentDimension a logic:DimensionThreshold row reads: the factored axis whose assessment level is tested against the row's logic:thresholdLevel. Range logic:AssessmentDimension (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:thresholdLevel
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:DimensionThreshold ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "threshold level"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The minimum logic:AssessmentLevel an assessment on a row's logic:sourceDimension must reach — by the logic:levelAtOrAbove order — for the row's logic:projectsLadderEdge to be emitted. Range logic:AssessmentLevel (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

# The shipped default profile: the threshold each ladder rung clears.

logic:defaultLadderProfile
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:LadderProjectionProfile ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "default ladder projection profile"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The shipped default logic:LadderProjectionProfile the coarse-ladder projection rules read: awareness ≥ emerging emits gmeow:isAwareOf, declarative familiarity ≥ competent emits gmeow:knowsAbout, conceptual understanding ≥ competent emits gmeow:understands, and procedural competence ≥ strong together with transfer ≥ strong emit gmeow:hasMastered."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:hasThresholdRow logic:ladderRowAwareness ,
        logic:ladderRowDeclarative ,
        logic:ladderRowConceptual ,
        logic:ladderRowProceduralMastery ,
        logic:ladderRowTransferMastery .

logic:ladderRowAwareness
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:DimensionThreshold ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "ladder row: awareness → is aware of"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The default-profile row emitting gmeow:isAwareOf when the awareness dimension reaches logic:levelEmerging."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:projectsLadderEdge gmeow:isAwareOf ;
    logic:sourceDimension logic:dimensionAwareness ;
    logic:thresholdLevel logic:levelEmerging .

logic:ladderRowDeclarative
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:DimensionThreshold ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "ladder row: declarative familiarity → knows about"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The default-profile row emitting gmeow:knowsAbout when the declarative-familiarity dimension reaches logic:levelCompetent."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:projectsLadderEdge gmeow:knowsAbout ;
    logic:sourceDimension logic:dimensionDeclarativeFamiliarity ;
    logic:thresholdLevel logic:levelCompetent .

logic:ladderRowConceptual
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:DimensionThreshold ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "ladder row: conceptual understanding → understands"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The default-profile row emitting gmeow:understands when the conceptual-understanding dimension reaches logic:levelCompetent."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:projectsLadderEdge gmeow:understands ;
    logic:sourceDimension logic:dimensionConceptualUnderstanding ;
    logic:thresholdLevel logic:levelCompetent .

logic:ladderRowProceduralMastery
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:DimensionThreshold ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "ladder row: procedural competence → has mastered"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The procedural half of the default-profile gmeow:hasMastered rung: procedural competence must reach logic:levelStrong. Read together with logic:ladderRowTransferMastery — both must clear for gmeow:hasMastered."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:projectsLadderEdge gmeow:hasMastered ;
    logic:sourceDimension logic:dimensionProceduralCompetence ;
    logic:thresholdLevel logic:levelStrong .

logic:ladderRowTransferMastery
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:DimensionThreshold ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "ladder row: transfer → has mastered"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The transfer half of the default-profile gmeow:hasMastered rung: transfer must reach logic:levelStrong. Read together with logic:ladderRowProceduralMastery — both must clear for gmeow:hasMastered, so mastery of one narrow task never implies broad command."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:projectsLadderEdge gmeow:hasMastered ;
    logic:sourceDimension logic:dimensionTransfer ;
    logic:thresholdLevel logic:levelStrong .

# The four projection rules. The three single-dimension rungs read their dimension
# and threshold from the profile row; the gmeow:hasMastered rung conjoins the two
# rows (procedural AND transfer), so both halves must clear.

logic:ruleProjectIsAwareOf
    a logic:Rule ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "project ladder edge: is aware of"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Emits gmeow:isAwareOf from an assessment whose dimension and level clear the gmeow:isAwareOf row of a logic:LadderProjectionProfile. Positive Horn; the threshold is read from the profile, not hard-coded."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:provenance logic:ruleProjectIsAwareOf ;
    logic:head [
        rdf:subject   "?agent" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:isAwareOf ;
        rdf:object    "?subject"
    ] ;
    logic:body [
        rdf:subject   "?profile" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:hasThresholdRow ;
        rdf:object    "?row"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?row" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:projectsLadderEdge ;
        rdf:object    gmeow:isAwareOf
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?row" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:sourceDimension ;
        rdf:object    "?dim"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?row" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:thresholdLevel ;
        rdf:object    "?threshold"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?assessment" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:assessmentDimension ;
        rdf:object    "?dim"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?assessment" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:assessedAgent ;
        rdf:object    "?agent"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?assessment" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:assessmentSubject ;
        rdf:object    "?subject"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?assessment" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:assessmentLevel ;
        rdf:object    "?level"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?level" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:levelAtOrAbove ;
        rdf:object    "?threshold"
    ] .

logic:ruleProjectKnowsAbout
    a logic:Rule ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "project ladder edge: knows about"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Emits gmeow:knowsAbout from an assessment whose dimension and level clear the gmeow:knowsAbout row of a logic:LadderProjectionProfile. Positive Horn; the threshold is read from the profile. The canonical source of a gmeow:knowsAbout edge — never gmeow:hasSkill."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:provenance logic:ruleProjectKnowsAbout ;
    logic:head [
        rdf:subject   "?agent" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:knowsAbout ;
        rdf:object    "?subject"
    ] ;
    logic:body [
        rdf:subject   "?profile" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:hasThresholdRow ;
        rdf:object    "?row"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?row" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:projectsLadderEdge ;
        rdf:object    gmeow:knowsAbout
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?row" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:sourceDimension ;
        rdf:object    "?dim"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?row" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:thresholdLevel ;
        rdf:object    "?threshold"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?assessment" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:assessmentDimension ;
        rdf:object    "?dim"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?assessment" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:assessedAgent ;
        rdf:object    "?agent"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?assessment" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:assessmentSubject ;
        rdf:object    "?subject"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?assessment" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:assessmentLevel ;
        rdf:object    "?level"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?level" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:levelAtOrAbove ;
        rdf:object    "?threshold"
    ] .

logic:ruleProjectUnderstands
    a logic:Rule ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "project ladder edge: understands"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Emits gmeow:understands from an assessment whose dimension and level clear the gmeow:understands row of a logic:LadderProjectionProfile. Positive Horn; the threshold is read from the profile."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:provenance logic:ruleProjectUnderstands ;
    logic:head [
        rdf:subject   "?agent" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:understands ;
        rdf:object    "?subject"
    ] ;
    logic:body [
        rdf:subject   "?profile" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:hasThresholdRow ;
        rdf:object    "?row"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?row" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:projectsLadderEdge ;
        rdf:object    gmeow:understands
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?row" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:sourceDimension ;
        rdf:object    "?dim"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?row" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:thresholdLevel ;
        rdf:object    "?threshold"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?assessment" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:assessmentDimension ;
        rdf:object    "?dim"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?assessment" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:assessedAgent ;
        rdf:object    "?agent"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?assessment" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:assessmentSubject ;
        rdf:object    "?subject"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?assessment" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:assessmentLevel ;
        rdf:object    "?level"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?level" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:levelAtOrAbove ;
        rdf:object    "?threshold"
    ] .

logic:ruleProjectHasMastered
    a logic:Rule ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "project ladder edge: has mastered"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Emits gmeow:hasMastered only when BOTH a procedural-competence assessment and a transfer assessment of the same agent on the same subject clear their gmeow:hasMastered rows, where both rows belong to the SAME logic:LadderProjectionProfile. The two-row conjunction is why mastery of one narrow task no longer implies broad command — transfer must clear too — and the shared-profile join is why a procedural threshold from one profile can never be mixed with a transfer threshold from another. Positive Horn; thresholds read from the profile."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:provenance logic:ruleProjectHasMastered ;
    logic:head [
        rdf:subject   "?agent" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:hasMastered ;
        rdf:object    "?subject"
    ] ;
    logic:body [
        rdf:subject   "?profile" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:hasThresholdRow ;
        rdf:object    "?rowProc"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?profile" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:hasThresholdRow ;
        rdf:object    "?rowTransfer"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?rowProc" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:projectsLadderEdge ;
        rdf:object    gmeow:hasMastered
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?rowProc" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:sourceDimension ;
        rdf:object    logic:dimensionProceduralCompetence
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?rowProc" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:thresholdLevel ;
        rdf:object    "?thresholdProc"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?assessProc" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:assessmentDimension ;
        rdf:object    logic:dimensionProceduralCompetence
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?assessProc" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:assessedAgent ;
        rdf:object    "?agent"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?assessProc" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:assessmentSubject ;
        rdf:object    "?subject"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?assessProc" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:assessmentLevel ;
        rdf:object    "?levelProc"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?levelProc" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:levelAtOrAbove ;
        rdf:object    "?thresholdProc"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?rowTransfer" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:projectsLadderEdge ;
        rdf:object    gmeow:hasMastered
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?rowTransfer" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:sourceDimension ;
        rdf:object    logic:dimensionTransfer
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?rowTransfer" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:thresholdLevel ;
        rdf:object    "?thresholdTransfer"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?assessTransfer" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:assessmentDimension ;
        rdf:object    logic:dimensionTransfer
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?assessTransfer" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:assessedAgent ;
        rdf:object    "?agent"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?assessTransfer" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:assessmentSubject ;
        rdf:object    "?subject"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?assessTransfer" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:assessmentLevel ;
        rdf:object    "?levelTransfer"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?levelTransfer" ;
        rdf:predicate logic:levelAtOrAbove ;
        rdf:object    "?thresholdTransfer"
    ] .

# ── Defeasible evidence: support that can come apart ────────────────────────────
# A first-class, reified declaration that one relation is DEFEASIBLE (defeater-
# blockable) evidence for another, never a strict entailment. The recast of
# expertise's gmeow:hasSkill → gmeow:knowsAbout: possessing a skill (tacit can-do)
# is defeasible evidence for knowing-about (descriptive, fact-level familiarity),
# the two coming apart (tacit competence with no articulable knowledge, and vice
# versa). Because the
# support is defeasible, the shipped reasoning NEVER materializes the supported
# edge from the evidence: gmeow:knowsAbout's only shipped source is the
# declarative-familiarity ladder projection, never gmeow:hasSkill. A consumer that
# opts into defeasible reasoning can draw the supported edge under a declared
# contract (demonstrated in the conformance corpus), defeated when the competence
# is purely tacit.
#
# NON-ENTAILMENT GUARD: the predicate-global logic:NonEntailmentObligation
# machinery cannot express "knowsAbout must not come FROM hasSkill", because
# gmeow:knowsAbout IS a legitimate rule head (the declarative-familiarity ladder
# projection) — a predicate-global obligation on it would resolve to
# logic:ObligationViolated, a hard error. The precise, strictly-stronger guard is
# the source-specific verification query that no gmeow:knowsAbout edge is derived
# whose only support is gmeow:hasSkill, enforced under make verify.

logic:DefeasibleEvidence
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Defeasible Evidence"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A reified declaration that one relation or fact (logic:evidenceProperty) is DEFEASIBLE — defeater-blockable — evidence for another (logic:evidenceFor), carrying its logic:defeasibleStrength, and explicitly NOT a strict entailment. The support can come apart: the evidence may hold while the supported claim fails (and conversely), so the engine never materializes the supported edge from the evidence under the default reasoning — only a consumer opting into defeasible reasoning under a declared contract draws it, defeated when a declared defeater holds. The central recast of any 'X is evidence for Y, not X entails Y' relationship; its first instance is gmeow:hasSkill as defeasible evidence for gmeow:knowsAbout."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:evidenceProperty
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:DefeasibleEvidence ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "evidence property"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The evidential relation a logic:DefeasibleEvidence declares to bear defeasibly on another — the 'from' side (e.g. gmeow:hasSkill). Range is left open (a property or a claim), stated in prose; the object is used by punning, the gmeow:pairsWith convention."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:evidenceFor
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:DefeasibleEvidence ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "evidence for"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The relation or claim a logic:DefeasibleEvidence defeasibly supports — the 'to' side (e.g. gmeow:knowsAbout). Defeasible support, never strict entailment: the supported edge is not materialized from the evidence under the default reasoning. Range is left open (a property or a claim), stated in prose."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:defeasibleStrength
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:DefeasibleEvidence ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "defeasible strength"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A solver-layer measure of how strongly a logic:DefeasibleEvidence supports its logic:evidenceFor target before any defeater — a ranking annotation, never asserted as a reasoned axiom and never a probability. Range is left open (an ordinal label or a numeric weight), stated in prose."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:skillEvidenceForKnowsAbout
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:DefeasibleEvidence ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "skill is defeasible evidence for knowing about"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The shipped declaration recasting expertise's former gmeow:hasSkill ⊑ gmeow:knowsAbout: possessing a skill in a subject is DEFEASIBLE evidence that the agent knows about it, not a strict subproperty entailment — tacit competence and descriptive, fact-level knowing-about come apart. The supported gmeow:knowsAbout edge is never materialized from gmeow:hasSkill under the default reasoning (its only shipped source is the declarative-familiarity ladder projection); a consumer opting into defeasible reasoning draws it, defeated when the competence is purely tacit."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:evidenceProperty gmeow:hasSkill ;
    logic:evidenceFor gmeow:knowsAbout ;
    logic:defeasibleStrength "moderate" .

# === Transaction layer: serial composition, concurrency, and anomalies =======
# The serial-conjunction combinator (a program operator typed APART from logical
# conjunction), the three separately-declared concurrency concerns kept apart
# (history criterion vs guarantee strength vs implementation mechanism), and the
# history-level serialization anomaly that is a finding, never a contradiction
# witness. Normative in design/LOGIC-TRANSACTION.md, §Concurrent transactions.

# --- Serial composition operator ---------------------------------------------

logic:SerialConjunction
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Serial Conjunction"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The serial-conjunction program combinator (⊗, 'do φ then ψ'): the path along which the program executes splits so that φ holds over a prefix and ψ holds over the remaining suffix. It is a PROGRAM combinator over the transaction layer's path semantics, typed APART from ordinary (at-a-state) logical conjunction — a program operator is never conflated with the logical connective that holds at a single state, matching the formula-versus-program operator typing of the IR. Its two operands are carried by logic:leftOperand (the prefix program) and logic:rightOperand (the suffix program). The base relations of the layer are elementary state transitions, this serial conjunction, and executional entailment."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:leftOperand
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "left operand"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a binary transaction-program combinator (for example a logic:SerialConjunction) to its left/prefix operand — the program that holds over the prefix of the executing path. Range a transaction-program node (stated in prose). Paired with logic:rightOperand."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:rightOperand
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "right operand"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a binary transaction-program combinator (for example a logic:SerialConjunction) to its right/suffix operand — the program that holds over the suffix of the executing path. Range a transaction-program node (stated in prose). Paired with logic:leftOperand."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

# --- Branching, concurrent, iterative, and fallback combinators ---------------
# The four missing program combinators that complete the transaction layer's
# operator set as named in logic:Plan's definition and LOGIC-TELEOLOGY.md.
# Each is typed APART from the corresponding logical connective — a program
# operator is never confused with a formula connective — and mirrors
# logic:SerialConjunction exactly in structure and annotation style.
# Normative in design/LOGIC-TRANSACTION.md and design/LOGIC-TELEOLOGY.md.

logic:Choice
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Choice"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The guarded-choice program combinator: selects one of two sub-programs based on whether a guard situation holds at the current state. The left operand (logic:leftOperand) is executed when the guard holds; the right operand (logic:rightOperand) is executed when it does not. The guard is declared through logic:guardSituation, reusing the same property the conditional goal expression reads — a choice combinator is a PROGRAM operator that dispatches on a guard, typed APART from a conditional formula connective that holds at a single state. The two operands are binary, carried by logic:leftOperand and logic:rightOperand (the same properties logic:SerialConjunction uses). A plan whose branches are conditioned on what an earlier observation revealed is a POLICY — a reading of a plan, not a separate class — and its branches are resolved through logic:planBranch, logic:branchGuard, and logic:nextActionSchema; logic:Choice is the structural combinator that expresses the branching operator in the program body. Distinct from goal-level logic:DisjunctiveGoal, which evaluates a truth-at-a-state condition over sub-expressions, not a program that dispatches control to one of two sub-programs."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:ConcurrentComposition
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Concurrent Composition"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The concurrent-composition program combinator: two sub-programs advance together with their elementary steps interleaved over a shared path. The left sub-program is carried by logic:leftOperand and the right by logic:rightOperand. This is the COMPOSITION OPERATOR that states two programs run concurrently — it is DISTINCT from the three separately-declared concurrency correctness concerns the transaction layer keeps apart: (a) logic:SerializabilityCriterion is a correctness PROPERTY OF A HISTORY (conflict-serializability or view-serializability), (b) logic:IsolationLevel is the declared GUARANTEE STRENGTH a schedule must meet, and (c) logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol is the IMPLEMENTATION MECHANISM enforcing that strength. ConcurrentComposition names the structural operator; whether the resulting history is serializable, what isolation is declared, and which protocol enforces it are separately-declared facets. A logic:ConcurrentHistory carries the conflict edges whose cycle structure logic:SerializationAnomaly detects; logic:ConcurrentComposition names the program that gives rise to such a history. Typed APART from ordinary (at-a-state) conjunction — concurrent programs advance over a shared path segment, while a conjunctive formula holds at a single state."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Iteration
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Iteration"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The iteration program combinator: repeats a body sub-program while a loop condition holds. The body is carried by logic:iterationBody and the loop condition by logic:iterationCondition. Binary left/right operand semantics do not fit iteration — a loop has a body and a separate condition, not two co-equal operands — so logic:iterationBody and logic:iterationCondition are minted as dedicated properties rather than repurposing logic:leftOperand / logic:rightOperand. A logic:Iteration is the program-level counterpart of the loop/retry structure logic:StrongCyclicPlanSuccess quantifies over: a strong-cyclic plan succeeds when every fair execution of a loop through recoverable failures terminates at the goal in finitely many steps. The loop condition is a situation type checked before each body execution; when it does not hold the iteration terminates. Typed APART from recursive goal structures and from plain goal decomposition, which carry satisfaction dependency rather than control flow."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:iterationBody
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "iteration body"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:Iteration combinator to the sub-program that constitutes its loop body — the program executed on each iteration pass. Domain logic:Iteration, range a transaction-program node (stated in prose). Paired with logic:iterationCondition, which carries the guard situation checked before each pass. Distinct from logic:leftOperand / logic:rightOperand (binary co-equal operands of serial, choice, concurrent, and fallback combinators): a loop body is not co-equal with a loop condition."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:iterationCondition
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "iteration condition"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:Iteration combinator to the situation type that gates each pass of the loop body — the loop is executed while this situation obtains at the current state; when it does not hold the iteration terminates. Domain logic:Iteration, range logic:Situation (stated in prose). Paired with logic:iterationBody. Reuses the situation-type pattern of logic:guardSituation and logic:boundSituationType: the engine reads this against the current path state via logic:situationObtains."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:Fallback
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Fallback"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The fallback program combinator: attempts the primary sub-program (logic:leftOperand); if it fails (the primary executional entailment does not hold from the current state), executes the alternate sub-program (logic:rightOperand). It is a PROGRAM combinator over the transaction layer path semantics, typed APART from action-level logic:compensation: a compensation undoes the EFFECT of an action that ran and reached an outcome, recovering from a realized nondeterministic outcome branch, while logic:Fallback is a STRUCTURAL OPERATOR that routes control to an alternate path when the primary program cannot succeed from the current state. The two sub-programs are binary, carried by logic:leftOperand (the primary) and logic:rightOperand (the alternate), reusing the same properties logic:SerialConjunction and logic:Choice use. A plan strong-cyclic success through recoverable failures is the quantification-level counterpart: logic:Fallback is the operator that makes recovery structurally expressible in the program body."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

# --- Plan-to-path link (closing the four-link chain) -------------------------
# The chain intention -> plan -> action -> transaction-path is otherwise
# expressible through existing terms: gmeow:Intention carries its goal via
# gmeow:intentionGoal and motivates the action occurrence via gmeow:motivates;
# logic:Plan carries the same goal via logic:planGoal; the action occurrence
# (a gmeow:Event) links to its reusable type via logic:instantiatesSchema. The
# one genuine gap is relating a Plan to the specific Path along which it ran,
# which logic:executedAlongPath closes. It CONNECTS the plan and the path; it
# does NOT subsume either — a plan is the program, a path is the executed run.

logic:executedAlongPath
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "executed along path"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a program run — a logic:Plan or a logic:TransactionOutcome — to the logic:Path along which it executed: the executed history that realizes the program. Domain logic:Plan or logic:TransactionOutcome, range logic:Path (stated in prose). This is the one link the four-notion chain intention -> plan -> action -> transaction-path did not already have: intention reaches its goal and action through gmeow:intentionGoal / gmeow:motivates, a logic:Plan reaches the same goal through logic:planGoal, and an action occurrence reaches its type through logic:instantiatesSchema, but no existing term tied a program to the run that executed it. It CONNECTS the program to its path but does NOT subsume either: a plan is the program (what is intended to be done), a path is the executed run (how state actually changed); the link records that this program ran along that history without conflating the two."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

# --- Canonical process model: the DAG-workflow profile + flow edges ----------
# The decidable, schedulable SHADOW of the canonical process model. A "DAG
# workflow" is NOT a kind of process but a statically-certified ACYCLIC fragment
# of logic:Plan, expressed as a Resource-facet value (logic:DagWorkflowResource)
# requested by a named contract (logic:DagWorkflowContract) — never a standalone
# class (design/LOGIC-CONTRACT.md, "Why a contract, not a profile"). The genuinely
# missing canonical edge is DATAFLOW: logic:dataflowConsumes is the binary
# dependency a DAG executor schedules over; logic:ControlFlowEdge /
# logic:DataFlowEdge are its reified FLOW-GRAPH form (the graph the acyclicity
# certifier runs Tarjan SCC over), complementary to — not a duplicate of — the
# structured-program combinators (logic:Choice, logic:Iteration,
# logic:ConcurrentComposition, logic:Fallback), which are the program-TREE form an
# interpreter walks. The DAG fragment excludes the loop combinator logic:Iteration
# (the program-level counterpart of logic:StrongCyclicPlanSuccess); a cyclic plan
# stays valid canonically but resolves to `unsupported` under the DAG profile,
# the offending edge disclosed by logic:dagCycleWitness — never silently truncated.

logic:dataflowConsumes
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "dataflow consumes"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a process node — a logic:Plan step, a pipeline stage, or a procedure step — to an upstream node whose product it reads: the canonical binary dataflow dependency, oriented consumer -> producer (an executor inverts it to schedule producers first). The transitive closure must be acyclic for the DAG-workflow profile (logic:DagWorkflowResource); a cycle takes the plan out of the certified acyclic fragment and is disclosed through logic:dagCycleWitness, never silently dropped. Domain and range a process node (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). The reified FLOW-GRAPH counterpart is logic:DataFlowEdge; downstream surfaces such as gmeow:dataflowConsumes specialize this property."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:dataflowProduces
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    owl:inverseOf logic:dataflowConsumes ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "dataflow produces"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The inverse of logic:dataflowConsumes: relates a process node to a downstream node that reads its product (producer -> consumer). The canonical authored direction is logic:dataflowConsumes, so this inverse is normally left to be inferred rather than asserted. Domain and range a process node (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:ControlFlowEdge
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf logic:Relator ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Control-Flow Edge"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A reified control-flow edge between two process nodes — the canonical FLOW-GRAPH form of control flow, mediating a source node (logic:flowFrom) and a target node (logic:flowTo). Complementary to, NOT a duplicate of, the structured-program combinators (logic:Choice, logic:Iteration, logic:ConcurrentComposition, logic:Fallback): the combinators are the program-TREE form an interpreter walks, while a logic:ControlFlowEdge is the binary-edge form the DAG-workflow acyclicity certifier runs Tarjan SCC over. A graph carrying a logic:Iteration loop edge (or any back-edge) is outside the DAG fragment. Downstream reified control-flow relators such as gmeow:ControlFlow specialize this class. A Relator mediating two distinct relata (its flowFrom and flowTo nodes), satisfying the relator-mediation discipline."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:DataFlowEdge
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf logic:Relator ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Data-Flow Edge"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A reified dataflow edge between two process nodes — the FLOW-GRAPH counterpart of the logic:dataflowConsumes property, mediating a source (producer) node via logic:flowFrom and a target (consumer) node via logic:flowTo. Use the property form (logic:dataflowConsumes) for a bare binary dependency and this reified form when an edge must carry its own attributes (the flowing entity, a guard, an order). Downstream reified dataflow relators such as gmeow:DataFlow specialize this class. A Relator mediating two distinct relata, satisfying the relator-mediation discipline."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:flowFrom
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "flow from"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a reified flow edge (logic:ControlFlowEdge or logic:DataFlowEdge) to its source process node — the predecessor in a control-flow edge, the producer in a dataflow edge. Domain a flow edge, range a process node (stated in prose). Paired with logic:flowTo; the two mediation legs that make a flow edge a well-formed Relator."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:flowTo
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "flow to"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a reified flow edge (logic:ControlFlowEdge or logic:DataFlowEdge) to its target process node — the successor in a control-flow edge, the consumer in a dataflow edge. Domain a flow edge, range a process node (stated in prose). Paired with logic:flowFrom."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:DagWorkflowResource
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ResourcePolicy ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "DAG-Workflow Resource"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The resource execution policy of the DAG-workflow profile: it requires the plan's control/dataflow graph to be a loop-free (acyclic) DAG — no logic:Iteration and an acyclic logic:dataflowConsumes / flow-edge closure — so the schedule is a topological order with a hard termination guarantee, and the result reports logic:CompleteForFragment. Acyclicity is the universal structural guarantee certified here; a typed terminal discipline such as the build pipeline's single gmeow:kindSink is an additional per-surface constraint, not part of this graph-level certification. A specialization of the certified-fragment discipline of logic:CertifiedFragmentResource applied to process control flow rather than rule recursion; because resource is an execution policy holding independent properties together, a contract may carry both a DAG-workflow requirement and a budget at once. A plan outside the acyclic fragment is still valid canonically but resolves to `unsupported` under this policy, the offending edge disclosed by logic:dagCycleWitness — never silently truncated."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:DagWorkflowContract
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ReasoningContract ;
    logic:resourcePolicy logic:DagWorkflowResource ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "DAG-Workflow Contract"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The named ReasoningContract that requests the DAG-workflow resource policy (logic:resourcePolicy logic:DagWorkflowResource), under which a loop-free logic:Plan is topologically schedulable and complete-for-fragment. It is a CONTRACT (a standing request on the Resource facet), NOT a logic:ReasoningPreset: a preset bundles a model-semantics selection, whereas this fixes only the execution-discipline (Resource) facet — the contract-not-profile doctrine, applied so the resource discipline is a facet a contract requests, not a semantic profile. The dogfooded build pipeline runs logic:executedUnderContract this contract; a cyclic plan resolves to `unsupported` with its offending edge named rather than being approximated to a nearby supported semantics."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:dagCycleWitness
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "DAG cycle witness"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates an `unsupported` DAG-workflow verdict to a disclosed offending edge or cycle member — the back-edge or logic:Iteration that places a plan outside the certified acyclic fragment — MULTI-valued (a graph may carry several cycles). Mirrors the witness-disclosure discipline of logic:forbiddenViolationWitness: the certifier never silently truncates a cyclic plan, it surfaces exactly which edges break acyclicity while the plan stays valid under a non-DAG contract. Domain a reasoning result or coherence outcome carrying the `unsupported` evaluation status, range a flow edge or process node (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

# =========================================================================== #
# The well-founded materializer's intra-engine phase plan — dogfooded as data. #
#                                                                             #
# This logic:Plan is the AUTHORED MODEL of the phase sequence the native       #
# well-founded-semantics evaluator runs per world in                          #
# crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs (materialize()). It is the canonical-process #
# model applied ONE SCALE DOWN from the build pipeline (gmeow:pipeline-build): #
# where the pipeline is the inter-stage DAG, this plan is the intra-engine     #
# pass sequence of a single reasoning step. BOUNDARY (Principle 12,            #
# non-negotiable): this is authored SOURCE the parity test                     #
# crates/pipeline/tests/wellfounded_plan_parity.rs checks the Rust runtime     #
# against (gmeow_logic::WELL_FOUNDED_PHASES) — the reasoner NEVER parses this   #
# RDF at scheduling or runtime; the native loop is the runtime, the plan is    #
# its declared twin.                                                           #
#                                                                             #
# materialize() runs exactly three phases per world:                          #
#   1. wfMaterializeEdb   — seed the per-world EDB (world_edb_facts +          #
#                           echo_asserted + seed FactStore).                   #
#   2. wfResolveFixpoint  — the alternating fixpoint (van Gelder): the ITERATED #
#                           phase — loop { U = lmr(K); K2 = lmr(U); break when  #
#                           K2.key_set() == K.key_set() }. Modelled as a        #
#                           logic:Iteration whose logic:iterationCondition is   #
#                           the situation "the double-reduct fixpoint is not    #
#                           yet reached" (K2 != K).                             #
#   3. wfConstructModel   — final reduct against the well-founded model W,      #
#                           hard-fail on a partial model, emit derived rows.    #
#                                                                             #
# The phase order is the SerialConjunction (materialize ; (resolve ;          #
# construct)), reachable from the plan through logic:planBody. Because the     #
# middle phase is a logic:Iteration (a loop), this plan is OUTSIDE the         #
# certified acyclic DAG fragment BY CONSTRUCTION — that is correct and         #
# expected, so (unlike gmeow:pipeline-build) it does NOT run                    #
# logic:executedUnderContract logic:DagWorkflowContract.                       #
# =========================================================================== #

# Shared action-theory facets the three phase ActionSchemas carry to satisfy
# logic:ActionSchemaShape (logic:precondition + logic:capability are REQUIRED).
logic:wfWorldSeeded
    a logic:Situation ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "well-founded world seeded"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The situation gate the well-founded materializer's phase action schemas ground on: the per-world store is selected and its asserted EDB facts are reachable (the sorted worlds list of crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize()). The shared logic:precondition of the three intra-engine phase schemas — the elementary phase transition applies only once a world is in scope."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .

logic:wfReductEngineCapability
    a logic:GenericDependence ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "well-founded reduct-engine capability"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The executional precondition on the actor the well-founded materializer's phase action schemas carry as their logic:capability: the least-model-of-reduct engine (crate::rule_ir::least_model_of_reduct) is available to evaluate a reduct against a reference fact set. The generic ability the native engine must hold to run any of the three phases — distinct from logic:wfWorldSeeded, which is a precondition on the world state, not on the engine."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .

# The loop condition of the alternating-fixpoint phase: the double-reduct
# fixpoint is NOT YET reached (K2.key_set() != K.key_set()). The logic:Iteration
# runs its body while this situation obtains; when it ceases (K2 == K) the loop
# terminates and W = K is the well-founded model.
logic:wfFixpointNotReached
    a logic:Situation ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "well-founded fixpoint not reached"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The loop-guard situation of the alternating-fixpoint phase: the double-reduct step has not yet converged — the new under-estimate K2 differs from the previous K by fact-key set (K2.key_set() != K.key_set() in crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs). The logic:iterationCondition of logic:wfResolveLoop: the loop body re-runs while this obtains, and the iteration terminates when it ceases (K2 == K), at which point W = K is the well-founded model's set of true atoms."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .

# Phase 1 — seed the per-world EDB.
logic:wfMaterializeEdb
    a logic:ActionSchema ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "well-founded materialize EDB"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Phase 1 of the well-founded materializer (crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize()): seed the per-world EDB — collect world_edb_facts, echo the asserted rows, and load them (sorted-key order) into the seed FactStore that the alternating fixpoint starts from. The first elementary phase transition of the intra-engine plan; its successor is the alternating-fixpoint resolution."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ;
    logic:precondition logic:wfWorldSeeded ;
    logic:capability logic:wfReductEngineCapability .

# Phase 2 — the alternating fixpoint (the ITERATED phase).
logic:wfResolveFixpoint
    a logic:ActionSchema ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "well-founded resolve fixpoint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Phase 2 of the well-founded materializer (crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize()): the alternating fixpoint of van Gelder — the double-reduct step U = least_model_of_reduct(reference = K) then K2 = least_model_of_reduct(reference = U), repeated until K2 and K have the same fact-key set. The body of the logic:Iteration logic:wfResolveLoop; the loop runs while logic:wfFixpointNotReached obtains and converges on W = K, the well-founded model's set of true atoms. The single ITERATED phase of the plan — why the plan is outside the acyclic DAG fragment."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ;
    logic:precondition logic:wfWorldSeeded ;
    logic:capability logic:wfReductEngineCapability .

# Phase 3 — final reduct + emit.
logic:wfConstructModel
    a logic:ActionSchema ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "well-founded construct model"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Phase 3 of the well-founded materializer (crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize()): the final reduct against the converged well-founded model W — least_model_of_reduct(reference = W), a HARD FAIL if the result's fact-key set differs from W (an undefined/partial model, unsupported in v1), then emit the derived non-EDB rows stamped with the world graph. The last elementary phase transition of the intra-engine plan."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ;
    logic:precondition logic:wfWorldSeeded ;
    logic:capability logic:wfReductEngineCapability .

# The combinator tree (program form an interpreter walks).
#   wfResolveLoop      = Iteration(body = wfResolveFixpoint,
#                                  condition = wfFixpointNotReached)
#   wfResolveThenBuild = SerialConjunction(left = wfResolveLoop,
#                                          right = wfConstructModel)
#   wfPhaseSequence    = SerialConjunction(left = wfMaterializeEdb,
#                                          right = wfResolveThenBuild)
# Phase order, left-first: materialize ; (resolve* ; construct).
logic:wfResolveLoop
    a logic:Iteration ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "well-founded resolve loop"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:Iteration combinator wrapping the alternating-fixpoint phase of the well-founded materializer: its logic:iterationBody is logic:wfResolveFixpoint (the double-reduct step) and its logic:iterationCondition is logic:wfFixpointNotReached (K2 != K). The loop is the program-level twin of the `loop { … break when K2.key_set() == K.key_set() }` of crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs — the back-edge that places logic:wellFoundedMaterializerPlan outside the certified acyclic DAG fragment."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ;
    logic:iterationBody logic:wfResolveFixpoint ;
    logic:iterationCondition logic:wfFixpointNotReached .

logic:wfResolveThenBuild
    a logic:SerialConjunction ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "well-founded resolve then build"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The inner logic:SerialConjunction of the well-founded materializer's phase plan: do the alternating-fixpoint loop (logic:leftOperand logic:wfResolveLoop), THEN construct the final model (logic:rightOperand logic:wfConstructModel). The suffix program of the plan's outer serial conjunction."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ;
    logic:leftOperand logic:wfResolveLoop ;
    logic:rightOperand logic:wfConstructModel .

logic:wfPhaseSequence
    a logic:SerialConjunction ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "well-founded phase sequence"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The ROOT logic:SerialConjunction of the well-founded materializer's phase plan: do the EDB-seeding phase (logic:leftOperand logic:wfMaterializeEdb), THEN the resolve-then-build suffix (logic:rightOperand logic:wfResolveThenBuild). Walked left-first, the combinator tree yields the execution order materialize ; resolve* ; construct — the program twin of crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize() and of gmeow_logic::WELL_FOUNDED_PHASES. The program root logic:wellFoundedMaterializerPlan reaches it through logic:planBody."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ;
    logic:leftOperand logic:wfMaterializeEdb ;
    logic:rightOperand logic:wfResolveThenBuild .

# The plan's success criterion: the converged well-founded model emitted.
logic:goalWellFoundedModel
    a gmeow:Goal ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "well-founded model goal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The success criterion of the well-founded materializer's phase plan: the total (two-valued) well-founded model of the rules over every world is computed and its derived non-EDB rows emitted. The gmeow:Goal logic:wellFoundedMaterializerPlan is arranged to reach; a partial model is a hard failure, never a partial success."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .

# The plan: the authored twin of crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize().
logic:wellFoundedMaterializerPlan
    a logic:Plan ,
        gmeow:SocialObject ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "well-founded materializer plan"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The AUTHORED MODEL of the intra-engine phase sequence the native well-founded-semantics evaluator runs per world (crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize()): the canonical process model applied one scale down from the build pipeline (gmeow:pipeline-build) — an intra-engine pass sequence rather than an inter-stage DAG. Its logic:planBody is the root combinator logic:wfPhaseSequence, whose left-first walk yields the three phases materialize (logic:wfMaterializeEdb) ; resolve* (the logic:Iteration logic:wfResolveLoop over logic:wfResolveFixpoint, gated by logic:wfFixpointNotReached) ; construct (logic:wfConstructModel) — matching gmeow_logic::WELL_FOUNDED_PHASES. Because the middle phase is a logic:Iteration (a loop), this plan is OUTSIDE the certified acyclic DAG fragment by construction; that is correct and expected, so it does NOT run logic:executedUnderContract logic:DagWorkflowContract. Principle 12 BOUNDARY: this plan is authored SOURCE the parity gate crates/pipeline/tests/wellfounded_plan_parity.rs checks the Rust runtime against — the reasoner NEVER parses this RDF at scheduling or runtime; the native loop is the runtime, the plan is its declared twin. As a logic:Plan it asserts its own gmeow:SocialObject sort directly, the prose grounding of logic:Plan licensing no DL inference of it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ;
    logic:planBody logic:wfPhaseSequence ;
    logic:planGoal logic:goalWellFoundedModel ;
    logic:planSuccessMode logic:StrongPlanSuccess .

# --- Transaction outcome: the executional-entailment verdict surface ----------
# The recorded result of EXECUTING a transaction program (the combinators above)
# under executional entailment — the native engine's verdict, surfaced as quads
# so the success/failure decision and the executed path carry into the
# derivation graph rather than being discarded after evaluation.

logic:TransactionOutcome
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Transaction Outcome"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The recorded result of executing a transaction program from a start state under executional entailment: the program succeeds iff there exists a path from the start state along which it holds, and failure leaves the start state untouched. It carries logic:outcomeOfProgram (the program executed), logic:transactionStart (the state it started from), and logic:transactionSucceeds (the boolean verdict); on success it is linked by logic:executedAlongPath to the logic:Path of states the run traversed and the per-step support is recorded as supersession. Typed APART from logic:GoalEvaluation, which records at-a-state satisfaction of a goal, and from logic:PlanSuccessMode, which classifies a plan's success mode over its nondeterministic outcome set: a logic:TransactionOutcome records ONE concrete executed run's success or failure under executional entailment, not a satisfaction judgement and not a mode classification."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:outcomeOfProgram
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "outcome of program"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:TransactionOutcome to the transaction program whose execution it records — a transaction-program combinator node (logic:SerialConjunction, logic:Choice, logic:Fallback, or logic:Iteration). Domain logic:TransactionOutcome, range a transaction-program node (stated in prose). It ties the verdict back to the program that produced it without conflating the outcome (a run record) with the program (the structure that was run)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:transactionStart
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "transaction start"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:TransactionOutcome to the gmeow:State the program executed from — the start state of the executional-entailment run. Domain logic:TransactionOutcome, range gmeow:State (stated in prose). On failure the start state is left untouched (no successor is materialized); on success it is the first state of the logic:executedAlongPath path. The input side marks the executable program root with logic:transitionFromState; logic:transactionStart records, on the outcome, the start the verdict was computed from."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:transactionSucceeds
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "transaction succeeds"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The boolean executional-entailment verdict of a logic:TransactionOutcome: true iff there exists a path from logic:transactionStart along which the program holds, false otherwise. Domain logic:TransactionOutcome, range xsd:boolean (stated in prose). Kept distinct from goal satisfaction (logic:satisfactionStatus over a logic:GoalEvaluation) and from plan success mode (logic:planSuccessMode): it is the bare 'a path exists from the start' reading of the transaction layer, and a false verdict is honest total failure rather than a weak or partial success."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:executedHypotheticallyAs
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "executed hypothetically as"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The content-addressed witness (a digest) of a hypothetical (sandbox) transaction run: present on a logic:TransactionOutcome exactly when the program executed under logic:HypotheticalExecution, recording the identity of the discarded run whose verdict (logic:transactionSucceeds) was computed without committing its effects. The run's effect substrate — the executed logic:Path, the per-step logic:TransactionStep records, and the supersession quads — is intentionally ABSENT, because the sandbox operator tests without committing; this digest is therefore the sole standing trace that the run occurred and what it ranged over. Nothing is asserted to be erased, only never emitted, so suppression-never-erasure holds for free. Single-valued. Domain logic:TransactionOutcome, range xsd:string (stated in prose). The committed counterpart (logic:CommittedExecution) emits the full effect substrate and carries no such witness."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

# --- Concurrency: three distinct, separately-declared concerns ----------------

logic:SerializabilityCriterion
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Serializability Criterion"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A correctness property OF A HISTORY — not a protocol and not a guarantee strength. The closed value class of serializability criteria for a concurrent transaction history. Its individuals are logic:ConflictSerializability (an equivalent serial order exists reachable with no swap of conflicting operations) and logic:ViewSerializability (some serial order has the same read-from and final-write relationships). The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. This is one of three distinct, separately-declared concurrency concerns that must NOT be conflated: a logic:SerializabilityCriterion is a property of a history, a logic:IsolationLevel is a declared guarantee strength, and a logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol is an implementation mechanism — keeping them apart is required because they are not interchangeable and an implicit assumption about any one of them is a defect."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:ConflictSerializability
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:SerializabilityCriterion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Conflict Serializability"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:SerializabilityCriterion value satisfied when an equivalent serial order exists that is reachable from the history by swapping only non-conflicting operations — no swap of a pair of conflicting operations is required. A history property, not a protocol. Contrast logic:ViewSerializability."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ViewSerializability
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:SerializabilityCriterion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "View Serializability"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:SerializabilityCriterion value satisfied when some serial order has the same read-from and final-write relationships as the history — equivalent on what each read observed and which write was last. A history property, not a protocol. Strictly weaker than logic:ConflictSerializability is not implied; the two are distinct criteria a history may satisfy."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:IsolationLevel
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Isolation Level"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The declared GUARANTEE STRENGTH a schedule must meet — not a history property and not an implementation mechanism. The closed value class spanning the standard isolation spectrum up to and including full serializability and opacity. Its individuals are logic:ReadUncommittedIsolation, logic:ReadCommittedIsolation, logic:RepeatableReadIsolation, logic:SnapshotIsolation, logic:SerializableIsolation, and logic:OpacityIsolation — the strongest, under which even aborted or in-flight transactions never observe an inconsistent state, strictly stronger than serializability. The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. This is one of three distinct, separately-declared concurrency concerns that must NOT be conflated: a logic:IsolationLevel is a guarantee strength, a logic:SerializabilityCriterion is a property of a history, and a logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol is an implementation mechanism."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:ReadUncommittedIsolation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:IsolationLevel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Read Uncommitted Isolation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:IsolationLevel guarantee under which a transaction may observe uncommitted writes of others — the weakest level of the standard spectrum, admitting dirty reads."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ReadCommittedIsolation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:IsolationLevel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Read Committed Isolation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:IsolationLevel guarantee under which a transaction observes only committed writes, but successive reads of the same item may differ — dirty reads excluded, non-repeatable reads still admitted."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:RepeatableReadIsolation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:IsolationLevel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Repeatable Read Isolation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:IsolationLevel guarantee under which re-reads of an item a transaction has read return the same value — non-repeatable reads excluded, phantom rows still admitted."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:SnapshotIsolation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:IsolationLevel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Snapshot Isolation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:IsolationLevel guarantee under which a transaction reads from a consistent snapshot taken at its start — strong against most anomalies yet still admitting write skew, so strictly weaker than logic:SerializableIsolation."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:SerializableIsolation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:IsolationLevel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Serializable Isolation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:IsolationLevel guarantee under which the schedule is equivalent to some serial execution of the committed transactions — full serializability. Strictly weaker than logic:OpacityIsolation, which additionally constrains aborted and in-flight transactions."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:OpacityIsolation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:IsolationLevel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Opacity Isolation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:IsolationLevel guarantee under which even aborted or in-flight transactions never observe an inconsistent state — the strongest level, STRICTLY STRONGER than serializability (logic:SerializableIsolation), which constrains only committed transactions."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Concurrency Control Protocol"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The IMPLEMENTATION MECHANISM that enforces a chosen isolation level — HOW a guarantee is achieved, never the guarantee itself. The closed value class of concurrency-control protocols. Its individuals are logic:StrictTwoPhaseLocking, logic:StrongStrictTwoPhaseLocking, logic:TimestampOrdering, and logic:OptimisticValidation. The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. This is one of three distinct, separately-declared concurrency concerns that must NOT be conflated: a logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol is a mechanism, a logic:SerializabilityCriterion is a property of a history, and a logic:IsolationLevel is a guarantee strength — a protocol is how a guarantee is achieved, it is never the guarantee itself."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:StrictTwoPhaseLocking
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Strict Two-Phase Locking"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol that holds all EXCLUSIVE (write) locks until the transaction commits or aborts, preventing cascading aborts on writes. Contrast logic:StrongStrictTwoPhaseLocking, which additionally holds shared (read) locks to commit."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:StrongStrictTwoPhaseLocking
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Strong Strict Two-Phase Locking"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol that holds ALL locks — both shared (read) and exclusive (write) — until commit or abort, yielding the strongest, strictest two-phase-locking discipline. The strong-strict variant the design names distinctly from the strict variant (logic:StrictTwoPhaseLocking), which releases shared locks earlier."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:TimestampOrdering
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Timestamp Ordering"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol that assigns each transaction a timestamp and orders conflicting operations by it, aborting any operation that would violate the timestamp order. A mechanism, not a guarantee."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:OptimisticValidation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Optimistic Validation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol that lets transactions run without locking and validates for conflicts at commit time, aborting and retrying on a detected conflict. A mechanism, not a guarantee."@x-gmeow-english .

# --- Serialization anomaly: a finding, never a contradiction witness ----------

logic:SerializationAnomaly
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Serialization Anomaly"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A HISTORY-LEVEL finding: a pattern of conflicting operations, read-from edges, and happens-before arcs in a transaction history that admits no equivalent serial execution under the declared policy. Lost updates, write skew, and read/write anomalies are findings of this kind. It is DISTINCT from a contradiction witness (logic:contradictionWitness, which asserts ⊥ within a single state) and must NOT be modelled as one: the final state after a non-serializable schedule may be perfectly logically consistent while the schedule still has no equivalent serial execution, so a serialization anomaly is a property of the history, never a logical contradiction inside a state. It is surfaced as a finding with its dependency cycle or violated isolation level described; a non-serializable schedule is never silently linearized."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

# --- Concurrent history: the derived conflict graph + anomaly surface ----------
# The transaction history of a concurrent composition (logic:ConcurrentComposition)
# and the conflict-edge / criterion / finding vocabulary the native concurrent
# evaluator DERIVES from an interleaved run and the serialization-anomaly engine
# classifies. A history is a property bearer kept APART from the program that gives
# rise to it (the composition) and from the executional-entailment verdict (the
# outcome). Normative in design/LOGIC-TRANSACTION.md §Concurrent transactions.

logic:ConcurrentHistory
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Concurrent History"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The transaction history of a concurrent composition: the node that carries the logic:precedes conflict edges whose cycle structure logic:SerializationAnomaly classifies. The native concurrent evaluator DERIVES it from the interleaved execution of a logic:ConcurrentComposition's two legs (it may also be authored directly as a conflict graph). It is a HISTORY-LEVEL property bearer, kept DISTINCT from the logic:ConcurrentComposition PROGRAM that gives rise to it and from the logic:TransactionOutcome VERDICT of running that program — a history records which conflicting operations were ordered against which, not whether a path exists. Its serializability is judged against the logic:serializabilityCriterion it carries (default logic:ConflictSerializability); a cyclic conflict graph is surfaced as a logic:SerializationAnomaly finding, never silently linearized and never a logical contradiction within a state."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:precedes
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "precedes"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A conflict (precedence) edge in a logic:ConcurrentHistory: 'from precedes to' orders the conflicting operation of transaction 'from' before that of transaction 'to' in the witnessed schedule. Two operations conflict when they touch the same item and at least one writes it; the edge direction records which came first in the interleaving. Domain and range are transaction-program nodes (stated in prose). A CYCLE over logic:precedes is a serialization anomaly (logic:SerializationAnomaly) — between two transactions it requires edges in BOTH directions, the write-skew / lost-update shape — and is NEVER a logical contradiction (logic:contradictionWitness): it is a property of the history, not of any single state."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:serializabilityCriterion
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "serializability criterion"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ConcurrentHistory to the logic:SerializabilityCriterion its schedule is classified against — logic:ConflictSerializability (the default when none is stated) or logic:ViewSerializability. Domain logic:ConcurrentHistory, range logic:SerializabilityCriterion (stated in prose). This is the history-property dimension only: it is kept SEPARATE from logic:IsolationLevel (a declared guarantee strength) and logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol (an implementation mechanism), the two other concurrency concerns the layer never conflates. The criterion a detected anomaly violates is recorded on the finding through logic:violatedCriterion."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:concurrentComposedFrom
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "concurrent composed from"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a DERIVED logic:ConcurrentHistory to each of the two transaction-program operands (the logic:leftOperand and logic:rightOperand of the logic:ConcurrentComposition) whose interleaved elementary steps produced its conflict edges. Domain logic:ConcurrentHistory, range a transaction-program node (stated in prose); multi-valued (one link per operand). It is the audit trail from the history back to the authored sub-programs that gave rise to it, kept distinct from logic:precedes (an edge BETWEEN the transactions within the history) — this link points OUT to the programs, not between operations."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:derivedHistory
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "derived history"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:TransactionOutcome of a logic:ConcurrentComposition run to the logic:ConcurrentHistory the native evaluator derived from the interleaved execution of its two legs. Domain logic:TransactionOutcome, range logic:ConcurrentHistory (stated in prose). It SEPARATES the executional-entailment verdict (the outcome — does a path exist) from the derived concurrency surface (the history — how the conflicting operations were ordered and whether that ordering is serializable): a concurrent run records BOTH, linked by this property, so neither the verdict nor the serializability finding is conflated with the other."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:violatedCriterion
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "violated criterion"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:SerializationAnomaly finding to the logic:SerializabilityCriterion it violates — the criterion (logic:ConflictSerializability or logic:ViewSerializability) under which the history admits no equivalent serial execution. Domain logic:SerializationAnomaly, range logic:SerializabilityCriterion (stated in prose). It names WHICH history property the anomaly breaches; it does not assert a logical contradiction (the schedule's final state may be perfectly consistent), keeping the finding a property of the history rather than of any state."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:anomalyCycle
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "anomaly cycle"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The detected dependency cycle of a logic:SerializationAnomaly, rendered as the canonical sequence of transaction IRIs joined by ' -> ' (rotated to start at the lexicographically smallest member and closed back to it, so the same history always yields the same description). Domain logic:SerializationAnomaly, range xsd:string (stated in prose). It is a human-readable DESCRIPTION of the history-level finding — the conflict-graph cycle that has no equivalent serial order — never a claim of ⊥ within a state; a non-serializable schedule is surfaced with its cycle described here, never silently linearized."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

# ── The full first-order formula AST surface (TBox + RBox) ────────────────────
# The reified vocabulary the typed full-FOL formula core serializes into: a
# logic:Formula tree of quantifiers (logic:forall / logic:exists), connectives
# (logic:and / logic:or / logic:not / logic:antecedent+logic:consequent /
# logic:iff), and atomic predications (logic:relation over ordered term-carrier
# arguments). Horn+NAF rules remain the recognized sub-fragment carried by
# logic:Rule; this surface carries the formulas that exceed it. Relations are
# reified as logic:Type individuals (the HiLog reflection — see logic:instanceOf
# / logic:orderedType / logic:Type), so the object level stays first-order: there
# is no predicate-variable term.

logic:Formula
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Formula"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A first-order formula node: the reified AST node a non-Horn logic: statement compiles into. A logic:Formula is a quantifier (carrying logic:forall or logic:exists over a body and one or more logic:quantifiedVariable bindings), a connective (logic:and, logic:or, logic:not, logic:antecedent with logic:consequent, or logic:iff over sub-formulae), or an atomic predication (logic:relation over ordered logic:argument terms). It is the unified full-FOL core of which Horn+NAF derivation rules are a recognized sub-fragment; the canonical RDF 1.2 serialization round-trips it losslessly, while weaker projections carry any formula they cannot express as flagged unsupported residue."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:SequenceMarker
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Sequence Marker"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A variadic argument placeholder (the Common Logic '…x' form) that binds a sequence of terms rather than a single term, generalizing the fixed arity-three atom to predications of any arity. A term-carrier argument whose value is a logic:termSequenceMarker denotes one; keeping it a distinct kind stops a single-term variable from being mistaken for a sequence one."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:hasFormula
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:range logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "has formula"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a program or container to a top-level logic:Formula it asserts. Top-level formulae are reached by this property; sub-formulae are reached by the connective and quantifier properties, so a formula referenced as another's component is not also a top-level assertion."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:forall
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:range logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "for all"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a universal-quantifier logic:Formula to its body formula. The bound variables are carried by logic:quantifiedVariable; their block order is significant. Universal quantification ranges over individuals in the domain of discourse (the object level stays first-order)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:exists
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:range logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "exists"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates an existential-quantifier logic:Formula to its body formula. The bound variables are carried by logic:quantifiedVariable. Existential witnesses are Skolemized only at the evaluable-lowering layer; the AST node pins the binder and body, not the witness identity."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:and
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:range logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "and"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a conjunction logic:Formula to each of its operand sub-formulae (multi-valued, two or more). Conjunction is commutative and associative, so the canonical identity flattens nested conjunctions and is insensitive to operand order."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:or
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:range logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "or"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a disjunction logic:Formula to each of its operand sub-formulae (multi-valued, two or more). Disjunction is commutative and associative, so the canonical identity flattens nested disjunctions and is insensitive to operand order."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:not
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:range logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "not"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a strong-negation logic:Formula to its single negated sub-formula. This is explicit (classical) negation and is kept distinct from negation-as-failure, which is a body-literal flag on a derivation rule (logic:negatedBody): the two are never conflated."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:antecedent
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:range logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "antecedent"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a material-implication logic:Formula to its antecedent (the hypothesis). Paired with logic:consequent; the two name the implication's operands explicitly so the ordered, non-commutative reading never depends on serialization order."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:consequent
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:range logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "consequent"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a material-implication logic:Formula to its consequent (the conclusion). Paired with logic:antecedent; their presence marks the node as an implication, distinct from the commutative logic:iff."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:iff
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:range logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "if and only if"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a biconditional logic:Formula to each of its two operand sub-formulae. The biconditional is commutative, so the canonical identity is insensitive to which operand is which — unlike the ordered logic:antecedent / logic:consequent of an implication."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:relation
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:range logic:Type ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "relation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates an atomic-predication logic:Formula to the relation it predicates, over its ordered logic:argument terms. The relation is reified as a logic:Type individual per the HiLog reflection (see logic:instanceOf and logic:orderedType): predicating over a reified relation individual keeps the object level first-order rather than admitting a predicate variable, so no separate relation or predicate class is minted."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:argument
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "argument"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates an atomic-predication logic:Formula to one of its argument term-carriers. Each carrier fixes its position with logic:termIndex and its value with exactly one term-value property (logic:termIri, logic:termVariable, logic:termLiteral, or logic:termSequenceMarker), so a variadic argument list — including sequence markers — round-trips with its order and term kinds intact."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:quantifiedVariable
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "quantified variable"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a quantifier logic:Formula to one of its bound-variable term-carriers. Each carrier fixes its position in the binder block with logic:termIndex and its name with logic:termVariable; block order is significant, because bound-variable renaming preserves meaning but reordering a quantifier prefix does not."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:termIri
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "term IRI"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Carries an IRI-constant term value on an argument term-carrier: the argument is an individual (or a reified relation or type) named by this IRI. One of the four mutually exclusive term-value properties; exactly one is present on each carrier."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:termIndex
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "term index"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The zero-based ordinal of a term-carrier within its ordered list — an argument within an atomic predication, or a bound variable within a quantifier block. Fixing position explicitly makes the variadic, order-significant lists round-trip independent of RDF statement order."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:termVariable
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "term variable"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Carries a variable term value (the authored variable name, without a sigil) on a term-carrier: a single-term variable, bound by an enclosing quantifier or free. One of the four mutually exclusive term-value properties."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:termLiteral
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range rdfs:Literal ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "term literal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Carries a data-literal term value (its lexical form) on an argument term-carrier; the term's datatype rides on the companion logic:termLiteralDatatype. One of the four mutually exclusive term-value properties."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:termLiteralDatatype
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:range rdfs:Datatype ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "term literal datatype"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Carries the datatype IRI of a literal term value on an argument term-carrier that also bears logic:termLiteral. Absent for a plain literal. Held separately from the literal so the typed-literal term round-trips losslessly regardless of how an intermediate reader handles literal datatypes."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:termSequenceMarker
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "term sequence marker"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Carries a sequence-marker term value (the authored marker name) on an argument term-carrier: the argument is a logic:SequenceMarker binding a sequence of terms rather than a single one. One of the four mutually exclusive term-value properties."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

# ── The full-FOL residue shape vocabulary (loss-ledger disclosure) ────────────
# The closed value set a Horn-fragment projection target discloses when it cannot
# carry a logic:Formula: each tag names which first-order construct exceeds the
# Horn+NAF fragment, so the loss ledger states the kind of residue carried-and-
# flagged in the canonical logic: layer rather than emitting an opaque note.

logic:FormulaShape
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Formula Shape"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The closed class of first-order shape tags a Horn-fragment projection target discloses when it cannot represent a logic:Formula. Each individual names one construct that pushes a formula beyond the binary Horn+NAF fragment, so the loss ledger records which constructs were carried-and-flagged in the canonical logic: layer instead of one opaque note. The set is closed — its individuals are logic:Disjunctive, logic:Nested, logic:Quantified, logic:StrongNegation, and logic:Variadic — so a misspelt tag names no declared value."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:Disjunctive
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormulaShape ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Disjunctive"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The residue shape tag for a formula in which a disjunction (logic:or) appears — a choice the single determinate body of a Horn rule cannot express. Disclosed when a Horn-fragment target carries such a formula as flagged unsupported residue."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Nested
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormulaShape ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Nested"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The residue shape tag for a formula that is a connective or quantifier tree rather than a flat predication — it carries logical structure (logic:and, logic:or, logic:not, an implication, logic:iff, or a quantifier) that the flat body of a Horn rule cannot hold. Disclosed when a Horn-fragment target carries such a formula as flagged unsupported residue."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Quantified
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormulaShape ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Quantified"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The residue shape tag for a formula in which an explicit quantifier (logic:forall or logic:exists) appears — quantification nested or alternating beyond the implicit universal closure of a Horn rule. Disclosed when a Horn-fragment target carries such a formula as flagged unsupported residue."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:StrongNegation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormulaShape ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Strong Negation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The residue shape tag for a formula in which strong (explicit, classical) negation (logic:not) appears — distinct from negation-as-failure, which a Horn rule body already carries. Disclosed when a Horn-fragment target carries such a formula as flagged unsupported residue."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:Variadic
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormulaShape ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Variadic"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The residue shape tag for an atomic predication whose argument arity is not the binary Horn shape: it carries a logic:SequenceMarker or a non-binary (unary or n-ary) argument list — the generalization beyond the fixed arity-three triple. Disclosed when a Horn-fragment target carries such a formula as flagged unsupported residue."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:formalizes
    a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "formalizes"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A bridge annotation from a logic: foundational term to the gmeow: domain concept it formalizes: the central reasoning vocabulary (argumentation semantics, Belnap information states) names the domain construct that mirrors it, so the domain term's documentation can surface the formalization without the domain slice ever asserting a logic: triple. Subject is a logic: term, object a gmeow: term, both stated in prose; an annotation property, never a reasoned axiom, so it carries no DL or EL profile weight."@x-gmeow-english .
vann:preferredNamespacePrefix
    a owl:AnnotationProperty .

vann:preferredNamespaceUri
    a owl:AnnotationProperty .
